{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate","id":1211683,"title":"Speculating on the content of \"Lunars: Fangs at the Gate\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-25T21:01:57-07:00","id":1211683,"title":"Speculating on the content of \"Lunars: Fangs at the Gate\"","content":"If we follow the pattern of What Fire Has Wrought...<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter One: The Lunars</b> will touch on the history of Luna's Beloved, how they experience Exaltation and Luna's visitation, and the bestial nature of their Essence. There might be a rough census about how many of the 400 Lunar Exalted can be found in any of Creation's five directions.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Two: The Silver Pact </b>will talk about the loose bonds of obligation and favors that bind the Lunar Exalted. This starts with finding new Lunars and whisking them away to the safety of the wilds for education and Tattoos, which discharges the debt the older Lunars owe to the Pact for receiving the same service when they first Exalted, while putting that same debt upon the new Lunars to be paid forward in kind later. The Pact will be laid out as a network of information exchange, mutual self-defense, and favor-trading. More detail will be given about how a young Lunar can seek apprenticeship to an elder, asking boons and taking on quests in payment, and how elders might approach juniors for singular favors in return for great boons.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Three: Luminaries</b> will introduce the major political figures and factions within the Pact and outside of it. This and the previous chapter will be reversed in order from their equivalents in What Fire Has Wrought, but I think -- if only in this case -- this progression makes more sense.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Four: Dominions </b>will cover the kingdoms created and shaped by those major figures discussed in Chapter Three.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then chapters for character creation, traits, Lunar Charms, Martial Arts and Sorcery, and some Quick Stats for notable figures.<br /> <br /> They might get a Chapter for artifacts, or it might be given entirely over to mundane animals, to provide a greater variety of Heart's Blood than the Corebook offers.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps the animals might share space with the notable figures in a larger Chapter 10, since it's already a place of Quick Stats? That would make a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm certainly not expecting as many as eight Martial Arts Styles, and might be surprised to see as many as three. One might be Celestial Monkey Style. Any others would have to be totally new, since White Reaper and Silver-Voiced Nightingale were in the Core, Terrible Ascent-Driven Beast Style doesn't do anything special, and everything else is either elemental, Abyssal, or to some extent Sidereal.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I would be unsurprised to see at least two or three new Sorcerous Initiations, at least a few Terrestrial Circle spells, and a dozen Celestial Circle spells.<br /> <br /> Getting as many artifacts as the Heirlooms would be cool (especially since Vance said Lunars can craft better than Dragon-Blooded, and so should have a Five-Dot or two), but like Martial Arts, the word count will probably be curtailed to make room in Chapter 10 for a lot of animals.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not expecting a return of the damned Litany or whatever those waste-of-space &quot;rules&quot; were called.<br /> <br /> Likewise, &quot;Renown&quot; isn't likely to return, and good riddance. The Influence Merit seems to more than suffice.<br /> <br /> <br /> I want to see lots of canonical Lunar &quot;Half-Castes&quot;; the Moon-Touched. Previous editions have always given Lunar rulers beastmen followers, but have rather shied away from those who also (or only) inherited the less-physical, more-magical gifts of the Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> I also want to see God-Blooded princes and princesses, born of romantic or political unions with mighty spirits; Elementals, terrestrial gods, stray Celestial gods, demons, Fair Folk, <i>anything</i>.<br /> <br /> These magical children would never stand a chance against Dragon-Blooded, but they would more useful agents than mere mortals.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also want to see a lot more sorcerous workings used on peoples, territories, edifices, and tools passed down among mortals, as Lunar Exalted make use of Terrestrial and Celestial sorcery to bolster the power of their holdings and followers, with none of the Realm\u2019s distrust of the art.<br /> <br /> Full Moon kings who never become sorcerers can trade favors across the Silver Pact to acquire the services of Celestial sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Halta is cute, with people living in trees with talking animals, but that really seems to be only scratching the surface of the kind of fantasy societies and enchanted environments that Lunars could create which are inimical and resistant to invasion or assimilation by the Realm, Lookshy, or Prasad.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have ensorcelled the land to produce bountiful crops, but even if you take it from my people, good luck maintaining the blessing without performing the spiritual rites which would blaspheme your phony religion!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, you turned my transformed people against me? Will you still enjoy their loyalty after following the rites of the Immaculate faith robs them of the strength I gave them within a generation?\u201d<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-26-2018, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T21:11:19-07:00","id":1211684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210795-this-thread-is-amazing?p=1211672#post1211672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that Rain Deathflyer comes of as the young junior partner backing Halta emphasizes the problem of First Age survivors being the default for Elder Lunars.<br /> <br /> Ideally the norm for Elder Lunars should be centuries old but Exalted post-contagion. Meeting a Shogunate survivor should be a big deal - and First Age survivors should be whispered legends.</div> </div> </div> </div>If &quot;Fangs at the Gate&quot; give the Shogunate-era Lunar elders the kind of focus the First Age survivors got in the last two Editions, and gives the First Age elders basically no attention at all...<br /> <br /> Well, that might be just spiffy.<br /> <br /> Do we REALLY need to hear about how little Ma Ha Suchi, Leviathan, and Lillith are and have been doing, again? We get it already; they're depressed and sulking and want you damn kids off of their lawn.<br /> <br /> Tammuz and Magnificent Jaguar also don't need to return unless they've actually been accomplishing anything.<br /> <br /> Rain Deathflier is supposed to be Shogunate-era, so if he's supposed to have anything to do with Halta, it had better be greatly changed for the stronger and weirder. Especially if he's still lovers with a First Age elder. What the hell has Silver Python ever done?<br /> <br /> Raksi is the most active and productive of all of them, which isn't particularly encouraging since she's Raksi. She's at least more respectable than before, but how high a bar was that to clear?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T22:30:23-07:00","id":1211694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211684#post1211684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If &quot;Fangs at the Gate&quot; give the Shogunate-era Lunar elders the kind of focus the First Age survivors got in the last two Editions, and gives the First Age elders basically no attention at all...<br /> <br /> Well, that might be just spiffy.<br /> <br /> Do we REALLY need to hear about how little Ma Ha Suchi, Leviathan, and Lillith are and have been doing, again? We get it already; they're depressed and sulking and want you damn kids off of their lawn.<br /> <br /> Tammuz and Magnificent Jaguar also don't need to return unless they've actually been accomplishing anything.<br /> <br /> Rain Deathflier is supposed to be Shogunate-era, so if he's supposed to have anything to do with Halta, it had better be greatly changed for the stronger and weirder. Especially if he's still lovers with a First Age elder. What the hell has Silver Python ever done?<br /> <br /> Raksi is the most active and productive of all of them, which isn't particularly encouraging since she's Raksi. She's at least more respectable than before, but how high a bar was that to clear?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who is to say they wouldn't tune them up like they did Mnemon and add new facets to their character that makes them more interesting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T22:41:55-07:00","id":1211696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate#post1211683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting as many artifacts as the Heirlooms would be cool (especially since Vance said Lunars can craft better than Dragon-Blooded, and so should have a Five-Dot or two)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohh would you look at that fumes<br /> ... ohh, also I hope they put in plenty of beasties, particularly the more <i>extreme </i>ones, insects, tyrant lizards, that kind of thing<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23635,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","user":"Lion Hamster","date":". 04-26-2018, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T00:10:48-07:00","id":1211706,"title":"","content":"Tyrant lizards are already in the Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T00:18:36-07:00","id":1211709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211694#post1211694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is to say they wouldn't tune them up like they did Mnemon and add new facets to their character that makes them more interesting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance's said previously he's felt many of the Lunar elders deserve better, citing Lilith, Raksi and Ma-Ha-Suchi.<br /> <br /> He's also said they may introduce new Lunar elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T02:17:11-07:00","id":1211721,"title":"","content":"I think that's very likely to happen! There's also some things where it doesn't actually require too much adding. Half of the stuff that could make Raksi interesting in third edition is already there in the first edition. Lilith's whole concept is there basically. Ma-Ha-Suchi is an odd one where I'm not sure how to &quot;overhaul him&quot; or if you need to, since the corebook already gives a decent sense of his deal. Hearing about it from the perspective of his would-be Lunar charges or allies would be awesome though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T05:33:25-07:00","id":1211753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211706#post1211706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tyrant lizards are already in the Core.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Kind of thing&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T05:41:44-07:00","id":1211756,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing they will not dedicate that much wordcount to the silver pact.<br /> There's this thing about media: it doesn't do much to change opinions, but it sets the narrative. If the silver pact is written about far more than its alternatives (like regional zeitgeists about lunars), it will be the primary, almost only, setting presumption about lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> So my guess is that the silver pact won't have more than half a chapter for itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T06:06:47-07:00","id":1211760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211756#post1211756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing they will not dedicate that much wordcount to the silver pact.<br /> There's this thing about media: it doesn't do much to change opinions, but it sets the narrative. If the silver pact is written about far more than its alternatives (like regional zeitgeists about lunars), it will be the primary, almost only, setting presumption about lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> So my guess is that the silver pact won't have more than half a chapter for itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are far more options for Dragon-Blooded than the Realm now, but there was still an entire chapter dedicated to the Great Houses and an entire other chapter dedicated to Dynastic life within the Realm.<br /> <br /> Places like Fajad, Prasad, and even Lookshy have get that kind of detail in an entirely separate book, and otherwise only get mentioned in a separate, non-Great Houses, non-Dynastic childhood chapter. And the separate book will actually go into more detail about the Dynasty, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T07:04:55-07:00","id":1211778,"title":"","content":"I think the last time I checked with Robert Vance, he might have said that Celestial Monkey Style wouldn\u2019t be in the Lunar book.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m hesitant to take that seriously, because of Sun Wukong the shapeshifting Stone Monkey King, Sage Surpassing Heaven. Not exactly a Sidereal figure, that one.<br /> <br /> <br /> We\u2019ve already gotten the other four classic Chinese animal Styles: Snake, Tiger, Crane, and now Mantis.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure there\u2019s a Chinese Dragon Style as well, and we just got five whole Dragon Styles.<br /> <br /> The corebook already gave us White Reaper and Silver-Voiced Nightingale Styles. <br /> <br /> We\u2019ve already gotten all of the previous sneaky ninja assassin Styles: Ebon Shadow, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan, Black Claw, and White Veil. <br /> <br /> There\u2019s Crystal Chameleon Style, I suppose, but I would expect to see that in the Sidereals book rather than Celestial Monkey. Lunars who want to be stealthy in combat can temporarily assume small forms, and turn into cheetahs and birds when they want to be fast.<br /> <br /> The Four Arguments of Virtue Styles were made for gods by other gods or Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Hungry Ghost is primarily Abyssal.<br /> <br /> Laughing Wounds Style isn\u2019t likely to return, based on developer comments. Even if it did: Abyssal. <br /> <br /> Crimson Pentacle, Even Blade, Fivefold Shadow Hand, Seafaring Hero, Ill Lily, Jade Mountain, and Night Breeze Styles are all \u201cI can\u2019t believe I\u2019m not Dragon-Blooded!\u201d Styles.<br /> <br /> Golden Exhalation Style... we already have Righteous Devil Style which now has a built-in Terrestrial level, and we have native Dragon-Blooded firewand Charms.<br /> <br /> Falling Blossom Style is \u201cI am an expendable NPC\u201d Style, and Quick Character stat blocks don\u2019t need a fully-written Martial Arts Style Charm tree.<br /> <br /> Path of the Arbiter is \u201cI am a mortal pretending to be a Solar!\u201d Style, but mortals can\u2019t learn Charms anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, I\u2019ve narrowed the options of possible returning Styles which are not Monkey to three, and I\u2019ll address them in another post.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-26-2018, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T07:09:12-07:00","id":1211781,"title":"","content":"Idiot question; is Fangs at the Gate a confirmed subtitle? And if so, wherefrom?<br /> <br /> (I thought I'd been keeping up, but...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T07:28:11-07:00","id":1211791,"title":"","content":"Who says any of the styles in the Lunars book have to be an update to an old one? <br /> <br /> Also, Celestial Monkey wasn't all that memorable or interesting, at least not to me. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Really, only three things stuck with me: <br /> <br /> -One, how nonsensical it felt for your ability to practice the style to <i>implode</i> if you ever raised your Virtue dots too high.<br /> <br /> -Two, hitting people in places corresponding to their Virtue dots, it really felt like someone was tripping over themself to get a dick joke printed.<br /> <br /> -Three, the capstone permitting me to treat whatever weapons and armor I wanted as acceptable for the style felt like it was dragging the idea of &quot;having any real feel to it&quot; out back and putting a round in its head.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'd much rather see a new style in its place, such as Scorpion, Falcon, Bull, Spider, or Wolf Style. <i>If</i> we have to bring Monkey back, it needs to be overhauled pretty drastically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T07:28:37-07:00","id":1211792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211781#post1211781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idiot question; is Fangs at the Gate a confirmed subtitle? And if so, wherefrom?<br /> <br /> (I thought I'd been keeping up, but...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I can confirm that the full name of the book is <b>Lunars: Fangs at the Gate</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T07:31:07-07:00","id":1211793,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be surprised if it's just Moneky, not Celestial monkey. Kind of like how &quot;Silver-Voiced&quot; is kinda an add-on to what is ultimately just Nightingale Style.<br /> <br /> Centipede wouldn't be bad to see back. And if we soemday see Scorpion, Lizard and Toad, we can have the Five Deadly Venoms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T07:47:11-07:00","id":1211798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211781#post1211781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idiot question; is Fangs at the Gate a confirmed subtitle? And if so, wherefrom?<br /> <br /> (I thought I'd been keeping up, but...)</div> </div> </div> </div>We initially got it from Dixie Cochran, who revealed it with permission from Eric in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/what-kind-of-vault-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">this week's Monday Meeting comments</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:54:07-07:00","id":1211828,"title":"","content":"I actually think that the lunars book would be a great place for extra mutations (as merits), along with what mutations in the core actually count as such for the purposes of things like Saga Beat Virtue. This would be especially true if they go the route of using merits/mutations to enhance shapeshifting forms or chimerism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:56:45-07:00","id":1211831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211791#post1211791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says any of the styles in the Lunars book have to be an update to an old one?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know. Who did say such a thing? <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Celestial Monkey wasn't all that memorable or interesting, at least not to me. </div> </div> </div>Monkey Tail Distraction Strike, Flowing Mirror of Opposition Technique, and Walking in the Footsteps of Ten Thousand Things. As well as fighting with a staff like Sun Wukong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -One, how nonsensical it felt for your ability to practice the style to <i>implode</i> if you ever raised your Virtue dots too high. </div> </div> </div>Assuming the the Style had anything to do with Intimacies, I could see the Form Charm temporarily demoting all Major and Defining Intimacies to Minor as the martial artist temporarily gains or strengthens by one step a Principle of \u201cDon\u2019t take anything seriously\u201d, with extra effects if the stylist already has that as a Defining Principle. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Two, hitting people in places corresponding to their Virtue dots, it really felt like someone was tripping over themself to get a dick joke printed. </div> </div> </div>Nailing your opponent somewhere sensitive, whether groin, stomach, head, or heart, is still a viable attack. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Three, the capstone permitting me to treat whatever weapons and armor I wanted as acceptable for the style felt like it was dragging the idea of &quot;having any real feel to it&quot; out back and putting a round in its head. </div> </div> </div>Totally agreed. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>If</i> we have to bring Monkey back, it needs to be overhauled pretty drastically. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> The Style was never well-designed. But the same can be said for the Lunar Exalted. If something grand can be made of the Lunar Exalted at last, why not this Style?<br /> <br /> Give the Monkey King his due. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd much rather see a new style in its place, such as Scorpion, Falcon, Bull, Spider, or Wolf Style. </div> </div> </div>There is a bit more to be said about the old before I am ready to speculate about something new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T09:00:30-07:00","id":1211836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211828#post1211828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think that the lunars book would be a great place for extra mutations (as merits), along with what mutations in the core actually count as such for the purposes of things like Saga Beat Virtue. This would be especially true if they go the route of using merits/mutations to enhance shapeshifting forms or chimerism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am expecting plenty of new Supernatural Merits, especially for the sake of building Hybrid Forms and various flavors of Beastfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T10:18:22-07:00","id":1211872,"title":"","content":"Terrible Ascent-Driven Beast Style allowed no weapons. It allowed any weight-class of armor, which is odd because it was all about jumping down from and into great heights and across great distances to attack and retreat, even while clinching an enemy.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s nothing that can\u2019t be done as well or better with Lunar Attribute Charms. The advantage would be buying these Charms with Lunar XP instead of general XP, especially for Lunars who don\u2019t favor Strength and/or Dexterity. <br /> <br /> It couldn\u2019t be used in animal forms, which are what Lunars would normally rely upon to make up for physical shortcomings. <br /> <br /> For Lunars, it is \u201cI can\u2019t believe I\u2019m not in animal form; no seriously, am I an idiot, why am I not in animal form?\u201d Style.<br /> <br /> For anyone else, there are better choices. Crane Style, for one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T12:30:14-07:00","id":1211934,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d hope Martial Arts in the Lunar book would be a ton of new animal Styles as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T12:50:08-07:00","id":1211943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211934#post1211934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d hope Martial Arts in the Lunar book would be a ton of new animal Styles as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the major draw of Lunars is turning into animals rather than pretending to be them.<br /> <br /> Between that and the number of animal Styles and Styles in general already available to players, the only reason I\u2019m expecting even one Style in the book is because there hasn\u2019t been an Exalted fatsplat book lacking one since... the very first Lunar book.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is arguably more important to Lunars than Martial Arts; their powerful and enthusiastic use of sorcery is tied up in how and why they have the image and reputation and themes of witchcraft.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-26-2018, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T13:33:20-07:00","id":1211956,"title":"","content":"There aren\u2019t that many animal styles. They should make up the majority of styles but currently number about a quarter of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:04:33-07:00","id":1211970,"title":"","content":"Hmm, not sure what to speculate upon if the chapter structure has been suggested...<br /> <br /> \u200bActually, I think the suggestions in the first post have some redundancies. I don't think a chapter on the Silver Pact <i>and</i> on famous figures <i>and</i> character write-ups is necessary, because at least two of those are overlapping. I don't think individual Lunars really have the scope of Great Houses to warrant a chapter just to them that isn't the chapter for quick characters.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think instead, there might be a chapter on the Silver Pact, and then a chapter (perhaps not a very long one) to give insight into the experience of Lunars that opt out of the Pact and go do their own thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211696#post1211696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ohh would you look at that fumes</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, what else do you expect to see when you're looking at the pot.<br /> <br /> Or is it the kettle?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:23:37-07:00","id":1211983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211956#post1211956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There aren\u2019t that many animal styles. They should make up the majority of styles but currently number about a quarter of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m all for it if \u201cShark Style\u201d is about fighting underwater and \u201cEagle Style\u201d is about fighting with a set of wings which allow you to fly.<br /> <br /> But \u201cRhinocerous/Ox-Dragon\u201d Style of fighting with a lance, shield, heavy armor and sometimes a horse would have been more appropriate for the Dragon-Blooded book than the Lunar one.<br /> <br /> Last I heard about Turtle Style, it might involve the use of a bo staff rather than Captain America\u2019s mighty shield-work. I called my attempt at a shield-centric Style \u201cPlated Dragon\u201d.<br /> <br /> I made a very enthusiast attempt at a Spider Style with garottes, bolas, nets, lassos...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-26-2018, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:32:40-07:00","id":1211988,"title":"","content":"I don't exactly doubt the explanation connecting Mantis Style to the Dragon Blooded, but I still feel as though it would be a bit post hoc. That might actually go for the others that aren't Immaculate Dragon as well.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich is my way of saying that to my eyes, it's better to use each hardback as an opportunity to get a few more Martial Arts out there, even if the basis of a given one being in a given book is a bit shaky, because to my mind it's better to get a constant drip of several and varied Martial Arts then getting one or two at a time up until a dedicated book filled with them comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T15:50:57-07:00","id":1212027,"title":"","content":"My first 3E Lunar character is going to be a Snakeman who becomes the boogeyman of his people, with a mongoose spirit shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:10:56-07:00","id":1212029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211988#post1211988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't exactly doubt the explanation connecting Mantis Style to the Dragon Blooded, but I still feel as though it would be a bit post hoc. That might actually go for the others that aren't Immaculate Dragon as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mantis Style is for monks and law enforcers (like magistrates) who want to capture and subdue people alive and mostly unharmed so that they can be tried in a court of law, re-educated, and reformed. It\u2019s an excellent fit for the kinder heroes of the various Dragon-Blooded empires.<br /> <br /> Golden Janissary Style is for Dragon-Blooded exorcists; both those who don\u2019t belong to the Immaculate Order, and those who decide that the Dragon Styles aren\u2019t anti-demon/undead enough for their needs. It\u2019s a fine fit.<br /> <br /> White Veil Style is a perfect fit for courtly intrigues. Lunar Exalted would make as much use of it as Dragon-Blooded, but you would want to use this book to help you play a Lunar assassin infiltrating a Dragon-Blooded stronghold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is my way of saying that to my eyes, it's better to use each hardback as an opportunity to get a few more Martial Arts out there, even if the basis of a given one being in a given book is a bit shaky, because to my mind it's better to get a constant drip of several and varied Martial Arts then getting one or two at a time up until a dedicated book filled with them comes out. </div> </div> </div>But it\u2019s better if the Lunars get more of what they can most uniquely benefit from and offer to players (shapeshifting into animals) than something on which they don\u2019t heavily depend.<br /> <br /> What Fire Has Wrought didn\u2019t need to detail a single beast (and did so for exactly one beast), but Fangs at the Gate needs to provide a LOT of spirit shapes for Lunar totem animals.<br /> <br /> Also, it would be best if any new Martial Arts Styles are particularly evocative of the \u201csavage, barbarian epic\u201d that Lunars are meant to deliver.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts employing the axe (throwing hatchet) and hammer would be nice. As would any involving two-handed great swords.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, we\u2019d have to wait until Abyssals for Black Swordsman Style.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-26-2018, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:16:48-07:00","id":1212031,"title":"","content":"Seeing as Lunars are 1) Attribute based, 2) Can never favor MA or MA charms, and 3) have no thematic ties to MA in general, or as a whole, I highly doubt we will see any MA's in the Lunar Book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:19:23-07:00","id":1212032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212029#post1212029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mantis Style is for monks and law enforcers (like magistrates) who want to capture and subdue people alive and mostly unharmed so that they can be tried in a court of law, re-educated, and reformed. It\u2019s an excellent fit for the kinder heroes of the various Dragon-Blooded empires.<br /> <br /> Golden Janissary Style is for Dragon-Blooded exorcists; both those who don\u2019t belong to the Immaculate Order, and those who decide that the Dragon Styles aren\u2019t anti-demon/undead enough for their needs. It\u2019s a fine fit.<br /> <br /> White Veil Style is a perfect fit for courtly intrigues. Lunar Exalted would make as much use of it as Dragon-Blooded, but you would want to use this book to help you play a Lunar assassin infiltrating a Dragon-Blooded stronghold.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bLike I said, they're all perfectly plausible explanations. I do not doubt them. I do not dispute them. I still think they're primarily there to anchor those Styles to this particular book, when they could be added just about anywhere<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it\u2019s better if the Lunars get more of what they can mostly uniquely benefit from and offer to players (shapeshifting into animals) than something on which they don\u2019t heavily depend.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't really disagree with that. After all, word count is limited, and if it comes down to the wire, it would probably be better for the book to stay on topic than to more-or-less add in a few Styles for their own sake.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it would be best if any new Martial Arts Styles are particularly evocative of the \u201csavage, barbarian epic\u201d that Lunars are meant to deliver.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat sounds like an effective and flexible throughline.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:20:25-07:00","id":1212033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212031#post1212031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as Lunars are 1) Attribute based, 2) Can never favor MA or MA charms, and 3) have no thematic ties to MA in general, or as a whole, I highly doubt we will see any MA's in the Lunar Book.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThey do have the (provisional) benefit of being able to combine their own combat Charms freely with Martial Arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:26:18-07:00","id":1212034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212033#post1212033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThey do have the (provisional) benefit of being able to combine their own combat Charms freely with Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's hardly a compelling argument to include them... Look I'm not going to be upset if they do include a few MA's in the Lunar book. I'm not against the idea. I just will not be the least bit surprised if when the KS goes live, there's no MA chapter. There's way too much stuff that needs to be in the book already without adding in a chapter that does not resonate with Lunars the way it does with Solars, and DB's.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:30:24-07:00","id":1212035,"title":"","content":"<i>Lunars</i> will have a &quot;Martial Arts and Sorcery&quot; chapter, in much the same manner as the core book and <i>Dragon-Blooded.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:33:25-07:00","id":1212038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212031#post1212031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as Lunars are 1) Attribute based, 2) Can never favor MA or MA charms, and 3) have no thematic ties to MA in general, or as a whole, I highly doubt we will see any MA's in the Lunar Book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas they can favor sorcery and spells, learn the mightiest sorcery short of Solar Circle, and have heavy thematic ties to sorcery as well as plenty of setting justification and encouragement for using it liberally.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I was sure there would be at least one MA, and maybe as many as three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-26-2018, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:33:30-07:00","id":1212039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212035#post1212035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Lunars</i> will have a &quot;Martial Arts and Sorcery&quot; chapter, in much the same manner as the core book and <i>Dragon-Blooded.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:36:07-07:00","id":1212041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212038#post1212038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whereas they can favor sorcery and spells, learn the mightiest sorcery short of Solar Circle, and have heavy thematic ties to sorcery as well as plenty of setting justification and encouragement for using it liberally.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, more Supernatural Merits, dozens of animals, etc. At least that was my thought process, but Word of Dev says MA is a go, so MA it is, I guess...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:39:19-07:00","id":1212043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212035#post1212035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Lunars</i> will have a &amp;quot;Martial Arts and Sorcery&amp;quot; chapter, in much the same manner as the core book and <i>Dragon-Blooded.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Will they have an Artifacts Chapter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:47:03-07:00","id":1212048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212043#post1212043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will they have an Artifacts Chapter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">10char</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:51:28-07:00","id":1212053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212041#post1212041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, more Supernatural Merits, dozens of animals, etc. At least that was my thought process, but Word of Dev says MA is a go, so MA it is, I guess...</div> </div> </div> </div>The book will have all of those things, too. I did not say otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T17:03:18-07:00","id":1212064,"title":"","content":"Lunar artifacts, is a thought that makes me happy. I hope the first draft is finished quickly, competently, and with style. I've waited so long for it.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm definitely a &quot;team Lunar&quot; guy despite the fact that being a &quot;team anything&quot; guy makes absolutely no sense whatsoever. I can dislike my counter logical desire to see Lunars be conspicuously awesome compared to other exalts, but I can't deny it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T20:48:03-07:00","id":1212132,"title":"","content":"Anyway, of the three Styles I said I'd narrowed it down to, I dissected and dismissed Terrible Ascent-Driven Beast Style above, and had the fundamental problem of First Pulse Style pointed out to me <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1211797-first-pulse-style-lunar-or-infernal-book\">in another thread</a>.<br /> <br /> The last one was Orgiastic Fugitive Style. I clearly recall Robert Vance saying he wasn't happy with this one; it didn't properly capture the nature of Drunken Boxing.<br /> <br /> Drunken Kung Fu Master seems like more of a Sidereal thing. Lunars have something of the oni about them, and the oni's love of alcohol is legendary, but not so much fighting effectively in a drunken stupor.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, that's about <i>it</i> for the old styles. It really does seem like the writers would have to create whole new Martial Arts Styles for the Lunar book, especially if Celestial Monkey is excluded.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, there was one I'd forgotten. <i>Lightning Hoof Style.</i><br /> <br /> If Lunars are barbarians, then Lunars can be Mongols, and the Mongol ticket to victory was mounted archery. Though the Marukan nation would no longer be able to practice this Style at all.<br /> <br /> Still, within a Pack of Lunar Exalted, you might have one that prefers to fight in the forms of beasts large enough to ride, and one who prefers to fight from the saddle. A Style for fighting from the back of any mounted creature might therefore be extremely appropriate for <i>Fangs at the Gate</i>.<br /> <br /> Lunar children who inherited enough of Luna's glory might even be able to learn these Charms for themselves, to strike their mother's enemies from astride her shoulders, like San the mononoke princess and her wolf-mother Moro.<br /> <br /> <br /> Other than that, Styles for axes, hammers, and two-handed swords. Fantasy barbarians are all about wielding frighteningly huge kill-sticks.<br /> <br /> But I definitely wouldn't turn up my nose at a Spider Style based around restraining with projectiles like bolas, nets, and lassos. That's also good hunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T21:16:32-07:00","id":1212136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212041#post1212041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, more Supernatural Merits, dozens of animals, etc. At least that was my thought process, but Word of Dev says MA is a go, so MA it is, I guess...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why would you read those as specifically in competition for space? I get that wordcount is finite so there is always a trade off including anything, but why do you see those topics specifically as being in competition with Martial Arts specifically?<br /> <br /> Except for with the Immaculate styles (since they don't have Auras), Lunars make more powerful martial artists than Dragon-Blooded do, since they are uninhibited by the Terrestrial keyword, and (last we heard) they can stack Dex Charms with Martial Arts Charms (though Vance said that may be subject to change in playtesting). Martial Arts is at least as valuable a subject to explore with them as it is with Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T21:35:11-07:00","id":1212140,"title":"","content":"My picks...<br /> <br /> Leopard Style - recapturing some of the more interesting elements of Terrible Ascent Driven Beast<br /> <br /> Monkey Style - agile, multidexterous, and deceptive - capture some of the better functioning elements of Celestial Monkey<br /> <br /> Falcon Style - swooping and spear based (doesn't require, but synchronizes very well with flight forms/charms)<br /> <br /> Spider Style - uses nets, but can also synchronize well if the Lunar has a web weaving form","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T05:26:38-07:00","id":1212230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212140#post1212140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My picks...<br /> <br /> Leopard Style - recapturing some of the more interesting elements of Terrible Ascent Driven Beast<br /> <br /> Monkey Style - agile, multidexterous, and deceptive - capture some of the better functioning elements of Celestial Monkey<br /> <br /> Falcon Style - swooping and spear based (doesn't require, but synchronizes very well with flight forms/charms)<br /> <br /> Spider Style - uses nets, but can also synchronize well if the Lunar has a web weaving form</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! These are exactly the MA styles I would love to see in the Lunar book!<br /> <br /> I think Eric or Vance also stated that this could be the right place to put Stone Lion.<br /> <br /> But I really hope they consider Leopard, Falcon, and Monkey too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T05:41:32-07:00","id":1212236,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a fighting-the-Wyld-focused MA. After all, the Wyld is as much an enemy to lunars living on the fringe of Creation as The Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T05:50:41-07:00","id":1212240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212230#post1212230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Eric or Vance also stated that this could be the right place to put Stone Lion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Style for emulating the Celestial Lions of Heaven and the Teodoza (so?) of Hell?<br /> <br /> Possibly also a Godzilla era kaiju named King Ceasar? The komainu / shisa / lion-dog?<br /> <br /> What was the focus of that Style, again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:15:31-07:00","id":1212261,"title":"","content":"I would really like a revamped Orgiastic Fugitive Style, don't care in which book, but a drunken master is so far a very obvious yet painfully unsupported concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:38:22-07:00","id":1212270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212240#post1212240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Style for emulating the Celestial Lions of Heaven and the Teodoza (so?) of Hell?<br /> <br /> Possibly also a Godzilla era kaiju named King Ceasar? The komainu / shisa / lion-dog?<br /> <br /> What was the focus of that Style, again?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> God, I cannot find the quote so help me. I think it was defend other/bodyguard focused?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:42:39-07:00","id":1212301,"title":"","content":"Vance has said that Orgiastic Fugitive Style is looking to be split into two MAs this edition. Seven Drunken Gods Style and Devil Pipe Style. <br /> <br /> We've also heard him talk about a Heavenly Executioner Style when asked about a Great Sword using martial art.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I'm in the boat that as a game with major Wuxia influences everyone should have Martial Arts appearing in their books. They cam interact with the overarching narrative of schools and competing philosophies via honorable combat and the tales of murder/betrayal/mentorship that can entail. Lunars don't favor it, but they can combine native charms with them and don't suffer the Terrestrial Keyword. That's a MAJOR boost in power to their use. To the point that everyone playtesting and the like will be going over them thoroughly to make sure it doesn't break the game. They likely won't get as many as the corebook, or even the Dragon-blooded book. But if at least 5 don't appear it'd look a bit weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:50:07-07:00","id":1212306,"title":"","content":"Over the course of the line, I want nothing more than Centipede, Toad, Lizard and Spider styles to show up. Need not be in one book, might not be sustainable as a trend of styles, but it'd be something I wouldn't mind seeing.<br /> <br /> At least Centipede though, as that was a cool and rarerly seen one in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:52:23-07:00","id":1212307,"title":"","content":"Holy crap! I need Devil Pipe Style! NOW!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T09:47:06-07:00","id":1212334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212270#post1212270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God, I cannot find the quote so help me. I think it was defend other/bodyguard focused?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cFangs at the Gate\u201d is a failure if it doesn\u2019t allow you to play as Gamera, Mothra, King Ceasar or any other \u201cguardian beast-god\u201d... but I am skeptical of how useful a Stone Lion Style would be for that concept, since you can\u2019t use Martial Arts in animal forms.<br /> <br /> What weapons would it even use? Tiger Claws or nothing, most likely. <br /> <br /> Lunar Attribute Charms for Defend Other could be used with any weapon. <br /> <br /> A more useful bodyguard Style is one that employs at least a shield.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:02:30-07:00","id":1212341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212301#post1212301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance has said that Orgiastic Fugitive Style is looking to be split into two MAs this edition. Seven Drunken Gods Style and Devil Pipe Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s exciting. I agree with tgueros, I\u2019d like to see Devil Pipe Style in \u201cFangs at the Gate\u201d. Seven Drunken Gods sounds like another Sidereal-esque Style, but who knows. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We've also heard him talk about a Heavenly Executioner Style when asked about a Great Sword using martial art. </div> </div> </div>Wouldn\u2019t that just be Violet Bier of Sorrows Style? Saturdan is the goddess of executioners. Sidereals have Single Point for katanas, so why not give VBoS some actual grounding by narrowing the kind of sword it uses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T14:02:10-07:00","id":1212413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212341#post1212341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s exciting. I agree with tgueros, I\u2019d like to see Devil Pipe Style in \u201cFangs at the Gate\u201d. Seven Drunken Gods sounds like another Sidereal-esque Style, but who knows</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean a style that thematically fits the Sidereal book, not one that would be a Sidereal Style, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T14:06:10-07:00","id":1212414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212413#post1212413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean a style that thematically fits the Sidereal book, not one that would be a Sidereal Style, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201c-esque\u201d means \u201clike\u201d. Sidereal-like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T14:27:58-07:00","id":1212424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212414#post1212414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u201c-esque\u201d means \u201clike\u201d. Sidereal-like.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the impression I took, just making sure it was the intent. Yeah, a drunken master style along with Violet Bier and Thrown Shadow and 5 Sidereal Styles would be cool for their book","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T14:53:54-07:00","id":1212440,"title":"","content":"Anyway, what about Moon-Touched and God-Blooded children?<br /> <br /> They would all be weaker than Terrestrials, and rarer because the power they pass down to their children becomes drastically watered-down. Nevertheless, they should exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:03:39-07:00","id":1212451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212440#post1212440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, what about Moon-Touched and God-Blooded children?<br /> <br /> They would all be weaker than Terrestrials, and rarer because the power they pass down to their children becomes drastically watered-down. Nevertheless, they should exist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If any Exalted have God-Blooded children by their nature, than yes, they should exist. I remain skeptical of that central premise though. I'd prefer it if Lunars had Charms to empower their descendants with certain effects, but they remain the continuing source of that power rather than being the child of an Exalted giving anyone inherent magic (other than Dragon-Blooded offspring having the potential to Exalt as Dragon-Blooded).<br /> <br /> But maybe if Exalt-Blooded were actually executed well this edition I could change my mind, but that remains my feeling from the last two editions attempts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T05:13:58-07:00","id":1212600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212451#post1212451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any Exalted have God-Blooded children by their nature, than yes, they should exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Celestial Exalted have been implied or stated to have this ability at higher Essence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd prefer it if Lunars had Charms to empower their descendants with certain effects, but they remain the continuing source of that power </div> </div> </div>As an approximation of the Solar Presence Charms which allow them to empower their chosen followers?<br /> <br /> I doubt the Lunars would entirely lack for choosing, and if Lunars had some way to ensure stronger children, why wouldn't Solars be able to do the same?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But maybe if Exalt-Blooded were actually executed well this edition I could change my mind, but that remains my feeling from the last two editions attempts. </div> </div> </div>Golden Children, Moon-Touched, and... Star Children? Star-Touched?... <br /> <br /> The developers said it wouldn't be as simple and powerful as giving them access to their parent's Charms. Rather, they would have smaller magical effects like those seen with spirits and magically-altered humans like Mist the Revolutionary. No different from God-Bloods, though with Spirit Charms being what they are in this edition, maybe a God-Blood might directly inherit a few of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T05:28:51-07:00","id":1212605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212341#post1212341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn\u2019t that just be Violet Bier of Sorrows Style? Saturdan is the goddess of executioners. Sidereals have Single Point for katanas, so why not give VBoS some actual grounding by narrowing the kind of sword it uses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I don't think Violet Bier's grounding problems stem from it's form weapon but rather from the fact that it's has charms themed on the other Maidens sitting at the start of the style like a grab bag. It's sort of a proto Hero Style from 1e where your Journeys who was going to learn Air Dragon would still eventually dip in and get Secrets of Future Strife + Blade of the Battle Maiden because they were too good to really say no to.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T06:15:18-07:00","id":1212623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212605#post1212605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I don't think Violet Bier's grounding problems stem from it's form weapon but rather from the fact that it's has charms themed on the other Maidens sitting at the start of the style like a grab bag. It's sort of a proto Hero Style from 1e where your Journeys who was going to learn Air Dragon would still eventually dip in and get Secrets of Future Strife + Blade of the Battle Maiden because they were too good to really say no to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The first four Charms are just... bad, for a Martial Arts Style. They don't really have anything to do with a self-contained Style, and everything to do with being Sidereal native Charms that were meant to make up for holes in their other Ability Charm trees.<br /> <br /> Maybe we'll be blessed with five Maiden Styles this time, with each of those four problematic Charms going to those and Violet Bier of Sorrows having a consistent and specific theme/strategy beyond &quot;Super Five Dragon Style, but for Sidereals.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> What does anyone think of the Lunar book having a new form of Lightning Hoof Style?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T07:51:33-07:00","id":1212658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212623#post1212623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does anyone think of the Lunar book having a new form of Lightning Hoof Style?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if it encourages a ridiculous centaur warform. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T08:52:34-07:00","id":1212683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212600#post1212600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Celestial Exalted have been implied or stated to have this ability at higher Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was being removed in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T08:59:25-07:00","id":1212687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212683#post1212683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that was being removed in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was explicitly stated that the children of Exalted would never be able to learn the Charms of their parents, but it was never suggested that the children of the Exalted couldn't inherit magical abilities of any kind.<br /> <br /> The Moon-Touched are referred twice in the corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T16:49:34-07:00","id":1213578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212683#post1212683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that was being removed in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m still holding out hope it will be. Any degree of celestial power, even if mechanically lesser than true Exalted Charms, passed along bloodlines undermines the setting\u2019s themes of what makes Celestial power different from Terrestrial.<br /> <br /> Yes I know it doesn\u2019t explicitly contradict what makes them different so long as it\u2019s not true Exaltation being passed on, but it can still thematically undermine the point without explicitly contradicting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T22:31:59-07:00","id":1213679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1213578#post1213578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any degree of celestial power, even if mechanically lesser than true Exalted Charms, passed along bloodlines undermines the setting\u2019s themes of what makes Celestial power different from Terrestrial.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's your opinion; I feel otherwise. <i>That said</i>, the previous Dev team said that supernatural powers were <i>not</i> a guaranteed thing among any stripe of God-Blooded. Maybe a given Sun-Child just has an extra dot each of Strength and Appearance, or just has skin the color of gold. <br /> <br /> The more puissant ones may well see dematerialized spirits or develop their own Charms, but either way, it's less about some written attack on your understanding of the way <i>Exaltations</i> work, and more a way of informing about how <i>Essence</i> works in the setting. Namely, the way it permeates and empowers the world around it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T01:54:38-07:00","id":1213705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1213578#post1213578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m still holding out hope it will be. Any degree of celestial power, even if mechanically lesser than true Exalted Charms, passed along bloodlines undermines the setting\u2019s themes of what makes Celestial power different from Terrestrial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. I think that some of those themes might be worth revising.<br /> <br /> \u200bI like the idea that it's possible for powerful Solar or Lunar Exalted to have weird kids in the same way that gods can as an expression of their divinity, particularly in a form of heroic narrative that can imply strength in one's children.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T03:03:51-07:00","id":1213716,"title":"","content":"Of course, Lunars' main avenue of empowering their children (and others) is to impart the powers of the beasts to them.<br /> <br /> Which they're apparently gonna get charms for. Just &quot;I give you the strength of a lion&quot; and boop, beastman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T04:04:08-07:00","id":1213729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1213716#post1213716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just &quot;I give you the strength of a lion&quot; and boop, beastman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the lions of the most renowned capability are the males.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T04:25:50-07:00","id":1213735,"title":"","content":"That's why they gave them the strength, not the hunting ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T05:36:53-07:00","id":1213752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1213729#post1213729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the lions of the most renowned capability are the males.</div> </div> </div> </div>Male lions can and do hunt very effectively, they just don't do it as much once they have a pride cause they have better things to do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T05:42:30-07:00","id":1213756,"title":"","content":"That is also an entirely irrelevant discussion to &quot;how beastmen are made&quot; and lunars empowering people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T05:53:16-07:00","id":1213763,"title":"","content":"Whether by inheritance, Charms, or simply sorcerous workings, the Lunar Exalted will not lack for methods to make their progeny and followers super-human, to varying degrees proportionate to the rarity and importance of the minion.<br /> <br /> The question isn\u2019t the how or the why, and all of the most impressive methods won\u2019t be available until at least Essence 3, anyway.<br /> <br /> The question is whether or not Third Edition will actually deliver on them, as past Editions never did. <br /> <br /> The fact that the core book bothered to tell us more about Yena\u2019s Daughters than directly about Yena Bone-Breaker herself is promising. It showed us that a Lunar\u2019s children can be heroes themselves; political actors who go out, do things, make names for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T07:57:15-07:00","id":1213793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1213763#post1213763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that the core book bothered to tell us more about Yena\u2019s Daughters than directly about Yena Bone-Breaker herself is promising. It showed us that a Lunar\u2019s children can be heroes themselves; political actors who go out, do things, make names for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYes, for people that might be new to them, it was a good way to introduce a focus on the relationship between Lunar Exalted and beast<b>folk</b> to have one delegating authority to a small number of accomplished children who all run their own kinds of bandit and guerrilla operations, rather than having a general army of them (even if Lunars having beastfolk armies are going to come from magic anyway).<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's the kind of thing that made me consider how Ma-Ha-Suchi's write-up referencing his children might refer to his literal children, rather than being a euphemism for a tribe of wolf-headed goatfolk. And given what is said about him, it's interesting to consider that most of his domain's public relations and foreign policy is conducted by those mutated (and possibly powerful) children, while he broods in his citadel.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T19:54:15-07:00","id":1214019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212064#post1212064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar artifacts, is a thought that makes me happy. I hope the first draft is finished quickly, competently, and with style. I've waited so long for it.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm definitely a &quot;team Lunar&quot; guy despite the fact that being a &quot;team anything&quot; guy makes absolutely no sense whatsoever. I can dislike my counter logical desire to see Lunars be conspicuously awesome compared to other exalts, but I can't deny it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what you mean, I have always really liked Lunars for some reason. Glad they have ended up being the next released splat. Of course, it doesn't hurt that while I really like the setting implications of exigents I have no confidence in making a decent charm set from scratch so its unlikely I would ever personally make an exigent character. I mean, I could always just use the example exigence charm sets or use somebody elses homebrew but that feels like cheating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T22:09:48-07:00","id":1214040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1214019#post1214019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, it doesn't hurt that while I really like the setting implications of exigents I have no confidence in making a decent charm set from scratch so its unlikely I would ever personally make an exigent character. I mean, I could always just use the example exigence charm sets or use somebody elses homebrew but that feels like cheating.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Charm sets in the Exigents book will be designed with the intent that players will use them for their own characters. Using them isn\u2019t supposed to feel like cheating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T22:33:00-07:00","id":1214043,"title":"","content":"I know its not intended, I am just a bit weird. But if I ever play a make your own exalt I want to make my own exalt instead of borrow one someone else made. But there is nothing wrong with just doing what is done for most splats and going by charm sets already laid down in the book or some guys home brew. Its just not my personal preference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T07:11:02-07:00","id":1214144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1212140#post1212140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leopard Style - recapturing some of the more interesting elements of Terrible Ascent Driven Beast</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you figure?<br /> <br /> The most interesting thing about the Style was that it had two pinnacle Charms, and that one of them allowed you to carry the person you\u2019re grappling as you run and leap about, while the other one let you use the rigid mobility Charms more flexibly. <br /> <br /> As for those mobility Charms, Solars already have Leaping Tiger Attack, Thunderbolt Attack Prana, God Speed Steps, and Leaping Dodge. Dragon-Blooded likewise have answers to those Charms. So will Lunars.<br /> <br /> Carrying someone you grapple is as simple as using a restraining action as you clinch them, and then moving. <br /> <br /> (Note to self: Check if it is possible to use Mountain-Crossing Leap Technique while restraining, and then throw the victim from the height of the arc.)<br /> <br /> Do you have more in mind than allowing Terrible Ascent-Driven Beast Style to use tiger claws? I don\u2019t think that will make enough of a difference, and especially not one from Tiger Style. <br /> <br /> I think the only reason TAB Style existed was to give Wood Aspect Dragon-Blooded another Style they could use without spending mote surcharges, and also to give mortal barbarians more Charms. <br /> <br /> But there no more surcharges, Wood Aspects have Wood Charms in every Ability (and plenty that let them climb and dance about in trees), and mortals no longer learn Charms. So it no longer has anything to offer that you can\u2019t get anywhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-02-2018, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T08:31:21-07:00","id":1214172,"title":"","content":"Could someone more familiar with OPP's history for this sort of thing give me some speculation on when we'd see the Lunar Kickstarter? Obviously development on a complicated splat like this could take a very long time, but is there a reasonable range? Right now my guess is like, 6-18 months, which seems like a wide gap.<br /> <br /> I'd love to ask the devs this, but I know that making educated guesses on the internet is something that fandoms go nuts over if there's a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T10:30:41-07:00","id":1214208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1214172#post1214172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone more familiar with OPP's history for this sort of thing give me some speculation on when we'd see the Lunar Kickstarter? Obviously development on a complicated splat like this could take a very long time, but is there a reasonable range? Right now my guess is like, 6-18 months, which seems like a wide gap.<br /> <br /> I'd love to ask the devs this, but I know that making educated guesses on the internet is something that fandoms go nuts over if there's a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't expect anything before the end of this year honestly. Although I'm not exactly what you could call the best guesstimator for this matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T10:41:00-07:00","id":1214213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1214172#post1214172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone more familiar with OPP's history for this sort of thing give me some speculation on when we'd see the Lunar Kickstarter? Obviously development on a complicated splat like this could take a very long time, but is there a reasonable range? Right now my guess is like, 6-18 months, which seems like a wide gap.<br /> <br /> I'd love to ask the devs this, but I know that making educated guesses on the internet is something that fandoms go nuts over if there's a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1214208#post1214208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't expect anything before the end of this year honestly. Although I'm not exactly what you could call the best guesstimator for this matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI agree with Gonzo. Anything for <i>this </i>year seems overly optimistic. It's in First Draft stage. It will likely take 3-6 months to get through the Second Draft stage at best. Then we need a majority of the art in and layout underway, which can take anywhere from 3-6 months on its own. These things do not overlap by very much as my understanding is that Art Notes get done up after the Second Draft. Somewhere in there is playtesting as well, though that's likely overlapped across multiple phases. <br /> <br /> After those are done, THEN the Kickstarter planning begins. None of this takes into account pushback from above, delays, a rough editing pass, playtesting finding big mechanical loopholes, etc. So 6-18 months feels like an appropriate range honestly. I'd say optimistically would be February 2019.<br /> <br /> My 2 cents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T10:41:21-07:00","id":1214214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1214172#post1214172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone more familiar with OPP's history for this sort of thing give me some speculation on when we'd see the Lunar Kickstarter? Obviously development on a complicated splat like this could take a very long time, but is there a reasonable range? Right now my guess is like, 6-18 months, which seems like a wide gap.<br /> <br /> I'd love to ask the devs this, but I know that making educated guesses on the internet is something that fandoms go nuts over if there's a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I can say is that we're probably going to do the same thing we did with Dragon-Blooded, and not launch the Kickstarter until we've got the complete text of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T07:22:23-07:00","id":1215032,"title":"","content":"<b>Chapter One: The Lunar Exalted</b><br /> <br /> * History of the Lunars <br /> *** Specific focus on the role of Lunars in the Age of Dreams, response to the Usurpation, and life since the Contagion and the rise of the Scarlet Empress<br /> *** (Sidebar: Solar and Lunar relationships in the Age of Dreams. Touch on origin of the Solar bond. Most were primarily political arrangements, seen as especially auspicious; several with matches founded on love, or at least amicible friendship. A few were abusive, but those were profound outliers)<br /> <br /> * Chosen by Luna <br /> *** The qualities most commonly found amongst those Chosen by Luna, and the experience of Lunar Exaltation<br /> *** (Sidebar: The essential humanity of beastmen)<br /> <br /> * Broken Castes<br /> *** Touch on the breaking of the castes between the Usurpation and the Contagion<br /> *** Description of the Castes, their roles and tendencies, common totems<br /> *** (Sidebar: The original five castes)<br /> <br /> * Essence Fever<br /> *** Animalistic insticts, a need to tear down the status quo, extraordinary intolerance of anyone or anything acting against her intimacies<br /> <br /> * Prestige Spreads<br /> *** The Silver Pact ('normal' Lunars, mutual protection and striving to tear down the Realm)<br /> *** Winding Paths (Lunars who eschew membership in organizations, striking their own paths)<br /> *** (Others?)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Two: The Silver Pact</b><br /> <br /> * What the Silver Pact is, and isn't<br /> *** Mutual support network<br /> *** Favor trading and gift economies<br /> *** Organization, not hierarchy<br /> <br /> * This time of tumult<br /> *** Returning Solars: A Golden Opportunity<br /> *** Rising Deathlords: A Darker Path<br /> *** The Sidereals: Puppetmasters of the Realm<br /> *** Others?<br /> <br /> * Sh'a Oka, the Black Lion<br /> *** Focus: Starve the beast<br /> *** Example: The claiming of the Caul<br /> <br /> * Ma-Ha-Suchi<br /> *** Focus: Rip out the throat<br /> *** Example: Direct assault against Realm strongholds, raising threshold marginalized people as barbarian armies<br /> <br /> * Raksi, the Queen of Fangs<br /> *** Focus: Fear cuts deeper than swords<br /> *** Example: Infiltration of a satrapy, ultimately leading to the Realm destroying it themselves<br /> <br /> (Almost certainly more; First Age and Shogunate-era Lunars, demonstrating different ways to further the Silver Pact's goals of tearing down the Realm)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Three: Character Creation</b><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Four: Traits</b><br /> <br /> * New Merits<br /> *** Heart's Blood<br /> *** Many other merits for capturing animalistic mutations<br /> *** (Sidebar: Supernatural Merits and the Lunar Exalted)<br /> <br /> * New Flaws<br /> *** Wyld-Addict<br /> <br /> * The Castes (Prestige spreads)<br /> *** Full Moon<br /> *** Changing Moon<br /> *** No Moon<br /> *** Casteless<br /> <br /> * Anima Effects<br /> <br /> * Character Advancement<br /> *** Lunar Experience<br /> *** Expression Bonus<br /> *** Caste Bonus<br /> *** Training Times<br /> *** Raising Essence<br /> <br /> * The Great Curse<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Five: Charms</b><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Six: Martial Arts and Sorcery</b><br /> <br /> * (Between three to five Martial Arts styles; at least two animal (I'd guess Lion and Monkey) and three esoteric. Maybe Heaven's Ladder makes it's return here!)<br /> *** (Sidebar: Lunars, Animals, and Martial Arts; in general, martial arts require a roughly humanoid form to use, although Storytellers may make exceptions on a case-by-case basis)<br /> *** (Sidebar: Beastman Transformation and Martial Arts. While in the powerful Beastman Transformation, Lunars use the Terrestrial tag with Martial Arts charms)<br /> * (Lunar specific sorcerous initations; probably one based on the Book of Three Circles because Raksi, and one based on weirdness from the Caul)<br /> *** (Smatterting of Terestrial and Celestial spells)<br /> *** (Example Sorcerous Projects, including creating Beastmen)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Seven: Marked and Bearing Glory</b><br /> <br /> * (Many more Hearthstones, about 2/3rds Standard and 1/3rd Greater)<br /> * (Sidebar: Lunars, Demenses and Manses)<br /> <br /> * Lunars and Artifacts<br /> *** Normal form resonance and dissonance<br /> *** Beastman Transformation is neutral to Moonsilver and dissonant to others<br /> <br /> * (Four to six artifact weapons; two to four artifact armors)<br /> *** (Sidebar: Making an artifact out of moonsilver tattoos. Short answer; don't- enhance with sorcerous projects or your native charms instead)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter Eight: All Things Great and Small</b><br /> <br /> * (Between four to eight Lunar NPCs)<br /> * (Lotta animals, around twenty to thirty. Also expect kickstarter levels to choose animals)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T07:41:11-07:00","id":1215046,"title":"","content":"It mostly seems like a solid idea of what the structure of the book could be.<br /> <br /> However:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1215032#post1215032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * Essence Fever<br /> *** Animalistic insticts, a need to tear down the status quo, extraordinary intolerance of anyone or anything acting against her intimacies</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI would not want this to be their Essence Fever. I think animal qualities should be present, but not leaned into this hard, and I wouldn't personally care for them being intrinsically anarchic.<br /> <br /> And<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Ma-Ha-Suchi<br /> *** Focus: Rip out the throat<br /> *** Example: Direct assault against Realm strongholds, raising threshold marginalized people as barbarian armies</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though an advantage to the book coming comparatively early is that it will be close enough to not completely override how Ma-Ha-Suchi was portrayed in the core again.<br /> <br /> \u200bNow, in fariness, in First Edition, his whole characterisation of &quot;I'm burnt out on the politics of the Exalted, just leave me alone&quot; was in a chapter fiction. And sure, sometimes things from an earlier book shouldn't constrain a later one if changes need to be made.<br /> <br /> \u200bI just think that Ma-Ha-Suchi as he is in the core is much more interesting than being yet another barbarian warlord.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:06:23-07:00","id":1215060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1215046#post1215046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI would not want this to be their Essence Fever. I think animal qualities should be present, but not leaned into this hard, and I wouldn't personally care for them being intrinsically anarchic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm leaning a bit into Keychain of Creation's portrayal here. I mean, I recognize this particular concept won't work for everyone, but I think it's vital that Essence Fever is presented distinctly for Lunars than Solars, and this was a stab at doing so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1215046#post1215046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI just think that Ma-Ha-Suchi as he is in the core is much more interesting than being yet another barbarian warlord.</div> </div> </div> </div>My hand to god, I'd forgotten Ma-Ha-Suchi was in the core. It's been a while &gt;&lt;<br /> And I agree, using him as the prototypical barbarian warlord would be... underselling. OTOH, I think there does and should need to be an example of the 'Fuck subtle, just murder' approach. Maybe introduce a new Lunar luminary for that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:45:11-07:00","id":1215077,"title":"","content":"I doubt anyone who says \u201cfuck subtle, just murder\u201d without any degree of nuance or anything lives long enough to become an elder or even a luminary.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re looking for someone who is taking the war to the Realm and is murdering people, Sh\u2019a Oka seems to be a good choice already.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll admit, I don\u2019t know that we\u2019ve got an elder who shows up, agitates a disenfranchised group against a nearby Satrapy, blesses some warriors with assured victory, and then runs off before they all get murdered. But I\u2019m not sure that was what you were going for either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:51:37-07:00","id":1215081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1215077#post1215077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll admit, I don\u2019t know that we\u2019ve got an elder who shows up, agitates a disenfranchised group against a nearby Satrapy, blesses some warriors with assured victory, and then runs off before they all get murdered. But I\u2019m not sure that was what you were going for either.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I was going for, yes.<br /> <br /> The Black Lion's approach- at least, from the little we see in one chapter fiction about how Faxai is being handled -is to starve the beast. Avoid direct confrontation, keep the Dynasty unable to gather wealth and resources, employ fabian tactics writ large.<br /> <br /> IMO, there should be a 'raise armies and smash at gates' figure, agitating for more direct and immediate solutions, to use as contrast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:57:00-07:00","id":1215087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1215081#post1215081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is what I was going for, yes.<br /> <br /> The Black Lion's approach- at least, from the little we see in one chapter fiction about how Faxai is being handled -is to starve the beast. Avoid direct confrontation, keep the Dynasty unable to gather wealth and resources, employ fabian tactics writ large.<br /> <br /> IMO, there should be a 'raise armies and smash at gates' figure, agitating for more direct and immediate solutions, to use as contrast.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Caul preview in The Realm, released during the DB Kickstarter, has the Black Lion leading armies of lionfolk against the Realm's fortresses on the Caul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T10:53:52-07:00","id":1215148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1215077#post1215077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt anyone who says \u201cfuck subtle, just murder\u201d without any degree of nuance or anything lives long enough to become an elder or even a luminary.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI was wondering about the idea of somebody that was already powerful before the Usurpation and managed to live through it and survive to the modern day...<br /> <br /> \u200bBut then realised how even most of them would probably still be limited to Essence 5, and thus, while powerful, not so powerful that they can treat the Realm and the Sidereals with significant open contempt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:56:54-07:00","id":1215186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1215032#post1215032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*** Specific focus on the role of Lunars in the Age of Dreams</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you didn\u2019t mean it like that, but I would avoid the idea that Lunar Exalted had a \u201crole\u201d the same way that \u201cWhat Fire Has Wrought\u201d did with the Dragon-Blooded. In the past ages, Dragon-Blooded could be kings and queens without a Celestial Exalt anywhere to be seen.<br /> <br /> \u201cRoles\u201d in the plural is fine, though. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Chosen by Luna <br /> *** The qualities most commonly found amongst those Chosen by Luna </div> </div> </div>We didn\u2019t get this with Solars, nor anything hinting at common qualities among those who \u201cbred true\u201d among Dragon-Blooded children.<br /> <br /> The developers don\u2019t seem to want to narrow possibilities about what kind of people might be Chosen by Luna. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Broken Castes<br /> *** Touch on the breaking of the castes between the Usurpation and the Contagion<br /> *** Description of the Castes, their roles and tendencies, common totems<br /> *** (Sidebar: The original five castes) </div> </div> </div>Some mention should be made that this wasn\u2019t the first time the Lunar Exalted recreated their Castes. But I don\u2019t want any details or even hints about what the five Castes of the First Age were like. <br /> <br /> If the current castes are anything like those they had for the War of the Gods, that might be neat to mention. Not sure that I would care for any suggestion that the Lunar Exalted didn\u2019t originally have any castes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Essence Fever<br /> *** Animalistic insticts, a need to tear down the status quo, extraordinary intolerance of anyone or anything acting against her intimacies </div> </div> </div>Ehhh... not sold. <br /> <br /> Definitely should talk about gaining and acting upon the instinctual knowledge of Heart\u2019s Blood acquisition and shapeshifting, along with urges to Hunt and Become. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * This time of tumult<br /> *** Returning Solars: A Golden Opportunity<br /> *** Rising Deathlords: A Darker Path </div> </div> </div>I like the implication that, from the Lunar perspective, both of these rising forces seem like dangerous but potentially useful allies or catspaws in their war against the Ream and Sidereals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Almost certainly more; First Age and Shogunate-era Lunars, demonstrating different ways to further the Silver Pact's goals of tearing down the Realm </div> </div> </div>I disagree with your assignment of focuses, but like the idea of the writing focusing on focuses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * New Flaws<br /> *** Wyld-Addict </div> </div> </div>I feel this is best left to a book about the Wyld itself. Solar Exalted have just as much or more reason to frequent the Wyld as Lunars, since Solars can appear anywhere and they can learn Wyld-Shaping Technique, but we didn\u2019t get this Flaw in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Leave it for a book that actually dives into the details about the Wyld and Wyld barbarians, not the Threshold.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *** Caste Bonus </div> </div> </div>Oh, that\u2019s probably how Robert intends to balance Casteless Lunars against Tattooed Lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *** (Sidebar: Lunars, Animals, and Martial Arts; in general, martial arts require a roughly humanoid form to use, although Storytellers may make exceptions on a case-by-case basis) </div> </div> </div>Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style should be pretty shape-agnostic, as long as your current body can vocalize. Or stamp out an audible beat. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *** (Sidebar: Beastman Transformation and Martial Arts. While in the powerful Beastman Transformation, Lunars use the Terrestrial tag with Martial Arts charms) </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting idea to balance DBT and prevent it from being the One True Build, on top of reducing resonance with artifacts. Perhaps it would also hinder Celestial Circle Sorcery?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *** (Example Sorcerous Projects, including creating Beastmen) </div> </div> </div>Oh, that\u2019s a cool idea. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * (Many more Hearthstones, about 2/3rds Standard and 1/3rd Greater)<br /> * (Sidebar: Lunars, Demenses and Manses) </div> </div> </div>If we didn\u2019t get this in \u201cWhat Fire Has Wrought\u201d, I definitely don\u2019t expect it in \u201cFangs at the Gate\u201d. Lunars have a harder time holding onto geographical assets than the Dragon-Blooded. <br /> <br /> We\u2019re waiting for \u201cTowers of the Mighty.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Chapter Eight: All Things Great and Small</b> </div> </div> </div>Or call it \u201cPredators and Prey\u201d.<br /> <br /> The Lunars are the predators. The animals, gigantic dinosaurs and all, are the prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:18:30-07:00","id":1215192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1215032#post1215032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Chapter One: The Lunar Exalted</b><br /> <br /> * History of the Lunars<br /> *** Specific focus on the role of Lunars in the Age of Dreams, response to the Usurpation, and life since the Contagion and the rise of the Scarlet Empress<br /> *** (Sidebar: Solar and Lunar relationships in the Age of Dreams. Touch on origin of the Solar bond. Most were primarily political arrangements, seen as especially auspicious; several with matches founded on love, or at least amicible friendship. A few were abusive, but those were profound outliers)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine that any information on Lunars re: the First Age is going to be very brief. That time is gone, it's not coming back, and the Chosen of Luna aren't what they were then. Related to this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Chosen by Luna<br /> *** The qualities most commonly found amongst those Chosen by Luna, and the experience of Lunar Exaltation<br /> *** (Sidebar: The essential humanity of beastmen)<br /> <br /> * Broken Castes<br /> *** Touch on the breaking of the castes between the Usurpation and the Contagion<br /> *** Description of the Castes, their roles and tendencies, common totems<br /> *** (Sidebar: The original five castes) </div> </div> </div>I doubt that we'll get much word count devoted to the former castes, either. Especially since in this case, the &quot;original five&quot; weren't actually the original castes that the Lunars had when they were first around; they changed after the Divine Revolution was over. The present set of castes is going to be the third such division, not the second.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Essence Fever<br /> *** Animalistic insticts, a need to tear down the status quo, extraordinary intolerance of anyone or anything acting against her intimacies </div> </div> </div>&quot;Animalistic instincts&quot; is at once an overly broad and misleadingly attributive description of behavior. One thing we might see, which 1e touched upon, is that everyone becomes a lot less squeamish about hunting and acquiring forms. Maybe they'll also &quot;toughen up&quot; in a manner similar to Akira Fudo after absorbing and overcoming Amon at the beginning of most iterations of Devilman, but that's even more of a personal interpretation on my part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 05-04-2018, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T13:50:04-07:00","id":1215223,"title":"","content":"The beastiary for the GURPS Black Ops book was titled \u201cThings to Hunt and Kill\u201d and a flowery version of that seems like it could work for Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T14:02:42-07:00","id":1215226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1215192#post1215192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Animalistic instincts&quot; is at once an overly broad and misleadingly attributive description of behavior. One thing we might see, which 1e touched upon, is that everyone becomes a lot less squeamish about hunting and acquiring forms. Maybe they'll also &quot;toughen up&quot; in a manner similar to Akira Fudo after absorbing and overcoming Amon at the beginning of most iterations of Devilman, but that's even more of a personal interpretation on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't always agree with you, but I <i>do </i>support anything that brings more Devilman into the setting.<br /> <br /> <sub>Okay so Infernals probably have more thematic claim, but 1) some overlap is <i>perfectly okay</i>, 2) Devilman's demons already have strong thematic connections to animals and nature, and 3) Infernals seem more like Apostles anyway.</sub><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T16:34:36-07:00","id":1215268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1215032#post1215032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*** (Sidebar: The original five castes)</div> </div> </div> </div>No. That's all dead a millennium, and should be left dead, especially as it suggests modern Lunars are broken and a patch job.<br /> <br /> Instead, I'd explicitly call the creation of the current castes something like the &quot;Third Remaking&quot;, suggesting that the Lunars are on their <i>fourth</i> set of castes since their creation. When Creation next changes, the Lunars will of course change to match it . . . but it's never going to be a matter of &quot;restoring&quot; one of their many past sets of castes, because Creation's never going back to the First Age, it's becoming something new. I'd then slip in a statement that Lunars had <i>seven</i> castes or something as of the Usurpation, just to cut off perpetration of the old canon &quot;these are the now-missing castes&quot; stuff completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T05:43:58-07:00","id":1220233,"title":"","content":"There's been no hint that this might happen, but:<br /> <br /> What are people's thoughts about the possibility of an ancient, noble-class warstrider being included in the Lunar book? (Not royal-class like the Walking Devil Tower)<br /> <br /> Does it feel like an appropriate inclusion to highlight an extreme example of what Lunars are still capable of, and call back to their former glory during the First Age? A reminder that the level of their usual tools and infrastructure is limited more by their situation than by a lack of capability?<br /> <br /> Does it feel like it would offers a vital contrast to all of the Lunar builds which don't necessarily synergize well with piloting a warstrider, so that building a Beastboy or a Werewolf character feels more meaningful because you could choose to play a combat-focused character who relies entirely on tools rather than shapeshifting, sorcery, or martial arts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T13:46:59-07:00","id":1220322,"title":"","content":"More likely in the Kickstarter built Companion than the Lunar hardback I\u2019d wager. Warstrider s require a great deal of infrastructure to maintain and Lunars are uniquely* capable of working on legendary-size scale without them - so it would seem an unlikely use of wordcount for the main book, though a welcome bonus for the companion if they got the chance.<br /> <br /> *At least uniquely in terms of corebook revealed Exalted. Infernal Shintai and Alchemicals Colossi are likely to give them avenues to Legendary-size without Warstriders as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T14:04:24-07:00","id":1220324,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with a moonsilver warstrider being in there (after all, the Walking Devil Tower isn't one you can really take with a character, as it's N/A), but it would be fairly down my list of what to see in there. *<br /> Part of a kickstarter extra makes more sense to me.<br /> <br /> *Saying this. I was thinking about what I would want to see there. Charms of course. Spells, especially Celestial ones. Some moonsilver artefacts. People seemed really keen on MA, but that's not a priority for me either; I'd be fine with a few animal styles or something, but Lunars are one of the less MA-focused Exalts, compared to DBs, Sidereals and Getimians.<br /> Lots of animals, of course. I suspect animals might take up a lot of the room that What Fire Has Wrought spent on MA/Sorcery/Evocations.<br /> All depends on word count, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T14:10:54-07:00","id":1220330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1220322#post1220322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Warstriders require a great deal of infrastructure to maintain</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify my idea, I was thinking of an ancient warstrider that an elder had hidden away somewhere until the time seemed right to unleash it. After all, the primary point of the thing would be to let a player with a newly Exalted Lunar use the thing, which is made easier if no one is currently using it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1220324#post1220324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fine with a moonsilver warstrider being in there (after all, the Walking Devil Tower isn't one you can really take with a character, as it's N/A)</div> </div> </div> </div>Storyteller and player agreements would allow it, and Karvara is as fine a warstrider to turn against the Realm as any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T14:44:53-07:00","id":1220340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1220330#post1220330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify my idea, I was thinking of an ancient warstrider that an elder had hidden away somewhere until the time seemed right to unleash it. After all, the primary point of the thing would be to let a player with a newly Exalted Lunar use the thing, which is made easier if no one is currently using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be the way to do it, yeah. I took Godspeed Vanguard: it's background was just that it was hidden somewhere in the wilderness ready to be found.<br /> <br /> I also think that a Moonsilver Warstrider might be one that could potentially survive better than any other warstriders without the necessary infrastructure (via evocations).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Storyteller and player agreements would allow it </div> </div> </div>Yes... but you could say that about anything. I don't think a lot of STs would let a PC start with an N/A artefact.<br /> <br /> Saying that, my ST did say if I played a DB in an Essence 5 Solar game, which is I was considering, that I could take an N/A warstrider (as it'd be balanced by my weaker power). But Karvara literally doesn't work for Dragonblood.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-19-2018, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T14:48:29-07:00","id":1220343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1220340#post1220340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that a Moonsilver Warstrider might be one that could potentially survive better than any other warstriders without the necessary infrastructure (via evocations).</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that moonsilver is the metal perhaps most associated with hunting, I've given thought to a moonsilver warstrider designed to operate across great distances and for lots of time without maintenance or repair, in order to better locate and pursue prey. I haven't come to satisfying conclusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T20:19:32-07:00","id":1220410,"title":"","content":"Returning to the idea that Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style is pretty form-agnostic (also likely designed by a Lunar Exalt), what do you think about the Lunar manual having a song-based Sorcery Initiation?<br /> <br /> There's one example ritual in the corebook, just as the Heptagram Initiation had one in the corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T21:09:20-07:00","id":1220427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1220410#post1220410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Returning to the idea that Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style is pretty form-agnostic (also likely designed by a Lunar Exalt), what do you think about the Lunar manual having a song-based Sorcery Initiation?<br /> <br /> There's one example ritual in the corebook, just as the Heptagram Initiation had one in the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>My gut puts a song-based initiation as a Serenity Sid thing, but I could see it.<br /> <br /> Initiation by ritual hunting could be a good Lunar one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T23:54:37-07:00","id":1220452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1220410#post1220410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what do you think about the Lunar manual having a song-based Sorcery Initiation?</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be a good place for it. Either that, or in the sorcery book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T03:47:24-07:00","id":1220493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1220340#post1220340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't think a lot of STs would let a PC start with an N/A artefact.</div> </div> </div> </div> Slight tangent.<br /> Is that based on the strength of the N/A rated artifacts we currently have in 3e or years of what N/A used to mean? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T04:22:52-07:00","id":1220499,"title":"","content":"The whole point of N/A is you can't start with them. They's why they don't have a dot rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T04:59:50-07:00","id":1220505,"title":"","content":"Essentially, what Elfive said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T05:21:34-07:00","id":1220514,"title":"","content":"Going to treat it as a vote for the latter.<br /> <br /> N/A is much more a part of the actual game system than it ever was for 2e even if I am presently unclear where it actually sits now.<br /> <br /> 2e used the category to keep power out of PCs hands that would destroy a sense of progression and warp games around their existence, if you started<br /> with the Five Metal Shrike you could blow up cities with a push of a button and nobody else could do anything like that until at least essence 5.<br /> <br /> This is much less the case with 3e where Karvara and Ascendant Nova Phoenix are going to be domineering if you let a PC have them but this would also be the case with essentially any other kind of artifact vehicle. I mean if you had Horizon Endeavor at your disposal from essence 1 you are hardly going to set up base somewhere landlocked.<br /> <br /> Its also true of the crafting system where N/A rated artifacts are a part of the craft system rather than covered in a sidebar and gated by Storyteller permission. The rather dismissive response suggests that none of this was really considered and that 2e conventions still dominate the mental space for what N/A looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","user":"Bastet","date":". 05-20-2018, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T05:54:31-07:00","id":1220526,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, has anyone ever thought that if you wanted to play as Coyote or Raven, who stole Fire from the Sun, you could reskin the sorcery initiation &quot;Pact with an Ifrit Lord&quot; and use the shaping ritual which allows you to steal the Essence from the fires and Fire Elementals around you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-20-2018, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T06:06:55-07:00","id":1220528,"title":"","content":"Similar but not quite, my version was more based on Prometheus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T09:12:28-07:00","id":1220553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1220493#post1220493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Slight tangent.<br /> Is that based on the strength of the N/A rated artifacts we currently have in 3e or years of what N/A used to mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's based on the ruling on Page 159 <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Artifacts of yet greater power may still be found in Creation on the rarest of occasions: mighty remnants of the long-fallen First Age such as invincible warstriders, \u201cten thousand-year daiklaves,\u201d or magical warships. These are considered to be rated Artifact N/A, and cannot be taken during character creation by spending points\u2014as these items are of chronicle-defining power, they may only make their way into a player\u2019s possession if the player and Storyteller both want to spin a game around that story, or if a player somehow forges or unearths such a world-shaking miracle during play.\u200b&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T10:50:20-07:00","id":1220578,"title":"","content":"Ok.<br /> I was trying to ascertain if Storytellers were bothering to really look at Karvara and Ascendant Nova Phoenix or if they felt the N/A rating told them everything they needed to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","user":"Bastet","date":". 05-20-2018, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T06:35:45-07:00","id":1221141,"title":"","content":"As a ST, I kind of skimmed them. Then I went back and looked at Karvara properly because it seemed cool. <br /> Then, as a player, when I told my ST I was thinking of playing a DB with a warstrider in an Essence 5 Solar game, and he said I could have one of those since it'd balance out, I went back and gave them a proper look (and concluded it wasn't really feasible anyway).<br /> <br /> But yeah, as an ST, I went &quot;oh, these are artefacts that you design your whole game around, not things new characters joining an existing game could feasibly start with.&quot; Based on them being N/A.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T22:24:34-07:00","id":1222352,"title":"","content":"Okay, random thought . . . .<br /> <br /> There are basically three classes of non-native magic available to the Exalted -- Evocations, Martial Arts, and Sorcery.<br /> <br /> There are three Lunar castes.<br /> <br /> What if Lunars had &quot;caste&quot; cost access to one of the three classes? Perhaps the mystical No Moons choose between Evocations and Sorcery (between powers of magic items, and magic spells), the warrior Full Moons between Evocations and Martial Arts (between the powers of weapons, and non-weapon combat), and the social Changing Moons choose between Martial Arts and Sorcery (between two classes of techniques created and transmitted by communities)?<br /> <br /> That leaves open the question of how to handle the casteless, of course. Pick one of any?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Alternate thought -- between the &quot;witch&quot; nature of Luna and the alien/uncanny nature of sorcery/necromancy, maybe all Lunars should get Favored costs for spells, period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","user":"Verzio","date":". 05-27-2018, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T00:25:44-07:00","id":1222362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1220514#post1220514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going to treat it as a vote for the latter.<br /> <br /> N/A is much more a part of the actual game system than it ever was for 2e even if I am presently unclear where it actually sits now.<br /> <br /> 2e used the category to keep power out of PCs hands that would destroy a sense of progression and warp games around their existence, if you started<br /> with the Five Metal Shrike you could blow up cities with a push of a button and nobody else could do anything like that until at least essence 5.<br /> <br /> This is much less the case with 3e where Karvara and Ascendant Nova Phoenix are going to be domineering if you let a PC have them but this would also be the case with essentially any other kind of artifact vehicle. I mean if you had Horizon Endeavor at your disposal from essence 1 you are hardly going to set up base somewhere landlocked.<br /> <br /> Its also true of the crafting system where N/A rated artifacts are a part of the craft system rather than covered in a sidebar and gated by Storyteller permission. The rather dismissive response suggests that none of this was really considered and that 2e conventions still dominate the mental space for what N/A looks like.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> None of which changes the fact that their Merit rating is literally &quot;non-applicable&quot; because they aren't purchasable as Merits. That's objectively what those words mean. Yes, the examples we have are less setting-break &quot;I WIN!&quot; buttons then they were in 2E, thank god, but they're still by design at a power tier above what is designed to be purchasable with Merit dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T02:48:57-07:00","id":1222368,"title":"","content":"Yes, keep making this about me not understanding what N/A means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T04:58:34-07:00","id":1222378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222352#post1222352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternate thought -- between the &quot;witch&quot; nature of Luna and the alien/uncanny nature of sorcery/necromancy, maybe all Lunars should get Favored costs for spells, period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like how Sidereals all Favor the Martial Arts Abilities.<br /> <br /> That could be neat, but with Sidereals it ties into how they alone can develop and teach Sidereal Martial Arts, whereas Lunars are not more gifted sorcerors or necromancers than Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T08:02:28-07:00","id":1222417,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar572_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"572\" data-vbnamecard=\"572\">Verzio</a> I wouldn't make the distinction of Evocation and MA Charms one of weapon and non-weapon combat. There are Evocations that come from non-weapon objects and MAs who are unusable without weapons, so that line of thought frays pretty quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T20:11:29-07:00","id":1222569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222378#post1222378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like how Sidereals all Favor the Martial Arts Abilities.<br /> <br /> That could be neat, but with Sidereals it ties into how they alone can develop and teach Sidereal Martial Arts, whereas Lunars are not more gifted sorcerors or necromancers than Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's sorta-parallel but not perfectly parallel. An alternative way to look is parallel to how Dragon-Blooded are the best-ish with Evocations among non-Solars because they are resonant with five MMs (if you count each color of jade as its own)/the most common MM(s). A sorcery affinity among all Lunars would fall somewhere in the middle of the Sidereal and DB examples. Only the best Solar and Sidereal sorcerers could learn spells as easily as <i>any</i> Lunar could, even if the peak of Solar sorcery is beyond what Lunars can reach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222417#post1222417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar572_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"572\" data-vbnamecard=\"572\">Verzio</a> I wouldn't make the distinction of Evocation and MA Charms one of weapon and non-weapon combat. There are Evocations that come from non-weapon objects and MAs who are unusable without weapons, so that line of thought frays pretty quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those were hyper-brief parenthetical stereotype explanations of how each pair of choices fits in with Caste themes, rather than attempts to actually make a holds-water distinction between the member elements. It's enough that <i>most</i> Evocations published are on weapons or armor to thematically tie Evocations to Full Moons as an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T20:58:30-07:00","id":1222574,"title":"","content":"Something that sort of stand sout to me with Lunars is they have a lot of things where they have a pretty solid assumed competence without bonsues. They're not Disonant with any metal, they can get the second circles of both sorcery and necromancy, they dont's uffer Terrestrial in MAs. They basically havea pretty solid baselien compitence and no real weaknesses. Like, looking at Sidereals I doubt they get past first Circle of necromancy, they're Dissonant with everything not-starmetal, and likely have a much more regimented Charmset. Other Celestials on par with them and Lunars will probably be a solid baseline competence though. The issue is to remember that Solars and thier kin have a really high total competence and non-Solars just aren't going to get that.<br /> <br /> But within the bounds of what Lunars get, they ahve nothing theys eem especially bad at when it comes ot baseline competence. It's a matter instead of what they do great with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T21:56:38-07:00","id":1222579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222569#post1222569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> Those were hyper-brief parenthetical stereotype explanations of how each pair of choices fits in with Caste themes, rather than attempts to actually make a holds-water distinction between the member elements. It's enough that <i>most</i> Evocations published are on weapons or armor to thematically tie Evocations to Full Moons as an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just pointing out what I think, it is not a sound way to put it.<br /> <br /> Anyone can find a reason for any of either Sorcery, MA Charms, or Evocations, be thematically tied to any of the Lunar Castes.<br /> <br /> Not every reason will be sound, so we can discuss flaws to help each other and try to make them better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T03:55:34-07:00","id":1222601,"title":"","content":"As it currently is set to stand, sorcery competence goes, in ascending order, terrestrials (first circle only)-&gt; lunars (second circle but can't favour it) -&gt; sidereals (second circle and <i>can</i> favour it) -&gt; solars (third circle), while necromancy goes sidereals (first circle only)-&gt; lunars (second circle but can't favour it)-&gt; solars (second circle and <i>can</i> favour it) -&gt; abyssals (third circle). <br /> <br /> So there's a sort of symmetry there. They're just barely in third place for both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T04:11:08-07:00","id":1222603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222352#post1222352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Lunars had &quot;caste&quot; cost access to one of the three classes? Perhaps the mystical No Moons choose between Evocations and Sorcery (between powers of magic items, and magic spells), the warrior Full Moons between Evocations and Martial Arts (between the powers of weapons, and non-weapon combat), and the social Changing Moons choose between Martial Arts and Sorcery (between two classes of techniques created and transmitted by communities)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I see is that this would end up being seen as a deterrent to (for example) a Changing Moon owning Artifact rather than a bonus to a No Moon or Full Moon. <br /> <br /> Personally speaking I think Moonsilver Evocations play an important role in the changing face of Lunars, most notably moving away from the late 2e obsession with the Other Moons and the love affair with the Beyond. It resolves the &quot;too many hats&quot; problem and in a purely meta way they let you reach for the powersets of Chosen of the Moon which never came to pass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T14:14:18-07:00","id":1222705,"title":"","content":"What if the combination of Lunar Attribute Charms with Martial Arts Charms is so powerful that it makes up for a complete inability to favor Martial Arts Charms?<br /> <br /> What if Lunar Charms for spellcasting are so powerful that it makes up for a complete inability to favor Spells?<br /> <br /> What if Lunar XP is easier to acquire than Dragon or Solar XP, such that they have more of it, and more frequently, to spend on these things they cannot favor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T15:16:38-07:00","id":1222717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222705#post1222705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the combination of Lunar Attribute Charms with Martial Arts Charms is so powerful that it makes up for a complete inability to favor Martial Arts Charms?<br /> <br /> What if Lunar Charms for spellcasting are so powerful that it makes up for a complete inability to favor Spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you on these two. I fully expect, for martial arts at least, that the lunar's ability to throw native charms into the mix of <i>everything</i> they do will create room for synergies that are impossible for other exalt types. I am excited to see what synergies these will bring. <br /> <br /> Solars are at the peak of martial arts, but they cannot combine a martial arts charm with a melee charm. This may be somewhat tempered by much of what lunars can do being simple, but there'll till be plenty that they can do that Solars simply cannot.<br /> <br /> Sorcery might be a little trickier to swing. It's not like Solars can't bring occult charms to bear while shaping sorcery, or have their sorcery boosted by occult charms. Still, Intelligence charms may bring things to the table that are not possible with ability based charms. Unclear as yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222705#post1222705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Lunar XP is easier to acquire than Dragon or Solar XP, such that they have more of it, and more frequently, to spend on these things they cannot favor?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that I'd like to see lunars get xp at a greater rate than other splats. I hated 2E xp tax for not being a solar. I think I'd feel the same of any splat getting a power boost in this manner. Remember as well that the only thing that the splat xp cannot be spent on is native charms. Giving them a boost to splat xp therefore gives them a boost to attribute progression, ability progression, willpower, merits, evocations, <i>and </i>martial arts and sorcery. Trying to boost them like that may force the team to make a whole lot of tradeoffs that may not be pleasant for lunar players either. and that's all assuming that the players in question are even using the suggested rules for gaining splat xp. (mine currently isn't as it was deemed an annoying strong-arm method of forcing players to act in a prescribed way.)<br /> <br /> I would be very sad if lunar sorcerers and martial artists were unable to find a way to favor their respective fields of specialization. However, if that's the only way to balance the massive potential of combining attribute charms and their specialties freely then so be it. I would live with that. I do hope they find a different way to achieve that balance, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T16:41:46-07:00","id":1222739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222717#post1222717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcery might be a little trickier to swing. It's not like Solars can't bring occult charms to bear while shaping sorcery, or have their sorcery boosted by occult charms. Still, Intelligence charms may bring things to the table that are not possible with ability based charms. Unclear as yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, on the surface, boosting sorcery with Lunar Charms starts out three times as difficult for Lunars than Ability-based Exalted, since spells might have dice-pools based on any of the three Mental Attributes, and Lunars don't have an Occult Excellency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T17:35:07-07:00","id":1222757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222739#post1222739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, on the surface, boosting sorcery with Lunar Charms starts out three times as difficult for Lunars than Ability-based Exalted, since spells might have dice-pools based on any of the three Mental Attributes, and Lunars don't have an Occult Excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Stunts allowing one to fork in a second Attribute might alleviate some of that, since I'd imagine stunting your Intelligence into casting spells shouldn't be that hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T20:39:44-07:00","id":1222809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222705#post1222705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the combination of Lunar Attribute Charms with Martial Arts Charms is so powerful that it makes up for a complete inability to favor Martial Arts Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there seriously <i>anyone</i> who doesn\u2019t see this as a given? Show of hands, who here would not-favor Martial Arts in exchange for being able to combine it with Brawl <i>and</i> Melee Charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T20:59:39-07:00","id":1222816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222809#post1222809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there seriously <i>anyone</i> who doesn\u2019t see this as a given? Show of hands, who here would not-favor Martial Arts in exchange for being able to combine it with Brawl <i>and</i> Melee Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, the Brawl and Melee Charms were balanced against the inability to combine with Martial Arts Charms, and Attribute Charms would have to be balanced against that ability.<br /> <br /> So the question of &quot;power&quot; seems like an apple-and-orange comparison.<br /> <br /> But it's a simple observation that it would seem more convenient and satisfying to be able to combo your Martial Arts Charms with your native Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T23:21:13-07:00","id":1222835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222603#post1222603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I see is that this would end up being seen as a deterrent to (for example) a Changing Moon owning Artifact rather than a bonus to a No Moon or Full Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any incentive to do X can be seen as a deterrent to do Y if people are firmly determined to see it that way. But in context, no type of Solar has &quot;favored&quot; costs for Evocations, paying full unfavored charm costs. And DBs have it even worse, paying worse-than-unfavored costs with no means (like they can with spells) to reduce it to &quot;mere&quot; unfavored costs. If a lack of favored cost access is a deterrent to a Changing Moon owning an artifact, it's a deterrent to owning artifacts already suffered by all other Exalted.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Having worked that through, &quot;Nobody else can favor Evocations, why are you suggesting No Moons and Full Moons should have the chance&quot; strikes me as a quite serious objection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T23:45:05-07:00","id":1222836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222601#post1222601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it currently is set to stand, sorcery competence goes, in ascending order, terrestrials (first circle only)-&gt; lunars (second circle but can't favour it) -&gt; sidereals (second circle and <i>can</i> favour it) -&gt; solars (third circle), while necromancy goes sidereals (first circle only)-&gt; lunars (second circle but can't favour it)-&gt; solars (second circle and <i>can</i> favour it) -&gt; abyssals (third circle).<br /> <br /> So there's a sort of symmetry there. They're just barely in third place for both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which doesn't break by allowing Lunars favored costs for spells; it just moves Lunars up in general.<br /> <br /> For example, having all Lunars treat spells as favored, by individual characters (because nobody plays a splat as a collective) it would be:<br /> <br /> Sorcery: Terrestrials (first circle only)-&gt; Sidereals who don't have Occult as caste/favored -&gt; Sidereals who have Occult as caste/favored and Lunars -&gt; Solars (third circle).<br /> Necromancy: Sidereals (first circle only) -&gt; Solars who don't have Occult as caste/favored -&gt; Solars who have Occult as caste/favored and Lunars -&gt; Abyssals (third circle).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T02:18:32-07:00","id":1222851,"title":"","content":"I honestly can't see the problem with Lunars being able to favor MA or Sorc, and same goes with other attribute exalted <br /> If it was too strong with favored it would still be too strong unfavored still, XP doesn't make a combination of charms and spells weaker. <br /> All this does in a mixed splat game with 4-5 people is that a Lunar that want to do MA or Sorc will fall behind in XP in those areas, And there is always a second person that dig in to Sorcery or MA and suddenly you might have a Lunar sorc with a sid or solar sorc, and if the Lunar and the Solar/sid pour same amount of xp in sorc the Lunar will fall behind fast, because it isn't only 2xp, that can quickly become 10-20xp in a game, <br /> And beliving that you always will get flat +4 lunar xp is very optimistic, since we can also asume that the others will have flat +4 and then the lunar will fall behind in splat xp <br /> If the argument is &quot;I have seen Solar taking Evocation for unfavored&quot; than I have to remind you that non can favor evocation and most(not deebs) will be on equal foting there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T03:04:54-07:00","id":1222853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222835#post1222835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a lack of favored cost access is a deterrent to a Changing Moon owning an artifact, it's a deterrent to owning artifacts already suffered by all other Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are different conversations. The xp cost that Solars and Dragon-Blooded pay for Evocations is a reflection of the power they offer relative to their native charms. If three out of the four Caste options (including Casteless) can favour Evocations that becomes their default cost to any Lunar interested in them except Changing Moons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T06:12:02-07:00","id":1222875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222853#post1222853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The xp cost that Solars and Dragon-Blooded pay for Evocations is a reflection of the power they offer relative to their native charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Dragonblood, that's true, though I don't think it is for Solars.<br /> <br /> It might be for Lunars though. Their Moonsilver evocations are, I assume, balanced against Solar charms, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway. Regardless of whether it'd be balanced for them to favour MA/spells, have people considered how it'd work?<br /> Presumably, you'd favour spells if you favour Intelligence. That's fine.<br /> But what about MA? That's an actual ability after all, and Lunars have no favoured abilities. <br /> (In 2nd ed, 75% of Lunars favoured MA as their one favoured ability.)<br /> If you favour Dex? That makes Dex, already the best attribute, even better. Wits? That'd make No Moons the best Martial Artist, which is also odd.<br /> <br /> That does make me consider that it does make some sense to say Full Moons favour Martial Arts, and No Moons spells, but then what do Changing Moons get? Evocations doesn't really make much sense to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> My own personal preference would be for Lunars to favour any style based on an animal that they have the form for. Or just all animal styles. And not favour any other MAs.<br /> But I doubt that anyone else will want that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T07:44:06-07:00","id":1222895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222875#post1222875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Dragonblood, that's true, though I don't think it is for Solars.<br /> <br /> It might be for Lunars though. Their Moonsilver evocations are, I assume, balanced against Solar charms, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway. Regardless of whether it'd be balanced for them to favour MA/spells, have people considered how it'd work?<br /> Presumably, you'd favour spells if you favour Intelligence. That's fine.<br /> But what about MA? That's an actual ability after all, and Lunars have no favoured abilities.<br /> (In 2nd ed, 75% of Lunars favoured MA as their one favoured ability.)<br /> If you favour Dex? That makes Dex, already the best attribute, even better. Wits? That'd make No Moons the best Martial Artist, which is also odd.<br /> <br /> That does make me consider that it does make some sense to say Full Moons favour Martial Arts, and No Moons spells, but then what do Changing Moons get? Evocations doesn't really make much sense to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> My own personal preference would be for Lunars to favour any style based on an animal that they have the form for. Or just all animal styles. And not favour any other MAs.<br /> But I doubt that anyone else will want that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well why not let the Changing Moon choose ? <br /> I don't have the problem if a Lunar most choose beteween MA or Sorc even <br /> Can get one but not both, as long as the option exist","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T08:09:16-07:00","id":1222900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222851#post1222851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a Lunar that want to do MA or Sorc will fall behind in XP in those areas</div> </div> </div> </div>But they'll still end up with the powers that the want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there is always a second person that dig in to Sorcery or MA and suddenly you might have a Lunar sorc with a sid or solar sorc, and if the Lunar and the Solar/sid pour same amount of xp in sorc the Lunar will fall behind fast, because it isn't only 2xp, that can quickly become 10-20xp in a game,</div> </div> </div> </div>Are these other players set on purchasing the exact same Martial Arts and spells that the Lunar player is?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T08:31:43-07:00","id":1222905,"title":"","content":"Maybe an additional merit to favor MA? Costed so that at chargen it would still break even, but long run it would be a cost saving?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T09:31:32-07:00","id":1222921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222900#post1222900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they'll still end up with the powers that the want.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Are these other players set on purchasing the exact same Martial Arts and spells that the Lunar player is?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they still end up with the power then let them favor since if the charms are very powerfull with MA or Sorcery they will still be. all you are doing is making the game less fun<br /> <br /> Is it fun seeing that you have to invest more than other players that choose to do MA or Sorcery? knowing that your investment is gonna cost you more in the long run compared to others<br /> <br /> It wasn't fun in 2e and it is never fun in any game, knowing that there will be xp disparity <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T09:34:03-07:00","id":1222925,"title":"","content":"I cannot conceive of the mindset that is so fixated on the accounting side of things, or assesses such in terms of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T09:38:44-07:00","id":1222929,"title":"","content":"Different in strength in game shouldn't create disparity OOC Resources","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13712,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","user":"Illaden","date":".  the quotes was taken away 05-29-2018, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T10:14:38-07:00","id":1222935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222851#post1222851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly can't see the problem with Lunars being able to favor MA or Sorc, and same goes with other attribute exalted<br /> If it was too strong with favored it would still be too strong unfavored still, XP doesn't make a combination of charms and spells weaker.<br /> All this does in a mixed splat game with 4-5 people is that a Lunar that want to do MA or Sorc will fall behind in XP in those areas, And there is always a second person that dig in to Sorcery or MA and suddenly you might have a Lunar sorc with a sid or solar sorc, and if the Lunar and the Solar/sid pour same amount of xp in sorc the Lunar will fall behind fast, because it isn't only 2xp, that can quickly become 10-20xp in a game,<br /> And beliving that you always will get flat +4 lunar xp is very optimistic, since we can also asume that the others will have flat +4 and then the lunar will fall behind in splat xp<br /> If the argument is &quot;I have seen Solar taking Evocation for unfavored&quot; than I have to remind you that non can favor evocation and most(not deebs) will be on equal foting there</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that this is nonesense.<br /> <br /> It's not the martial arts ability that's potentially unbalanced with attribute charms. It's MA <i>charms</i> that are potentially unbalanced with them. For every 4 charms that a lunar could buy in MA, an exalt with MA favored can buy 5. <br /> <br /> There has to be a meaningful choice between buying MA charms and buying native charms. If MA charm+ attribute charm combos is so powerful then you must restrict it somehow or it becomes the 'one true build' for lunars.<br /> <br /> There are several ways to restrict them: Drop lunars down to terrestrial level for MA, nerf native charms to such an extent that they're not very effective with or without MA charms, Make attribute charms incompatible with MA charms (except excellency), or restrict progression in MA charms either by preventing them from favoring them or increasing the cost by 2 xp for all MA charms and then letting them favor or not.<br /> <br /> Choose at least one option. <br /> <br /> Otherwise you're gonna end up with charm synergies that'll bypass solar or sidereal level of competency in MA, even without the mastery keyword. At least, if the lunar charmset is as awesome as as we're all hoping it to be, that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T10:20:47-07:00","id":1222939,"title":"","content":"I'm an assumed optimizer/minmaxer and I don't care.<br /> <br /> I don't think all splats should be equal, and if something in Lunars justifies them having a bit of a harder time being Sorcerers or Martial Artists, that's fine.<br /> <br /> Lunars will probably have access to Merits at discounted or for free through Shapeshifting and Totem Spirit (or whatever it's called).<br /> <br /> I'm not gonna complain, even if I want to play a mutant Solar, are you? If not, why not? Cost disparity is not fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T11:27:11-07:00","id":1222950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222935#post1222935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that this is nonesense.<br /> <br /> It's not the martial arts ability that's potentially unbalanced with attribute charms. It's MA <i>charms</i> that are potentially unbalanced with them. For every 4 charms that a lunar could buy in MA, an exalt with MA favored can buy 5.<br /> <br /> There has to be a meaningful choice between buying MA charms and buying native charms. If MA charm+ attribute charm combos is so powerful then you must restrict it somehow or it becomes the 'one true build' for lunars.<br /> <br /> There are several ways to restrict them: Drop lunars down to terrestrial level for MA, nerf native charms to such an extent that they're not very effective with or without MA charms, Make attribute charms incompatible with MA charms (except excellency), or restrict progression in MA charms either by preventing them from favoring them or increasing the cost by 2 xp for all MA charms and then letting them favor or not.<br /> <br /> Choose at least one option.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you're gonna end up with charm synergies that'll bypass solar or sidereal level of competency in MA, even without the mastery keyword. At least, if the lunar charmset is as awesome as as we're all hoping it to be, that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was then having old splat cost to charms even wouldn't be a problem right? <br /> <br /> If charm x and spell y has a too powerful effect, no matter the xp cost it will still have the same powerful effect, all you are doing is creating a disparity with experience were the lunar has less good stuff comapared to others that can favor MA or Sorcer and lessening the fun for the one that ones to play a Lunar with those combination<br /> <br /> And having XP be a meassurement of how strong an exalted is, is just ridicoulos and I point again towards the old splatcost if we are going to use xp as a measurement of the strength of an Exalted power <br /> <br /> Yes there has to be meaningful choices between Martial art and Native charms and one of those are, Shapeshifting since you can't do MA while shapeshift <br /> So choosing MA for combat, you are not going to be effective in combat in an animal form compared to the one that chose to specialise in Shapeshift<br /> <br /> It just creates an optimization way at chargen were you choose as many MA charms just to save as much xp as possible in the long run, the same goes with spell <br /> Having the option to get a discount feels much better than not having it as a player","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T12:11:26-07:00","id":1222961,"title":"","content":"Do you find yourself buying up as many evocations as possible at chargen? This is no different. <br /> <br /> Especially since lunars can use ma with native charms. For lunars, martial arts are essentially evocations of the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T12:34:27-07:00","id":1222969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222950#post1222950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If charm x and spell y has a too powerful effect, no matter the xp cost it will still have the same powerful effect, all you are doing is creating a disparity with experience were the lunar has less good stuff comapared to others that can favor MA or Sorcer and lessening the fun for the one that ones to play a Lunar with those combination</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the charm synergy is going to be offset by the other guy having additional charms.<br /> <br /> Do I want more lunar charms or do I want to get a MA and have really good synergy with that? <br /> <br /> The alternative is to make it so that lunar charm don't with with MA at all. Would you prefer that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T12:43:58-07:00","id":1222971,"title":"","content":"Evocation doesn't have a discount to start with and almost everyone is on equal footing there <br /> <br /> Is it fun knowing that you will be charms/ma/spells behind since you didn't even have the option to get the discount? <br /> It has never been fun with disparity of experience <br /> <br /> The argument for them not having favored MA or Sorcery atm is that their native charms is strong with those two. Guess what They still are, Only difference is that the Lunar player just have to wait longer for fun stuff compared to others, that still will pull ahead and get their fun stuff faster. That isn't fun. <br /> <br /> The arguments you have presented haven't even been presented by the devs even so whatever I chose from them, they are going to be an argument trap honestly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T14:17:25-07:00","id":1223004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222971#post1222971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The argument for them not having favored MA or Sorcery atm is that their native charms is strong with those two. Guess what They still are, Only difference is that the Lunar player just have to wait longer for fun stuff compared to others, that still will pull ahead and get their fun stuff faster. That isn't fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>No matter how many times you assert this it doesn't make it true.<br /> <br /> Let me put it this way: <br /> <br /> The Devs are endeavoring to provide a play experience where a character with all native lunar charms and a character who dabbles in MA have roughly the same effective build. <br /> <br /> Since we've got a divide of regular xp and lunar xp, there is a limit to how much any given lunar can take lunar charms. The player must choose between several options to spend their lunar xp on. They can go stat heavy and boost up their attributes, abilities etc. Or they can go sorcery, evocations or MA if they want more charm effects.<br /> <br /> As you pointed out, being attribute based gives them no special advantage with sorcery or evocations. I'm kinda expecting lunars to get favored sorcery in the end but the jury is still out on that apparently. (plus DB get an extra surcharge on evocations <i>precisely</i> because otherwise they'd be a one-true-build scenario for DB characters)<br /> <br /> However, it <i>does</i> give them a special advantage with MA.<br /> <br /> Lunars can combo native charms with MA. Solars cannot. Sidereals cannot. DB cannot. <br /> <br /> So the devs have to do something to avoid a OTB scenario with lunar MA just like they have to avoid it with DB evocations. This is no different. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222971#post1222971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The arguments you have presented haven't even been presented by the devs even so whatever I chose from them, they are going to be an argument trap honestly</div> </div> </div> </div>Look<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023?p=1222743\"> here </a> for a good response to this.<br /> <br /> The options I came up with are fairly obvious ideas for balancing out MA synergy against native charms. <br /> <br /> Seriously, if you can actually come up with a suggestion to balance out Lunar charms with MA that wasn't on my list, please present it here. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The fundamental difference here is that in 2E it wasn't a balancing factor of a lunar choosing a lunar charm vs MA charm it was &quot;Lunars can't be as good as solars in anything and therefore we're going to make their character progression WAY slower AND we'll make individual charms less powerful.&quot; They did it to DB in 2E as well. From everything the Devs have said and from what we've seen in WFhW they're not planning on nerfing anybody or screwing them over with slower character progression this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T14:21:21-07:00","id":1223008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222971#post1222971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it fun knowing that you will be charms/ma/spells behind since you didn't even have the option to get the discount?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt probably helps to not fixate on something as ephemeral as whether or not everybody has the same number of Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illadan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The argument for them not having favored MA or Sorcery atm is that their native charms is strong with those two. Guess what They still are, Only difference is that the Lunar player just have to wait longer for fun stuff compared to others, that still will pull ahead and get their fun stuff faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that experience costs such as this are predicated on the idea that it being slightly harder to build up excessively powerful combinations alternately creates an incentive to focus one's character building elsewhere, or creates a delay that allows a smaller number of powers that produce power proportionate to somebody else's larger number of Charms that are less powerful or create less powerful combinations, so that they functionally remain on an equal footing even if that emerges from different numbers of powers.<br /> <br /> \u200bThink about it; you're granting the possibility of powerful combinations, so the question becomes one of whether or not the Lunar player is able to build those combinations at a fast enough rate that they actually pull ahead of other players that have spent an equal quantity of experience points (or have otherwise all been playing for the same length of time).<br /> <br /> What you're saying with &quot;it doesn't make a difference if it's too powerful, because it's still going to be too powerful when you finally do reach it&quot;...<br /> <br /> \u200bImagine if Solar Circle Sorcery was available at Essence 1 through Supernal Occult. In a certain sense, it actually <i>is</i> more powerful at the earlier stage then it would be by the time that it is possible to buy it, in the sense of how much the chronicle has developed, how far-reaching characters are in the early stories, and how one player is measured against all of the others. Solar Circle would be a lot easier to get early than many other Essence 5 powers, since it only has two prerequisites. Think about what that would mean at character creation; three Charms and one spell, not even a third of your starting power suite, and now you can summon Ligier from the word go. Sure, Ligier is going to be just as powerful by the time you get to him, but there's such a thing as narrative progression and an escalation curve.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat, by the way, is the manner in which I assess experience costs; it's not a measure of value, it's a pacing method.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for Lunars, I feel as though, if they're unable to get favoured costs for Martial Arts and sorcery, that's a necessary offset for how Attribute Charms work. Lunars are probably going to still have about as many Charms as the Dragon Blooded at the very least, but they're divided between 9 Attributes rather than 25 Abilities. No matter what way they slice it, every dot of an Attribute opens the door to about three times as many Charms as a dot of an Ability does for Solars and Terrestrials. Come to think of it, I think my prior query about a given Lunar having access to a large and diverse arsenal might still hold true, just that rather than being based on the Charms being cheaper, it would come from it being a lot easier for Charms to be the only thing that they need to worry about spending XP on. They're going to be able to get discounted costs on the dots and Charms of four out of nine of those Attributes. I think that there may be a few ways in which the numbers there put Lunars at a slight advantage, even if the costs of individual Charms aren't easier.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think that would be necessarily offset by that not including Martial Arts and spells in the range of things that one can get at a slightly faster rate.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere are alternating arguments between &quot;it doesn't need to be especially un-fun either&quot; and &quot;consider the possibility that getting your way would make things less fun for all of the players besides the Lunar&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T17:44:08-07:00","id":1223075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223008#post1223008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIt probably helps to not fixate on something as ephemeral as whether or not everybody has the same number of Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed; one game I ran, the other players had built all the way to Essence 3 before I introduced a new player at Essence 1, and plenty of fun was had by all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T19:41:55-07:00","id":1223091,"title":"","content":"I'm going to just indulge for a bit and reiterate what I'd like to see in this book:<br /> <br /> <b>Animals:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Thunder Lizard (brontosaurus)<br /> 2) Terror Wing (pterodactyl)<br /> 3) Giant Octopus/Squid<br /> 5) Whale<br /> 6) Dolphin<br /> 7) Seagull<br /> 8) Snake<br /> <br /> <b>Martial Arts:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Monkey Style (&quot;celestial&quot; or otherwise)<br /> 2) Hammer Style<br /> 3) Axe Style<br /> 4) Lightning Hoof Style<br /> <br /> <b>Artifacts:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Lightning Torment Hatchets<br /> 2) Gauntlets of Distant Claws<br /> 3) Death at the Root<br /> 4) Scabbard of the Living Weapon<br /> 5) A 5-dot cauldron which allows a Lunar to brew magical potions and ointments that retain their potency only as long as the Lunar commits the motes but which allows the user to bestow blessings on others through Evocations that Exalted Charms generally can't provide, and serves as a sorcerous means for works of empowerment<br /> 6) Circe's sorcerous shepherd's-crook staff of transforming dudes into animals and bewitching their minds<br /> 7) A shapeshifting robe that becomes any set of clothing you need for any social context or disguise<br /> 8) The Bellerophon reins of Servant Rider (Medusa) from the Fate/Stay Night franchise; bridle, control, and enrage any beast for battle<br /> 9) Armor that fuses with you and transforms you to mimic the spell Incomparable Body Armor<br /> 10) Venom symbiote living armor<br /> <br /> <b>Sorcerous Initiations:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Song-casting, spell-singing<br /> 2) Seasonal cycles, day/night cycles, lunar cycles, cooperation from two assistants in different stages of life than you (maiden, mother, crone / son, father, grandfather)<br /> 3) In the vein of &quot;Pact with an Ifrit Lord&quot;, &quot;Mentored by a Forge-God&quot;, because maybe I'd like to play <i>League of Legends'</i> Ornn as a Mountain Goat Lunar, and I imagine plenty of Solar players would appreciate an initiation that helps with crafting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-29-2018, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T05:46:22-07:00","id":1223180,"title":"","content":"A lot of those are things I'd like to see as well, but\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223091#post1223091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seagull</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not just reskin the Raiton? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223091#post1223091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snake</div> </div> </div> </div>Snakes are in the Core already. Or do you mean, like, constrictors?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223091#post1223091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hammer Style, Axe Style</div> </div> </div> </div>As in, styles that can be practiced with hammers or axes respectively? Just checking that I didn't miss some homebrew you're referencing or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223091#post1223091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death at the Root</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather wait until they hammered out all the rules for manses before they wrote up an axe specifically designed for fucking with manses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223091#post1223091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scabbard of the Living Weapon</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with the requirement of a whole separate artifact weapon you have to sheathe in it for the Scabbard to be effective, its effect is way too potent as-is. Being outright immune to combat from mortals is something that the current system has been trying to <i>avoid</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223091#post1223091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Armor that fuses with you and transforms you to mimic the spell Incomparable Body Armor</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be fun, but kinda steps on Unity's toes, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223091#post1223091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Venom symbiote living armor</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be fun, but kinda steps on perronele's toes, doesn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-30-2018, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T05:54:54-07:00","id":1223183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222875#post1222875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Dragonblood, that's true, though I don't think it is for Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Solars its not necessarily productive to view it as a 1-1 comparison to their native charms but the other things they can buy with Solar xp. The evocations on your daiklave stack with your investment in Solar Melee while your Martial Arts or Sorcery is mostly an alternative to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","user":"Bastet","date":". 05-30-2018, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:08:20-07:00","id":1223187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223180#post1223180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just reskin the Raiton?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I named the wrong species, but I was hoping for a bird that might have special merits for diving below water to swim after its prey, and definitely also special merits for flying long distances over water. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Snakes are in the Core already. Or do you mean, like, constrictors? </div> </div> </div>Must have missed the snake when I paged through, but having stats for giant constricting snakes would be cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As in, styles that can be practiced with hammers or axes respectively? Just checking that I didn't miss some homebrew you're referencing or something. </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve tried to homebrew such Styles, but no, I\u2019m hoping for new, official, professionally designed Styles that really let someone play up \u201cbig-muscled barbarian with a two-handed Kill Stick of chopping and smashing.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd rather wait until they hammered out all the rules for manses before they wrote up an axe specifically designed for fucking with manses. </div> </div> </div>It also breaks spells and sorcerous workings. But fair enough. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hopefully implemented better this time around. </div> </div> </div>I love Evocations!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could be fun, but kinda steps on Unity's toes, doesn't it? </div> </div> </div>Unity changes weight classes, but Incomparable Body Arsenal is always super-heavy and perhaps not compatible with flying (definitely not with swimming). Unity keys off of your Intimacies, and IBA lets you not breathe. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could be fun, but kinda steps on perronele's toes, doesn't it? </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know about those demons, and what little I knew didn\u2019t sound like Venom.<br /> <br /> Also, what\u2019s wrong with stepping on toes? Wasn\u2019t there a thread recently about how overlap was okay with magical materials?<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also artifacts that do what Charms do; does that cape of flying wings step on the toes of Eagle Wing Style or turning into a bird? Maybe an artifact Venom armor could have synergy with the cooperation of a demon Venom armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:33:54-07:00","id":1223196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223180#post1223180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could be fun, but kinda steps on Unity's toes, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> Could be fun, but kinda steps on perronele's toes, doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Artifacts have no toes!<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd I don't just mean that as a flippant comment on pieces of metal; I find the specificity of Artifact personalities and the Evocations that they produce to be so finely calibrated that one can make innumerable variations on any given single line pitch. Like when we were talking about moonsilver warstriders, and collectively came up with multiple paths for the basic idea of a stalker-hunter moonstrider.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnyway, it may just be because I was recently watching a documentary on Australian wildlife, but it would be interesting to see stats or a Lunar for a marsupial or egg-laying mammal. It would also fulfil the writer statement of it being worthwhile for having things around Lunars with some of the less obvious and aspirational animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:39:42-07:00","id":1223200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222875#post1222875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their Moonsilver evocations are, I assume, balanced against Solar charms, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you assume that? Lunar Exalted shouldn\u2019t have Solar-level Charms.<br /> <br /> Only orichalcum Resonant effects would be equal to Solar Charms, whereas moonsilver Resonant effects only need to be equal to Lunar Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:47:53-07:00","id":1223207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1222875#post1222875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be for Lunars though. Their Moonsilver evocations are, I assume, balanced against Solar charms, after all..</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure what you mean by that, Evocations are generally weaker than Solar Charms (at least where impact can be directly measured in simple mechanics terms) - those that are on par with the Solar Power tier get gates behind Solar Charms (or presumably Abyssal or Infernal Charms in the future).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:52:38-07:00","id":1223212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223200#post1223200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you assume that? Lunar Exalted shouldn\u2019t have Solar-level Charms.<br /> <br /> Only orichalcum Resonant effects would be equal to Solar Charms, whereas moonsilver Resonant effects only need to be equal to Lunar Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Alchemicals are going to ruin differentiating resonance power levels like that. Resonant powers deal more with theme than power level. If you need to gate off an evocation so someone less powerful than a Solar can\u2019t wield it, use a Charm prerequisite, because Orichalcum Alchemicals are going to be able to get resonant Orichalcum effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:41:03-07:00","id":1223238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223187#post1223187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I named the wrong species, but I was hoping for a bird that might have special merits for diving below water to swim after its prey, and definitely also special merits for flying long distances over water.</div> </div> </div> </div>These both seem like minor tweaks to an already-workable set of stats. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223187#post1223187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve tried to homebrew such Styles, but no, I\u2019m hoping for new, official, professionally designed Styles that really let someone play up \u201cbig-muscled barbarian with a two-handed Kill Stick of chopping and smashing.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there any discrete techniques unique to said muscle-guys that would serve to differentiate it from Melee? Like, don't get me wrong, an axe-compatible style seems pretty nifty, but, in the words of a pretty smart guy\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1211797-first-pulse-style-lunar-or-infernal-book?p=1211955#post1211955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about those street-rat orphan fighters and said to myself, \u201cDoes it really make sense that you\u2019d represent their combat skill with a Martial Arts Ability rather than Brawl?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223187#post1223187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Evocations!</div> </div> </div> </div>Me, too. And we've got some good devs on hand. But I just worry, y'know? &quot;Be careful what you wish for,&quot; and whatnot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223187#post1223187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know about those demons, and what little I knew didn\u2019t sound like Venom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly the symbiote can do stuff like scary shapeshifting, creating weapons, reproducing, and has a vulnerability to fire\u2026 but both are amorphous critters that flow over you like a second skin to protect you in combat, augment your ability to sense danger, and play off your darker impulses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223187#post1223187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what\u2019s wrong with stepping on toes? Wasn\u2019t there a thread recently about how overlap was okay with magical materials?</div> </div> </div> </div>My concern isn't so much about overlap damaging themes so much as, well, we're only going to get a finite amount of Exalted <i>stuff</i>. I'd rather see new things where we can, rather than retread the same things over and over again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:43:24-07:00","id":1223240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223212#post1223212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Alchemicals are going to ruin differentiating resonance power levels like that. Resonant powers deal more with theme than power level. If you need to gate off an evocation so someone less powerful than a Solar can\u2019t wield it, use a Charm prerequisite, because Orichalcum Alchemicals are going to be able to get resonant Orichalcum effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be mistaken, but I believe Vance himself said that resonance also serves as a way to control who has access to what effect. So if something is Orichalcum resonant, it is a pretty surefire way to guarantee that only Solars have access to it, and therefore create something on a Solar power level.<br /> <br /> Also what Bastet said. Evocations are expensive, even for Solars, probably because of their complementary nature.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:45:53-07:00","id":1223241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223212#post1223212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orichalcum Alchemicals are going to be able to get resonant Orichalcum effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you know that? Was this confirmed anywhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:45:57-07:00","id":1223242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223200#post1223200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you assume that? Lunar Exalted shouldn\u2019t have Solar-level Charms.<br /> <br /> Only orichalcum Resonant effects would be equal to Solar Charms, whereas moonsilver Resonant effects only need to be equal to Lunar Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I believe the balance of having solar level charms is simply gating them behind solar charms.<br /> <br /> Solars are equally resonant with moonsilver and orichalcum. They could conceivably get solar level effects out of both. Just name solar charms as re-requisites and BAM! solar level evocations that are not accessible by others. It's how they did jade artifacts as well.<br /> <br /> Presumably for every evocation gated by a solar charm there would be a similar-but-different evocation gated behind other resonant user's native charms. Aura charms for DB, or shapeshifting charms for lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:48:27-07:00","id":1223243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223241#post1223241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you know that? Was this confirmed anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>When homebrewing alchemicals my ST and I went with each alchemical caste being resonant with their own material and nuetral with others then they could take charms to gain resonance with different materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:55:12-07:00","id":1223247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223241#post1223241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you know that? Was this confirmed anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>I BELIEVE the devs have said the current plan, that\u2019s subject to change, is that that Alchemicals will be resonant with their caste-material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:59:15-07:00","id":1223249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1215268#post1215268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. [The First Age Castes are] all dead a millennium, and should be left dead, especially as it suggests modern Lunars are broken and a patch job.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just my headcanon, but the Casteless always bug me with being remade into the new Castes / transitioning through the new Castes. Isn't the point that they are without a fixed Caste or any remake intervention? So, the First Age Castes being alive an well, and transitioned through by the Casteless, is my preferred way of dealing with them, which brings these Castes, in transitory form, into the Time of Turmoil.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:00:22-07:00","id":1223250,"title":"","content":"Gotta admit, I can't help but think about the concept of them <i>not</i> resonating with the material they are <i>literally made of</i> and go &quot;how would that even work?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:00:29-07:00","id":1223251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223240#post1223240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might be mistaken, but I believe Vance himself said that resonance also serves as a way to control who has access to what effect. So if something is Orichalcum resonant, it is a pretty surefire way to guarantee that only Solars have access to it, and therefore create something on a Solar power level.<br /> <br /> Also what Bastet said. Evocations are expensive, even for Solars, probably because of their complementary nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resonance controls who has access to it yes. But that has more to do with theme than power level. Solars are not necessarily going to always be alone in being resonant with Orichalcum (Orichalcum Caste Alchemicals being the most likely to join them, in addition to Infernals).<br /> <br /> Charm gating is how you deal with effects that would be unbalanced Power wise if anyone else got them. Note that that isn\u2019t reserved for Orichalcum either - Solar Charm gating lets you add more powerful evocations to a Moonsilver Artifact without giving Lunars access to it, or Jade without giving Dragon Blooded access to it, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:14:12-07:00","id":1223260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223249#post1223249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is just my headcanon, but the Casteless always bug me with being remade into the new Castes / transitioning through the new Castes.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere are Casteless Lunars in the First Age as well. In all Editions, Lunars have always worked by gaining Castes some time after they Exalt; First Edition even said this was done with special initiation rituals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:20:08-07:00","id":1223263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223251#post1223251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Resonance controls who has access to it yes. But that has more to do with theme than power level. Solars are not necessarily going to always be alone in being resonant with Orichalcum (Orichalcum Caste Alchemicals being the most likely to join them, in addition to Infernals).<br /> <br /> Charm gating is how you deal with effects that would be unbalanced Power wise if anyone else got them. Note that that isn\u2019t reserved for Orichalcum either - Solar Charm gating lets you add more powerful evocations to a Moonsilver Artifact without giving Lunars access to it, or Jade without giving Dragon Blooded access to it, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm only saying what I recall, and like I said I might be mistaken, Vance saying.<br /> <br /> I agree that Charm Gating is much more effective, but also very rigid and exclusionary.<br /> <br /> If I want to make an Evocation available to anyone, but also want an additional effect for people that are resonant with the material, and if that material is Orichalcum, I can safely make that Solar level with the assumption that within RAW only Solars will access it.<br /> <br /> I might be wrong, but I doubt any consideration is given to Alchemical MM Resonance while designing Artifacts right now, they are many years down the line, I just don't see the thought burden being compensating for whatever it is that will only happen half a decade from now, if at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:44:22-07:00","id":1223271,"title":"","content":"I don't believe there's any intention to make any magical material resonance effects' more potent than others, at least far as they can be reduced to raw mechanics (certainly some materials are given to more showy effects than others) - a Solar wielding Jade is not meant to be cheating themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:50:21-07:00","id":1223275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223207#post1223207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m not sure what you mean by that, Evocations are generally weaker than Solar Charms (at least where impact can be directly measured in simple mechanics terms)</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they? Are the charms (for a Resonant user) of Unity, Flying Silver Dream, the Tusk of Galeach-Ma, Frost-Thorn Knuckles and the Wings of the Raptor weaker than Solar charms?* I'm not asking that Socratically, I'm genuinely not sure, I find it difficult to judge.<br /> <br /> *I'd mention Karvara, but that's an N/A artefact so probably isn't comparable to Solar charms.<br /> <br /> (Anyway, Sunder the Gold, that was why I assumed that. I assumed Moonsilver evocations are as powerful as Orichalcum evocations which are as powerful as Solar charms. I could be wrong. As I said, I find it difficult to judge.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:50:36-07:00","id":1223276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223271#post1223271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe there's any intention to make any magical material resonance effects' more potent than others, at least far as they can be reduced to raw mechanics (certainly some materials are given to more showy effects than others) - a Solar wielding Jade is not meant to be cheating themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>And neither is having Jade Artifacts supposed to be OTB for DBs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:54:16-07:00","id":1223279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223249#post1223249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is just my headcanon, but the Casteless always bug me with being remade into the new Castes / transitioning through the new Castes. Isn't the point that they are without a fixed Caste or any remake intervention? So, the First Age Castes being alive an well, and transitioned through by the Casteless, is my preferred way of dealing with them, which brings these Castes, in transitory form, into the Time of Turmoil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point with 3rd ed is that the Lunars evolved their entire exaltation. So the very inherent castes it can develop have changed.<br /> <br /> And I suspect that their first Age exaltations might have been so radically different that the old castes might not make sense for the current exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:55:20-07:00","id":1223281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223276#post1223276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And neither is having Jade Artifacts supposed to be OTB for DBs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think that's why they ended up having to pay more XP for them than Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T09:09:52-07:00","id":1223286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223275#post1223275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they? Are the charms (for a Resonant user) of Unity, Flying Silver Dream, the Tusk of Galeach-Ma, Frost-Thorn Knuckles and the Wings of the Raptor weaker than Solar charms?* I'm not asking that Socratically, I'm genuinely not sure, I find it difficult to judge.<br /> <br /> *I'd mention Karvara, but that's an N/A artefact so probably isn't comparable to Solar charms.<br /> <br /> (Anyway, Sunder the Gold, that was why I assumed that. I assumed Moonsilver evocations are as powerful as Orichalcum evocations which are as powerful as Solar charms. I could be wrong. As I said, I find it difficult to judge.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As per Vance - equal essence Lunar kaiju vs. Dragon-Blooded in a Resonant Warstrider, the Lunar has the advantage (though not an unbeatable one) because Celestial Exalted Charms are more powerful than <i>warstrider</i> Evocations.<br /> <br /> Remember Charms need to be judged as part of an interacting whole, not stand alone one-to-one comparisons in 3E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T09:37:14-07:00","id":1223296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223212#post1223212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Alchemicals are going to ruin differentiating resonance power levels like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an assumption based on no evidence.<br /> <br /> The Alchemical Exalted could easily lack full resonance with any material, having only neutrality with everything. Owing to the mix of materials used to create them in the first place, and the fact that they lack the power and skill of Solar Exalted, which is the reason why they fully resonate with everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T10:17:30-07:00","id":1223312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223238#post1223238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These both seem like minor tweaks to an already-workable set of stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe so.<br /> <br /> I could see the QC stats chapter having a bunch of sample merits like the Magical Merit examples in the core, to help tweak existing creatures. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there any discrete techniques unique to said muscle-guys that would serve to differentiate it from Melee? </div> </div> </div>Did Single Point and White Reaper serve to differentiate themselves from Melee?<br /> <br /> A boxing Style could try to differentiate itself from Brawl through its self-discipline and restricted tactics, but First Pulse\u2019s character was all about rejecting discipline and restricted tactics.<br /> <br /> Like Terrible Ascent Driven Beast Style, First Pulse only made sense in Second Edition, where Brawl was a Martial Art, Terrestrial Styles existed separate from Celestial ones, and Dragon-Blooded paid mote surcharges for anything out of Aspect. They were just ways to let Wood and Air Aspects Brawl like Water Aspects could with Terrestrial Hero Style.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> both are amorphous critters that flow over you like a second skin to protect you in combat, augment your ability to sense danger, and play off your darker impulses. </div> </div> </div>Maybe Exalted hosts can learn Evocations when wearing them, this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T10:26:47-07:00","id":1223313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223281#post1223281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think that's why they ended up having to pay more XP for them than Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there is a single reason for the cost disparity, I believe it is a combination of factors, and trying to point to one single thing that justifies it is an exercise in futility.<br /> <br /> Only the Devs can say for sure and clarify something in a manner that is not just speculation and ego-driven discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T10:30:41-07:00","id":1223315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223250#post1223250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta admit, I can't help but think about the concept of them <i>not</i> resonating with the material they are <i>literally made of</i> and go &amp;quot;how would that even work?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re actually mostly of clay.<br /> <br /> Also, by your logic, a Fire Aspect would be merely neutral with any jade but red jade.<br /> <br /> Alchemical Exalted have a weird relationship with artifacts given that their very Charms are artifacts. An Orichalcum Caste Alchemical has the easiest time acquiring Charms which evoke the themes of orichalcum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T10:49:05-07:00","id":1223322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223315#post1223315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They\u2019re actually mostly of clay.<br /> <br /> Also, by your logic, a Fire Aspect would be merely neutral with any jade but red jade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon Bloods are not made of jade<br /> <br /> the 'logic' that you imply here would only be consistent if there was a red jade caste alchemical or a black jade caste alchemical. Each color of jade is similar enough that encompassing all of them into a single group makes sense.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223315#post1223315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemical Exalted have a weird relationship with artifacts given that their very Charms are artifacts. An Orichalcum Caste Alchemical has the easiest time acquiring Charms which evoke the themes of orichalcum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemicals are an amalgamation of special clays, a heroic soul and one of the magical materials.<br /> <br /> The magical materials are not just an aesthetic difference between castes as you imply here, they are an irreducible part of each caste of alchemical.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that alchemcils in 2E were the only exalts on a solar level for craft and artifact production. <br /> <br /> It simply doesn't make sense to say that the exalted most associated with the MM and artifacts wouldn't resonate with any of them. In fact if I were a betting man, I would place money on the idea that alchemicals alone out of all exalt types will have favored costs to purchase <i>evocations</i><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T11:24:05-07:00","id":1223335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223286#post1223286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per Vance - equal essence Lunar kaiju vs. Dragon-Blooded in a Resonant Warstrider, the Lunar has the advantage (though not an unbeatable one) because Celestial Exalted Charms are more powerful than <i>warstrider</i> Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's necessarily a case of being more powerful, but of how well suited one is to fighting something that exists on that scale.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor instance, I doubt that a kaiju Lunar will have a power equivalent to the capstone power of Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation in its scope and widespread destructive potential, even if they're very good at tearing the Cathedral apart.<br /> <br /> \u200bSee also how a Solar that is high into Melee Charms likely has a fighting advantage against somebody that is similarly invested in Lore or Adamant sorcery, even though those people have a lot more destructive potential.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis is why we've had developers trying to expound on how limiting it is to frame all of these things in terms of relative power.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T12:15:52-07:00","id":1223349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223313#post1223313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think there is a single reason for the cost disparity, I believe it is a combination of factors, and trying to point to one single thing that justifies it is an exercise in futility.<br /> <br /> Only the Devs can say for sure and clarify something in a manner that is not just speculation and ego-driven discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said that because, IIRC, Vance said that they made spells and evocations more expensive for Dragonblood because they're better than Dragonblood charms and so if they didn't, DB players would want to just get lots of spells and evocations rather than take their actual charms.<br /> Which makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T12:41:59-07:00","id":1223356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223349#post1223349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said that because, IIRC, Vance said that they made spells and evocations more expensive for Dragonblood because they're better than Dragonblood charms and so if they didn't, DB players would want to just get lots of spells and evocations rather than take their actual charms.<br /> Which makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah ok! Must have missed that. So it is clear then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T12:50:25-07:00","id":1223360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223296#post1223296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is an assumption based on no evidence.<br /> <br /> The Alchemical Exalted could easily lack full resonance with any material, having only neutrality with everything. Owing to the mix of materials used to create them in the first place, and the fact that they lack the power and skill of Solar Exalted, which is the reason why they fully resonate with everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without evidence. It\u2019s subject to change, but I believe devs have confirmed the current assumption until they actually get to writing them and playtesting is they\u2019ll be resonant with their Caste material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T13:51:43-07:00","id":1223386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223312#post1223312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Single Point and White Reaper serve to differentiate themselves from Melee?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't being coy, Sunder - give me some examples of ways your hypothetical Axe Style Barbarian Guy <i>fights</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T14:09:37-07:00","id":1223392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223312#post1223312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Did Single Point and White Reaper serve to differentiate themselves from Melee?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they both have very distinct styles beyond what weapon they use and do things that Melee Charms don't have covered on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T14:12:26-07:00","id":1223393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223386#post1223386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't being coy, Sunder - give me some examples of ways your hypothetical Axe Style Barbarian Guy <i>fights</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you have asked the same thing of me if I asked for a non-elemental katana Style before Single Point was printed? Or a spear/scythe Style before White Reaper was printed?<br /> <br /> But my oldest concept for a two-handed hammer Style involved building and conserving circular momentum and harnessing the recoil of smashing someone with a blunt instrument in order to quickly rechamber and strike them again.<br /> <br /> The imagery would either be that of a swinging pendulum, or \u201cDevil Stars\u201d - comets whose circular paths out of the Wyld would lead them back into Creation every once in a while, where they would smash ordained stars from the sky and disrupt the paths of others before retreating back to the Wyld. <br /> <br /> An axe style might exploit how medium axes can be thrown, and dual-wielded. Perhaps it could extend the throwing tricks to work with heavy, two-hands axes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T14:20:12-07:00","id":1223398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223393#post1223393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you have asked the same thing of me if I asked for a non-elemental katana Style before Single Point was printed? Or a spear/scythe Style before White Reaper was printed?</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that like I wouldn't still ask for distinct techniques in a new katana or spear or scythe style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223393#post1223393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But my oldest concept for a two-handed hammer Style involved building and conserving circular momentum and harnessing the recoil of smashing someone with a blunt instrument in order to quickly rechamber and strike them again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, good. That's a lot more to work with than &quot;hammer style&quot; or &quot;barbarian.&quot; Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T14:30:58-07:00","id":1223401,"title":"","content":"Very Thor (10 characters)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T14:50:16-07:00","id":1223409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223398#post1223398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, good. That's a lot more to work with than &quot;hammer style&quot; or &quot;barbarian.&quot; Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The axe style might emulate tornadoes, deverishes, and whirlpools.<br /> <br /> A great sword Style would exploit the weapon\u2019s Balanced Overwhelming value, and draw inspiration from Monster Hunter\u2019s great sword style, executioner\u2019s swords, and Guts from Berserk, as well as the hyper-armor moves of the ultra-great swords From Software made in emulation of Guts. A mighty glacier Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T19:08:48-07:00","id":1223472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223286#post1223286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As per Vance - equal essence Lunar kaiju vs. Dragon-Blooded in a Resonant Warstrider, the Lunar has the advantage (though not an unbeatable one) because Celestial Exalted Charms are more powerful than <i>warstrider</i> Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking more about this statement, it occurs to me that it may also have been intended as a comment on how a Lunar compares to the kinds of Evocations that a Dragon Blood specifically would create, rather than across the board.<br /> <br /> \u200bApplying the principle of native Charm prerequisites being a good indicator for things that are too powerful to be balanced with other character... as an example, a Dragon Blood wielding All-Conquering Colossus probably can't use the capstone of throwing a large enemy into a manse or volcano several miles away to create a gigantic explosion, because that's at the end of a path that includes having Dragon Coil Technique.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the other hand, a Dragon Blood <i>can</i> still theoretically awaken Godsigh of Noonday Triumph; Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation only has one Evocation with a Solar Charm prerequisite, and none of the other Evocations branch off of that.<br /> <br /> \u200bMany of the other warstriders in Arms, even jade ones, have powers with Solar prerequisites, so it's a good bet that those are stronger than a Dragon Blood would manage; I suppose the Cathedral's armaments are acceptable through a combination of its premise being more on mastering built-in weapons than awakening mystical potential and how its destructive potential is more spread out than capable of being focused on single opponents. I couldn't say what a Dragon Blood wielding the likes of Crushing Spear of the Depths and Emerald Chevalier would be able to get out of them at higher Essence (and unfortunately we didn't get the stretch goal with which to get any hints), but I'd say that the distinction is worth considering before running off with any idea of Lunar or Solar Charms being stronger than the Evocations of a warstrider across the board.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T19:19:44-07:00","id":1223481,"title":"","content":"One of the things warstrider Evocations are supposed to be better at is &quot;scale&quot;. Warstrider Evocations are more often more effective against gigantic targets or large masses of targets than Exalted Charms.<br /> <br /> They are, after all, meant as weapons to fight giants and armies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T19:23:14-07:00","id":1223483,"title":"","content":"Certainly, my point from the beginning of this tangent has been that Evocations that are on par with Solar Charms get gated behind Solar charm prerequisites - as opposed to the idea that different material resonant effects are on different power levels: if that was the case, no Orichalcum Artifact would need to gage evocations behind Solar Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T19:28:58-07:00","id":1223484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223483#post1223483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly, my point from the beginning of this tangent has been that Evocations that are on par with Solar Charms get gated behind Solar charm prerequisites - as opposed to the idea that different material resonant effects are on different power levels: if that was the case, no Orichalcum Artifact would need to gage evocations behind Solar Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe we could take this line of conversation to a different thread? This is a thread about the Lunar book.<br /> <br /> What kind of animals you DO hope to see in the Lunar book?<br /> <br /> Or artifacts?<br /> <br /> Are there any particular canon Lunars you want to see depicted in the book? Such as characters you felt were botched in the past and might be better envisioned?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T19:52:36-07:00","id":1223489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223484#post1223484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any particular canon Lunars you want to see depicted in the book? Such as characters you felt were botched in the past and might be better envisioned?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'll be interested to see what might be done with Lilith. Particularly anything interesting that might be done around the idea of her having voluntarily spent several centuries as an owl.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I wouldn't want to disseminate that gimmick too widely, but it does make me wonder about the potential of Lunar characters to apply their particular situation and capabilities to bring them to some weird places.<br /> <br /> \u200bHeh, I actually wouldn't mind seeing... herself... the tiger Lunar used as an example of a failed and tiny Thousand Streams River project. Take the basics of her appearance and personality and location, and make her work in the new context. Possibly a bit more dignified, but not necessarily more successful; I don't think an example of somebody that is young with a war dominion that is a bit out of control would be out of place. Also, give her something better to wear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T05:24:24-07:00","id":1223583,"title":"","content":"If Ten Stripes is brought back I would prefer it not be her third outing as the ineffectual Lunar. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T05:54:29-07:00","id":1223587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223583#post1223583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Ten Stripes is brought back I would prefer it not be her third outing as the ineffectual Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yesss, I'm... genuinely not sure what I was thinking at the time...<br /> <br /> Third outing? Was she in First Edition? Now that I'm saying it, it sounds familiar, but I have no recollection of the details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T05:56:09-07:00","id":1223589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223583#post1223583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Ten Stripes is brought back I would prefer it not be her third outing as the ineffectual Lunar. </div> </div> </div> </div>Unless there is absolutely no place for a Lunar to be a screw-up, someone has to fulfill the role, and it might as well be the one who was always the screw-up.<br /> <br /> The difference ought to be the context in which she screws up.<br /> <br /> I would posit that what really bothers us about Ten Stripes is not how she screwed up in her social engineering efforts, but that social engineering as the Lunar \u201cthing\u201d was empty to begin with. It\u2019s not something that every Lunar should be expected to try, let alone succeed. <br /> <br /> Third Edition has moved into a good direction with this. Social engineering is not the Silver Pact\u2019s mission, but merely one of its tools or else a particular Lunar\u2019s hobby.<br /> <br /> Also, Ten Stripes seemed to fail at everything, even the things she should be good at. As a Full Moon, she died easily in single combat against a younger Alchemical. Who also happened to be the thoroughly unlikeable Autochthonian screw-up. (This screw-up was also Moonsilver Caste, as if the writer was deliberately pursuing a hateful theme.) I think the Alchemical even lost a later battle against a younger Dragon-Blood or Abyssal, just to rub more salt in the wound. <br /> <br /> Ten Stripes wasn\u2019t merely a joke. She was a mean and very unfunny joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T06:05:48-07:00","id":1223594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223489#post1223489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI'll be interested to see what might be done with Lilith. Particularly anything interesting that might be done around the idea of her having voluntarily spent several centuries as an owl.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, the word \u201cowl\u201d suggests an utterly unacceptable scale of existence. A Lunar should grow unbearably bored being an \u201cowl\u201d.<br /> <br /> If Lilith has spent centuries avoiding human form and even human thought, she still needs challenge and stimulation. She still has the strength of Luna\u2019s Chosen.<br /> <br /> She would be a demon-owl, a god-beast owl. A monster that hunts and devours other monsters and inspires fear and worship in any local human communities. <br /> <br /> She should be Godzilla in owl-form. Mothra with feathers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T06:17:48-07:00","id":1223599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223484#post1223484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of animals you DO hope to see in the Lunar book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Small, non-combat animals. Housecats, pet dogs, spiders, rabbits, small birds, etc. They haven't been done because a PC isn't going to fight them; but Lunars frequently turn into them (in my experience, more often than they turn into big dangerous animals; with my No Moon I was always turning into a spider or a small bird or a small cat, normally 2-3 times a session, whereas I'd turn into a bear or an Owlbear about once every 2-3 sessions).<br /> <br /> The rules may not need to be very complex, it depends on whether Lunars simply use the dice pool of the animal, or whichever dice pool is higher (if they use the higher one, then you don't need the Strength+Athletics of a rabbit because a Lunar's will be higher). And you may be able to see that all small animals have certain stats the same (like maybe all animals the size of a cat or smaller have Soak 1, and all insects have Soak 0). But some kind of guidance would be useful, even if it's not full stat-blocks (which may not be necessary, as I said).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, if Lunars can make their forms bigger, that may need some guidance in terms of stats. If I turn into a giant rabbit, is that based on a rabbit's stats with flat bonuses (like in 2nd ed)? Or does a giant form have set stats, but the merits of the animal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-31-2018, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T06:52:55-07:00","id":1223609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223594#post1223594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She would be a demon-owl, a god-beast owl. A monster that hunts and devours other monsters and inspires fear and worship in any local human communities.<br /> <br /> She should be Godzilla in owl-form. Mothra with feathers.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo what does a mouse Lunar do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T07:44:42-07:00","id":1223618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223609#post1223609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bSo what does a mouse Lunar do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t understand the question. A mouse Lunar does whatever a mouse Lunar wants. <br /> <br /> If they want to live as a beast as Lilith does, they burrow deep into the earth, or race across the fields, or dart across rivers. They prey upon anything smaller or slower than themselves as rodents do, instilling horror and fear in any witnesses. They are seen only when they wish to be seen, and people and monsters flee at the sight, in vein.<br /> <br /> Neither Lilith nor the mouse Lunar needs to assume larger-than-natural size, if I gave that unintended impression, though they likely will at some point.<br /> <br /> Or they could learn the body-splitting trick to hunt as a single swarm of owls or mice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T07:48:48-07:00","id":1223620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223609#post1223609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bSo what does a mouse Lunar do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously the mouse Lunar gets eaten by Lilith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T07:48:59-07:00","id":1223621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223599#post1223599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Small, non-combat animals. Housecats, pet dogs, spiders, rabbits, small birds, etc. They haven't been done</div> </div> </div> </div>Dogs and cats and small birds (raiton) are found in the core book. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you may be able to see that all small animals have certain stats the same (like maybe all animals the size of a cat or smaller have Soak 1, and all insects have Soak 0). But some kind of guidance would be useful, even if it's not full stat-blocks (which may not be necessary, as I said). </div> </div> </div>Guidance for tiny bug forms would be useful, yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if Lunars can make their forms bigger, that may need some guidance in terms of stats. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T08:36:33-07:00","id":1223632,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying that Lilith would necessarily need to have gone on an extended hiatus lasting several lifetimes in which she basically forsook human identity or involvement in the kinds of adventures typical of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bHowever, my feeling on the Celestial Exalted (possibly excluding the Sidereals) is that when they live for thousands of years, the idea that they're continuously doing grandiose things for the entire length of that both seems like it would be exhausting in character, and is kind of exhausting to try and conceptualise. In the case of most Exalted, I feel as though it's all right to have a sentiment that when they've been doing the derring-do for the duration of a couple centuries, it's all right for them to take a break for a few mortal lifetimes, in which they kind of settle into things that are mundane, even boring.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn Lilith's particular case, it might be that her own tragedies (and the length of time that she lived prior to the Usurpation) were severe enough that her idea of a hiatus was not only one that would go on indefinitely, but that included a desire to settle into a life and mindset even more simplified than that of normal humanity. A uniquely Lunar form of hermitage; forsake society for an extensive period of isolation and contemplation, in the form of an animal, rather than living in a cave with only stream water and wild fruit to sustain you.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think that if framed correctly, say in the manner of &quot;other elder Lunars remember Lilith as a highly accomplished huntress of the First Age, and the idea that something is finally prompting her to return to the world is a source of both excitement and a little bit of concern&quot;, then it doesn't need to be something that undermines her significance as a character, or the legitimacy of Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot all of the characters have lives as though they're the protagonists of an ongoing series, at least not at all times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T08:53:49-07:00","id":1223636,"title":"","content":"Lilith\u2019s idea of \u201cgrandiose\u201d would be different from yours. She could be slumming it and still scare the piss out of everything around her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T09:41:29-07:00","id":1223651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223589#post1223589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless there is absolutely no place for a Lunar to be a screw-up, someone has to fulfill the role, and it might as well be the one who was always the screw-up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ten Stripes was not a fuck up in Time of Tumult. She (or he; the text switches back and forth depending on how far into Crusaders of the Machine God you are) may have died, but her forces managed to rout those of Excessively Righteous Blossom even while Blossom was alive. Add onto that the general goodwill that most of the villages near the Silent Crescent had for them, and you get a very different character from 2e's total incompetent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T11:06:14-07:00","id":1223669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223589#post1223589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless there is absolutely no place for a Lunar to be a screw-up, someone has to fulfill the role, and it might as well be the one who was always the screw-up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. An officially designated screw-up is a colossal waste of words because their continued failure is more of a meme than a lesson for others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would posit that what really bothers us about Ten Stripes is not how she screwed up in her social engineering efforts, but that social engineering as the Lunar \u201cthing\u201d was empty to begin with. It\u2019s not something that every Lunar should be expected to try, let alone succeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with social engineering was that MoEP: Lunars was absolutely adamant that the Thousand Streams River Project was a righteous undertaking in a way that didn't create much in the way of story potential.<br /> <br /> Simenare was the example of a project going wrong it should have been been the sort of mistake a group of Lunar PCs could've made and demonstrated how this new element to the fluff could be a source of conflict. Instead it was just Ten Stripes making bad decision after bad decision and all it told us was that she was an idiot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T11:19:03-07:00","id":1223673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223669#post1223669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. An officially designated screw-up is a colossal waste of words because their continued failure is more of a meme than a lesson for others.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> I think there's a place for a Lunar screwing up... it's just not in the Lunar book. It's in What Fire Has Wrought, or The Realm, or maybe Sidereals, where a Dragonblood defeats a Lunar because of the Lunar's hubris or inexperience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T12:09:03-07:00","id":1223686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223651#post1223651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ten Stripes was not a fuck up in Time of Tumult. She (or he; the text switches back and forth depending on how far into Crusaders of the Machine God you are) may have died, but her forces managed to rout those of Excessively Righteous Blossom even while Blossom was alive. Add onto that the general goodwill that most of the villages near the Silent Crescent had for them, and you get a very different character from 2e's total incompetent.</div> </div> </div> </div>She was an incompetent in 1e\u2019s Autochthonian\u2019s manual, in one of its three canned adventures. So it was earlier than the second Lunar manual.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I\u2019m happier not having a screw-up. Always better to have an example of what to do than of what not to do.<br /> <br /> This seems related to how those ten rules of the Silver Pact were stupid, common sense things that all boiled down to \u201cdon\u2019t be an asshole\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T12:41:36-07:00","id":1223691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223636#post1223636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lilith\u2019s idea of \u201cgrandiose\u201d would be different from yours. She could be slumming it and still scare the piss out of everything around her.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBut it's possible to write a character as not being that. In the case of a Lunar, particularly a rather old one, I find it entirely possible for one to live in any shape for an extended period and have the average observer find them completely unremarkable. I have expressed my thoughts in what I think would be worthwhile and interesting in the idea of Lilith having retreated into a self-imposed exile of living the life of a relatively normal owl, rather then a deadly super owl.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor a hypothetical Ten Stripes... there's baggage there that needs to be deconstructed separately. For Lunar characters in general, as they would be presented in the book, I think that there's a valid place for the inclusion of failings, weaknesses and uncertainties, and of characters that are compromised in some manner. Not in the manner of somebody being a &quot;designated screw-up&quot;, and hence not somebody whose failures are exaggerated to a ludicrous point. Hell, not even for the sake of some kind of example of &quot;here's how a Lunar might act that you should avoid&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust something that would add some nuance to the presentation. Something that makes the overall picture a bit more believable and compelling and varied, adding to the image of a setting in which not everything is going well all the time, and not all of the major characters are aspirational. And I think that a Lunar book is a better place to put those details, because it's going to form the base standard for people's idea of them, and thus a more effective place to establish such ideas than in somebody else's book.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat Fire Has Wrought managed to include failures and weaknesses of some of the Dragon Blooded, whether they be Sesus Eshuvar not exactly being the picture of a dutiful husband, Belit being a highly accomplished woman who is spending her golden years languishing in bitterness and regret over the major unfulfilled ambitions, or House Tepet.<br /> <br /> \u200bI understand that the history of how Lunars have been written could create some apprehension around that, but I think if one leans too heavily on the idea that their book needs to make them out to be very impressive... really, that should generate a similar kind of apprehension, because the other two Lunars books tried doing that kind of thing as well, and I think that it's part of what made them among the weaker of the books detailing types of Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T13:46:43-07:00","id":1223706,"title":"","content":"Ten Stripes first shows up in Time of Tumult, where while she's defeated, her notable thing is she pretty much diverted the entire Yugashite leading force southward towards Gem and inflicted some big losses on them. Nothing in that write-upw as really much on her besides she apparently was powerful, might have been a notable ally to PCs, and generally caused issues for the Yugashi forces.<br /> <br /> That she is made an idiot in <b>Exalted: the Autochthonians</b> isn't much of use mentioning since everyone whow asn't Autochtonian was an idiot in those scenarios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T14:30:36-07:00","id":1223721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223706#post1223706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ten Stripes first shows up in Time of Tumult, where while she's defeated, her notable thing is she pretty much diverted the entire Yugashite leading force southward towards Gem and inflicted some big losses on them. Nothing in that write-upw as really much on her besides she apparently was powerful, might have been a notable ally to PCs, and generally caused issues for the Yugashi forces.<br /> <br /> That she is made an idiot in <b>Exalted: the Autochthonians</b> isn't much of use mentioning since everyone whow asn't Autochtonian was an idiot in those scenarios.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssals also made out like bandits, while the First and Forsaken Lion stole everyone's heat for years to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T16:29:22-07:00","id":1223755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223691#post1223691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBut it's possible to write a character as not being that. In the case of a Lunar, particularly a rather old one, I find it entirely possible for one to live in any shape for an extended period and have the average observer find them completely unremarkable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doing that for even 50 years is excessive, let alone the time since the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t ever want to read about another Lunar that decides to basically sleep away the better part of a millennium. These people were Chosen by Luna and invested with the power to rock the world. <br /> <br /> Can you point to any other Exalt who spent as many as 50 years attempting to accomplish absolutely nothing?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have expressed my thoughts in what I think would be worthwhile and interesting in the idea of Lilith having retreated into a self-imposed exile of living the life of a relatively normal owl, rather then a deadly super owl. </div> </div> </div>Normal owls fear being eaten or failing to catch food. Somehow I doubt she would tolerate going hungry unless she refused to hunt for the sake of experiencing gnawing hunger, or getting injured except out of a masochistic desire to bleed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T17:41:01-07:00","id":1223777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223755#post1223755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t ever want to read about another Lunar that decides to basically sleep away the better part of a millennium.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine; this is an extremely minor disagreement. All that I'm doing is answering the question of the kinds of things I would be interested in being in the book; I have my interests, you have yours. It's not a hill I have an interest in dying on.<br /> <br /> \u200bHowever, I do think that it's worth bringing up that Vance has stated that he likes the idea of Lilith having spent a long time as an owl, although I fully recognise that this in no way specifies it in terms of my preferences rather than yours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">These people were Chosen by Luna and invested with the power to rock the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOn the one hand, I don't think that the intentions of one's patrons is the most important metric by which to measure the life of an Exalt. On the other, this just goes back to my point about the conceptual and in-character exhaustion of expecting the Solar and Lunar Exalted to always be closing, without break or relief, for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe world can't always be rocking, because otherwise it falls over.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat and my perspective, which may be way off the mark, that Lunars striving for freedom can entail them employing their powers mostly for their own leisures, as well as expanding the range of what those leisures are. I see that as something in them a bit more than in the Solars or Sidereals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you point to any other Exalt who spent as many as 50 years attempting to accomplish absolutely nothing?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSetting aside the inherently loaded nature of the question with the phrasing &quot;attempting to accomplish absolutely nothing&quot; (which seems like a particularly pejorative way of viewing, say, somebody that has gone into retirement), I have an entire First Age in which to cheerfully make several of them up.<br /> <br /> \u200bI could also argue that Prince Aridhara eschewing the works of the mighty for the life of a travelling peddler, aiding the ordinary folk with small sorceries and subtle kindnesses, is closer to what I'm saying than what you are.<br /> <br /> Do you think she was a Lunar?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normal owls fear being eaten or failing to catch food. Somehow I doubt she would tolerate going hungry unless she refused to hunt for the sake of experiencing gnawing hunger, or getting injured except out of a masochistic desire to bleed.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHmm, I was initially inclined to dismiss this as pedantry that did not undermine the substance of my point, buuutt...<br /> <br /> \u200bActually it's interesting, you do actually bring up a point that I've been wondering while watching the BBC documentary series The Hunt on Netflix in the last few days; if a Lunar opting to spend an extended period of time in the form of a predatory animal might undermine local ecosystems by virtue of the capacity to be a vastly more successful predator than any natural one, considering how part of the balancing systems of an ecology is the indelible fact that most hunts end in failure.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf a Lunar is in the form of a blue whale, are they concerned with the sheer energy expenditure that it takes just to open their enormous mouths, and if not, is the blue whale Lunar willing to consume groups of krill that would not be dense enough to provide a mortal whale with sufficient calories? If so, does a Lunar going about in such a manner risk damaging the delicate balance of the ecosystem?<br /> <br /> \u200bOr if there's something instinctual to being a Lunar, especially while they're assuming the shape of an animal (which I'm inclined to view as something that basically every Lunar will frequently do for pure leisure reasons, especially seeing as their spirit shape is supposed to be a true form to them), it may be that a Lunar can naturally settle into a pattern of behaviour that means that they don't go around causing massive ecological devastation by virtue of the power of an Exalt every time they want to spend a week vacationing in the form of basically anything.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, while it is possible to regard the narrative of Lilith living an extended time as an owl in terms of her being a successful predator to the point that she quickly wipes out prey species within her flight radius, and either is constantly spreading her ecological devastation around, or is living as a kind of avian Shelob surrounded by a circle of quiet emptiness...<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I'm taking my cues from the First Edition core chapter fiction that introduced her, in which her assumption of owl form seems to go beyond an act of costume play and into a retreat from humanity and consciousness, I would actually be seeing things in terms of her having been an owl that would be frequently hungry and occasionally get a bit scratched up by a larger bird of prey swooping down upon her, even if on the whole she manages to be a bird that is a slightly more successful predator than the norm, who generally managed to outfly other predators, and always struggled free any time they caught her.<br /> <br /> \u200bI regard that in terms of an uncanny and mystical (in the sense of actual mystics, &quot;forsake all possessions and live in silence in the freaking desert&quot; kinds of mystics) thing for a <b>single, <i>solitary</i></b> Lunar to have been doing with her time. Partially because I'm simply enamoured with the fiction that introduced Lilith, partially because I like the idea of a famed ancient warrior Lunar having retreated into complete obscurity throughout the Second Age until such Time of Tumult as she is provoked back into action. And partially just in its own right, for the uncanniness and mysticism of a shapeshifter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T18:46:22-07:00","id":1223796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223777#post1223777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bHowever, I do think that it's worth bringing up that Vance has stated that he likes the idea of Lilith having spent a long time as an owl</div> </div> </div> </div>Leviathan has spent a long time as a whale; that didn't mean pretending to be a mortal whale. He's feared as a vengeful god across the entire Western Sea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> expecting the Solar and Lunar Exalted to always be closing, without break or relief, for thousands of years. </div> </div> </div>Better than expecting the Lunar Exalted to continue pushing a narrative of victimhood and &quot;history is what was done to us&quot; as though they had no power or responsibility to improve their lot in life or to have avoided it going to shit in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bThat and my perspective, which may be way off the mark, that Lunars striving for freedom can entail them employing their powers mostly for their own leisures, as well as expanding the range of what those leisures are. </div> </div> </div>Sleeping an entire era away like Magnificent Jaguar did cannot be considered leisure. He was dead to the world and had no biological need for that much rest.<br /> <br /> Neither can that be considered retirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T18:56:13-07:00","id":1223798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223796#post1223796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better than expecting the Lunar Exalted to continue pushing a narrative of victimhood and &quot;history is what was done to us&quot; as though they had no power or responsibility to improve their lot in life or to have avoided it going to shit in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI expect you to know me better than this.<br /> <br /> \u200bDon't presume to think you're the only one that has ever devoted significant energy to advocating for the Lunars, even if I'll grant that you've been doing it for longer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T19:09:45-07:00","id":1223801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223798#post1223798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI expect you to know me better than this.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies, that wasn't meant as an accusation of your motives.<br /> <br /> But my idea of Lunar &quot;retirement&quot; in the Second Age is Leviathan and Ma-Ha-Suchi. They're both sulking in depression, but their presence is unmistakeable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T19:57:56-07:00","id":1223818,"title":"","content":"I want to reiterate that what I meant there by &quot;retirement&quot; was the idea that, in the First Age, you might get some Exalted who need a break from the life of intrigue and adventure every few centuries, and wind up in a life situation in which they're doing something peaceful and mundane. They might occasionally use their powers to do something impressive in that context, such as hoist an entire tree trunk on their shoulders for firewood, but still just putting the call in their Essence aside for a while.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm compelled by the image that Lea has described in his conception of the relationship between Merela and the Unconquered Sun, in which they hook up every once in a while, except where for them hooking up entails living in a domestic co-habitation for decades and raise a few kids, because they've both got the time.<br /> <br /> \u200bHowever, those are part of my being contrary to the basic principle of &quot;the Exalted should be doing interesting things all their lives&quot;. The example of what I'm seeing with Lilith is specific and extreme both in what it entails for her personality, and in the idea of her intending it to be permanent. <br /> <br /> That and how I would enjoy the narrative of her being an infamous warrior that is only just returning to the game if, for the intervening period, she was unobtrusive.<br /> <br /> \u200bLeviathan's story, in which his retreat from society entails him becoming a great terror of the open oceans, that's a great story. I love that story. I don't want Lilith's story to be that one in a different biome.<br /> <br /> \u200bI couldn't say much for Magnificent Jaguar beyond not particularly minding that he's a person that looked at the downfall of the Age and decided to sleep it out.<br /> <br /> \u200bWe've got some other First Age Lunars that are a bit more active, and maybe room for a few others.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough on the other hand, I wouldn't exactly mind the idea that the surviving First Age Lunars are not necessarily the best suited to be driving the thrust of the Silver Pact. That the likes of your Sha'a Oka might look at Leviathan and feel as though his perspective and world view for having actually lived in the First Age is practically alien, as well as maybe the idea that having actually lived through what the loss of the Solars and downfall of the Old Realm has done to their Essence and needing to have their Castes remade might have given them some damage that they're perhaps better off being in the distance dealing with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T20:05:14-07:00","id":1223820,"title":"","content":"Remind me how a Lunar spending a few centuries R&amp;Ring as a bird is any different from, say, the great general returning to his farm to live in obscurity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T20:33:02-07:00","id":1223825,"title":"","content":"I like how Lilith demonstrates a distinctive approach to dealing with the fall into an Age of Sorrows as it compares with Leviathan and Ma-Ha-Suchi, it makes her feel very distinct and esoteric, which is a completely different flavor of interesting from Leviathan or Ma-Ha-Suchi.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's necessary to weigh the potential of the return of her first edition concept down with the sins of second edition's extended backstories of do-nothingness for people like Magnificent Jaguar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T20:36:37-07:00","id":1223826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223820#post1223820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remind me how a Lunar spending a few centuries R&amp;Ring as a bird is any different from, say, the great general returning to his farm to live in obscurity?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIn this particular context, I'd say that it might be a question of how Lilith is dealing with an ongoing challenge that is of significance to herself and the world, whereas I presume that the general in question is doing so at the end of a narrative of accomplishment.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat being said, while thinking of any literary antecedents for the idea of a general that wanted to remain on their farm as an alternative to war, I'm reminded of the example of Odysseus; the very first thing that he did in his story was try to employ his wit and guile to trick the people that wanted to call him away to apply those skills to adventure and glorious conquest into thinking him ineffectual and leaving him alone. Odysseus would have happily remained on his farm (and saved himself a lot of grief), and only managed to be coerced into participation because he didn't value his freedom over the life of his baby son.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T07:44:55-07:00","id":1223907,"title":"","content":"Edit: Wrong thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-01-2018, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T10:56:31-07:00","id":1223956,"title":"","content":"Lunars are the ones most punished for the concept of the 'distant past of the First Age'. Solars &amp; likes were all locked away, DBs were in charge but still died and had later generations, and Sidereals are so few that the First Age survivor concept falls on one guy, Kejak, and that's his theme. By comparison, multiple Lunars had to survive a Full Age to react to returning Solars, but not running things awesomely like Kejak got.<br /> One awesome adventure every 50 years for 2 millenia is 40 adventures. Writing a quarter of those gives 10 historical plothooks of awesomeness per 1st Age Lunar. That could easily fill a chapter of the book. 5 plothooks from each Shogunate Age Lunars to help pad out the timeline would make a big impact.<br /> If they get to be specifically responsible for losses to the Shogunate, named and referenced for later, or used to show us what a 3 century sorcerous working or Artifact Crafting can do they would give Lunars a much better base to stand on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24220,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","user":"Cryo-Seraph","date":". 06-01-2018, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T13:06:45-07:00","id":1223982,"title":"","content":"The past tradition of the Silver Pact achieving little since the Usurpation is a related but separate issue from the tradition of how none of the First Age survivors seems to be able to cope with depression or trauma even with several mortal life-times to rest, reflect, and recover.<br /> <br /> But for this Edition, Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s depressive sulk might be as much because of some relatively recent setback or defeat or loss, rather than one long, unbroken pity-party stretching back to the Usurpation. <br /> <br /> Magnificent Jaguar might be given a different reason for his long sleep, or maybe a different time-frame.<br /> <br /> Leviathan might be actively fighting the Realm rather than just hiding away, or bullying a sunken city of mortals and Dragon-Blooded. He might have better reasons to be with-holding powerful First Age weapons from other Lunars besides \u201cI don\u2019t feel like actually exerting myself yet\u201d.<br /> <br /> Lilith might have gotten over her abuse centuries ago and just decided she doesn\u2019t give a shit about the Realm, choosing to remain a retired hermit out of preference, but still remaining connected enough to the world that she can hear about the return of the Solars, so maybe she might accept Lunar students who seek her out for training in return for favors. <br /> <br /> In past Editions, the Lunar Exalted were victims. Even the Wyld victimized them.<br /> <br /> This time, they are victors. They broke their castes to remake them on purpose. They endured the Wyld like no one else could. They are slowly winning the war for the Caul and against the Realm, at least for now. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d like to see them allowed to have the emotional strength to overcome their psychological challenges as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-01-2018, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T23:56:43-07:00","id":1224096,"title":"","content":"Tammuz has... but that's one Elder out of all of them. I think it's fine to have one Elder who's still traumatised, but you're right. I'm not sure if it was an idea that got overused, or an explanation for why the Elders didn't seem to be doing much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T07:45:17-07:00","id":1224157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1224096#post1224096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tammuz has... but that's one Elder out of all of them. I think it's fine to have one Elder who's still traumatised, but you're right. I'm not sure if it was an idea that got overused, or an explanation for why the Elders didn't seem to be doing much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember Tammuz existing in First Edition, let alone accomplishing anything.<br /> <br /> Second Edition tried to sell us on the idea that Tammuz was somehow masterfully responsible for two nations of mortals resolving a dispute and building a nation that mortals don't need immortal demigods to help achieve. &quot;He is so successful, you can't even tell he actually did anything!&quot; Blah.<br /> <br /> Rain Deathflier and Silver Python were slightly more impressive, since they are credited with the creation of the San-Beasts and Ata-Beasts, as well as establishing the treaty with the Fair Folk. But that's all they did, and Halta was over-large, over-used, and over-important in Second Edition, as well as being underwhelming in terms of imagination. I faintly recall accusations of their society being too perfect and eglatarian and heroic. But returning to the two elder Lunars behind the whole thing, they seem to basically cease to exist after founding Halta.<br /> <br /> Raksi was allowed to accomplish somewhat more than that because she was a literally baby-eating evil antagonist. She was a raid boss with epic loot in the form of the Book of Three Circles which a circle of Solar players would naturally covet.<br /> <br /> Compared to these ancient terrors, the Spider King, the Black Wave Reavers, Yena Bone-Breaker, and Sha Oka'a are much more exciting and inspiring. They are clearly, actively engaged in the world, exerting all of their power and achieving commensurate results.<br /> <br /> Sha Oka'a in particular was Exalted during the Shogunate, and he didn't do one thing and then disappear. His story is one of constant activity and warfare, which is paying off in the modern day with near-complete control of the Caul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T07:57:23-07:00","id":1224160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223820#post1223820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remind me how a Lunar spending a few centuries R&amp;Ring as a bird is any different from, say, the great general returning to his farm to live in obscurity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the largest empire in the world actively trying to locate and murder that general and all of his step-brothers and step-sisters?<br /> <br /> Is &quot;returning to life a happy, peaceful life with a spouse and children&quot; equal to &quot;retreat forever into the un-reflective mind of a simple owl to avoid ever having to think or feel about the abuse you suffered&quot;?<br /> <br /> Lilith's centuries of exile were never painted as a desirable retirement, but as an unhealthy escape from trauma. It wasn't about her happening to like living as an owl, but finding that less painful than living as a woman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T08:09:20-07:00","id":1224165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223669#post1223669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. An officially designated screw-up is a colossal waste of words because their continued failure is more of a meme than a lesson for others.</div> </div> </div> </div>By &quot;always a screw-up&quot;, I meant that they were a character who always failed big at something or other in each previous Edition.<br /> <br /> I was definitely not excusing the existence of a character who fails at everything they attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T08:11:39-07:00","id":1224166,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I\u2019d like to see them allowed to have the emotional strength to overcome their psychological challenges as well.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bHmm, that's a fair point, although one that I'm still inclined to try and find reconciliation with some of my own interests.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bOne thing that occurs to me is a subject that I brought up with the Dragon Blooded; how their Medicine Charm for dealing with Flaws modelling mental illness don't go in for the idea of removing such conditions all together, but of reducing severity and relieving symptoms. In the case of the most ancient Lunars, the ones that remember their old Castes, I'm feeling that there may be a place for them having managed to develop means of dealing with the trauma to their Essence but where the injury is still a part of them, and always will be; managed, treated, but present, and still lending an element of difference to them.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bThat and the idea that having lived in the First Age can make it somewhat difficult for their younger peers to relate to them.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bMostly, I'm just interested in the line of thought that came with the idea that the First Age Lunars are not necessarily at the top of the Silver Pact. Possibly in the form of the attention they have to give to their own issues meaning that they're better off deferring those responsibilities to others, maybe with people that have only ever known the Second Age having the stronger perspective on how and why to fight being more suited as the driving force in the group. Maybe it's just a numbers game, and the smaller number of First Age elders creates a higher probability that younger ones will include the more driven or capable.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bAfter all, I expect the number of ancient Lunars with Essence over 5 to drop off sharply; past a certain point, the difference between being a thousand years old and coming up on 3,000 might not be very significant in terms of what you're capable of doing and how much respect you command.<br /> <br /> \u200bI want to go through a couple of other things...</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223982#post1223982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for this Edition, Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s depressive sulk might be as much because of some relatively recent setback or defeat or loss, rather than one long, unbroken pity-party stretching back to the Usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOn the one hand, I disagree with characterising his attitude as a depressive sulk, but do think there's potential in the idea that the onset of his weariness is a more recent occurrence. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magnificent Jaguar might be given a different reason for his long sleep, or maybe a different time-frame.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI have thoughts on his prior backstory, but would need time to rally them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leviathan might be actively fighting the Realm rather than just hiding away, or bullying a sunken city of mortals and Dragon-Blooded. He might have better reasons to be with-holding powerful First Age weapons from other Lunars besides \u201cI don\u2019t feel like actually exerting myself yet\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYes, I definitely think that if Leviathan still has Luthe, he needs to relate to it a bit differently. What I was saying before about what I liked about him was primarily in the manner of thinking that he's adopted a lifestyle that makes him virtually a behemoth; a terror who haunts the shipping lanes of the West, and boe betide and Dynast vessels that cross paths with him. I had a sense that among Lunars, he's admired and venerable and somebody that they're quite happy to leave off on his own doing his own thing, because it's achieving a worthwhile result, and nobody is exactly strongly motivated to find out exactly how deliberate his current lifestyle is. That there are Lunars who are uncertain whether or not his living in the manner that he does constitutes something being the matter with him, and are not sure which possibility is more concerning; best just to leave him to himself.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lilith might have gotten over her abuse centuries ago and just decided she doesn\u2019t give a shit about the Realm, choosing to remain a retired hermit out of preference, but still remaining connected enough to the world that she can hear about the return of the Solars, so maybe she might accept Lunar students who seek her out for training in return for favors.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI have mixed thoughts on the question of whether or not Lilith's pains are something that should come from abuse (whatever form it might have taken). On the one hand, I wouldn't want to diminish the idea that it's perfectly acceptable for an Exalted character to have faced such, that this doesn't lessen them, or that abuse is something that is somehow beneath them. On the other, I would also see problematic connotations in things such as a highly prominent woman Exalt being one whose life story is strongly characterised by abuse, and possible unfortunate implications in the idea of a reaction to that in the form of a social withdrawal (as well as the matter of pigeonholing the answer for exactly what went on with her that prompted her retreat).<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's a fine line, and one that would need to be given significant consideration.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T15:39:19-07:00","id":1224459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1223982#post1223982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magnificent Jaguar might be given a different reason for his long sleep, or maybe a different time-frame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two words: Limit Break.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lilith might have gotten over her abuse centuries ago and just decided she doesn\u2019t give a shit about the Realm, choosing to remain a retired hermit out of preference, but still remaining connected enough to the world that she can hear about the return of the Solars, so maybe she might accept Lunar students who seek her out for training in return for favors. </div> </div> </div>This or something like it honestly feels like the default assumption to me, at least for this edition? Sure, maybe her indefinite owldom started out as a trauma-induced reaction to the Usurpation and/or her life before it, but at some point her reason for keeping it up mutated from \u201cWoe is me\u201d to \u201cI am so <i>done</i> with <i>everything</i>\u201d or even \u201cYou know what, I <i>like</i> being an owl, stop judging me.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T13:46:54-07:00","id":1225070,"title":"","content":"So, Swaying Grass Style and Centipede Style are confirmed.<br /> <br /> Capoeira and Tae Kwan Do?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t really know what Centipede Style is supposed to be about. I remember something about iron-soled boots and questionable Extra Attack Charms. Can someone help me see the appeal?<br /> <br /> Swaying Grass Style gets me more excited for a possible Spider Style and the Grass Spider clan of Dragon-Blooded assassins who might use both... but not so much for Lunars, though the Grass Spiders at least might be allies of the Silver Pact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T14:22:10-07:00","id":1225080,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t see any particular connection between. Swaying Grass Style and a Spider Style wielded by the Grass Spiders. What makes you draw that conmection?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T15:03:49-07:00","id":1225094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1225080#post1225080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t see any particular connection between. Swaying Grass Style and a Spider Style wielded by the Grass Spiders. What makes you draw that conmection?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because going by names, the Grass Spiders hide in grass from which they ambush people with bolas and nets and finish them off with poison, Spider Style provides the bondage and poison, and Swaying Grass helps you move stealthily through swaying grass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T15:53:15-07:00","id":1225107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1225070#post1225070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t really know what Centipede Style is supposed to be about. I remember something about iron-soled boots and questionable Extra Attack Charms. Can someone help me see the appeal?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm excited because I'm a big fan of the Shaw Brothers classic <i>Five Deadly Venoms</i>, where a speed-focused Centipede was one of the five titular styles. I don't expect Toad due to overlap with native Resistance Charms, and Lizard (whose main gimmick is gecko-like wall-climbing) has a similar problem with Athletics Charms, but Centipede gives me some hope that we'll at least be able to approximate the full set by the end of this edition. Here's hoping for Scorpion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T16:14:50-07:00","id":1225112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1225070#post1225070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t really know what Centipede Style is supposed to be about. I remember something about iron-soled boots and questionable Extra Attack Charms. Can someone help me see the appeal?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI would suspect an alternative method of venomous attacks from Snake Style.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T17:09:11-07:00","id":1225117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1225107#post1225107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm excited because I'm a big fan of the Shaw Brothers classic <i>Five Deadly Venoms</i>, where a speed-focused Centipede was one of the five titular styles. I don't expect Toad due to overlap with native Resistance Charms, and Lizard (whose main gimmick is gecko-like wall-climbing) has a similar problem with Athletics Charms, but Centipede gives me some hope that we'll at least be able to approximate the full set by the end of this edition. Here's hoping for Scorpion!</div> </div> </div> </div>Centipede style is indeed heavily inspired by <i>Five Deadly Venoms</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T19:11:17-07:00","id":1225138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1225117#post1225117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Centipede style is indeed heavily inspired by <i>Five Deadly Venoms</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you kindly tell us anything more about it?<br /> <br /> Does it still use the same weapons as in Second Edition? Hook swords, seven-section staves, and iron-soled/armored boots?<br /> <br /> How do you see this particular Style enriching Lunar-centric stories in the way that White Veil, Golden Janissary, and Mantis Styles fit into stories revolving around Dragon-Blooded nations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-05-2018, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T20:17:17-07:00","id":1225156,"title":"","content":"Wow I just found the Dev diary because it was mentioned in the Ask Dev thread. Centipede Style and Swaying Grass Dance?! I thought we lost the chance to have those! I am so happy this pipe dream of having those in Canon a thing! And that Exigents will include advice on not just exigents but extrapolating the Exigent advice to apply to making your own unique Exalts! You guys do listen! These are literally all things I was rallying for! I thought I would have to vivisect the Exigent book for scrap of technology to do things like make the Immortal Weapons Exalted. Magnificent!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T20:19:39-07:00","id":1225157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211791#post1211791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says any of the styles in the Lunars book have to be an update to an old one?<br /> <br /> Also, Celestial Monkey wasn't all that memorable or interesting, at least not to me.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Really, only three things stuck with me:<br /> <br /> -One, how nonsensical it felt for your ability to practice the style to <i>implode</i> if you ever raised your Virtue dots too high.<br /> <br /> -Two, hitting people in places corresponding to their Virtue dots, it really felt like someone was tripping over themself to get a dick joke printed.<br /> <br /> -Three, the capstone permitting me to treat whatever weapons and armor I wanted as acceptable for the style felt like it was dragging the idea of &quot;having any real feel to it&quot; out back and putting a round in its head.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'd much rather see a new style in its place, such as Scorpion, Falcon, Bull, Spider, or Wolf Style. <i>If</i> we have to bring Monkey back, it needs to be overhauled pretty drastically.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But of course its going to be overhauled though. I don't expect any style not to be. I mean Snake was pretty much always snake but things like Ebon Shadow took out the hypnotism and what not. I go with styles based on the &quot;style&quot; of combat they bring. Usually the type of evocative martial arts from real world, or the type of weapon/armor they use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T08:04:03-07:00","id":1225582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1225112#post1225112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI would suspect an alternative method of venomous attacks from Snake Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on scenes from the movie and videos of real centipedes, I\u2019m guessing Centipede Style will look like a venomous Tiger Style. A brutal, rush-down, head-on approach in contrast to Snake\u2019s graceful evasion and quick strikes.<br /> <br /> Centipedes use their many legs to rush and tackle their prey with great speed and force. After they latch on with their poisonous claws, they use the leverage of their long bodies and many legs to hold, lift, slam, and flip their prey to render them helpless to escape or counter-grapple, all while continuing to tear at them with venomous claws.<br /> <br /> The Centipede Stylist in the movie attacked with confusing and fast movements that were hard to evade, and would clinch his victims with one arm to deliver deadly strikes with the other. He could also render a victim prone and barrage them with kicks to keep them down. <br /> <br /> But...<br /> <br /> We already have Tiger and Mantis for rush-down grappling that puts opponents on the floor and keeps them there. <br /> <br /> We also have Snake, White Veil, and Black Claw Styles: Three venomous Styles already. Four, if you count Wood Dragon Style, which is venomous in spirit with its soul-striking attacks.<br /> <br /> Poison is a weapon, and it is already well-represented with published Martial Arts Styles. I would like to see other weapons get at least as much attention as slashing swords and polearms and firewands got. Especially weapons that never got attention in previous Editions.<br /> <br /> Such as axes.<br /> <br /> Swords have had Fire Dragon and Violet Bier of Sorrows Styles, and now have Single Point Shining into the Void and Steel Devil Style, and they also had Even Blade and Five Dragon Style in a previous Edition. <br /> <br /> Spears have had White Reaper and Golden Janissary Styles, and they also had Crimson Pentacle Blade, Lightning Hoof, and Five Dragon Styles in a previous Edition.<br /> <br /> We currently and traditionally have more Styles that use hook swords, seven-section staves, and war fans than Styles that use hammers, and none that have ever used axes.<br /> <br /> Conversely, what do you suppose was the most popular weapon in the world? A weapon which doubled as an indispensable tool of labor, and which was far simpler and cheaper to make than swords.<br /> <br /> The humble ax. <br /> <br /> If Swaying Grass Style is being included because Luna famously chooses slaves in bondage and because Lunars foment rebellion among slaves, then axes deserve Martial Arts representation as the weapon of choice for poor peasants and farmers and militias defending their homes from imperial conquerors, and also iconically used by raiding bands of barbarians and \u201csub-human\u201d monster races like goblins, orcs, trolls, ogres, minotaurs...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T08:24:15-07:00","id":1225588,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m looking forward to Swaying Grass Style, because Capoeira is cool and kicking-exclusive fighters have lacked support. I like bringing Performance into combat, and I hope that this can be taken as a sign that the book will include a Performance-related sorcery initiation. Ar Tonelico song magic and Bayonetta dance-summoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T08:50:04-07:00","id":1225598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1225582#post1225582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poison is a weapon, and it is already well-represented with published Martial Arts Styles. I would like to see other weapons get at least as much attention as slashing swords and polearms and firewands got. Especially weapons that never got attention in previous Editions.<br /> <br /> Such as axes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could argue that the spear is more basic and more widespread <i>as a weapon</i> than the axe, but there's a more pertinent issue here with regard to martial arts styles.<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear examples if you've got them, but I can't think of much fictional or real-world precedent for stylish axe fighting. The recent God of War Leviathan Axe is pretty flashy... but that's really more a matter of Evocations rather than Kratos knowing axe-fu. (Although I'll admit that the Bloodstorm Blade Prestige Class in 3.5 D&amp;D's Tome of Battle did do returning thrown melee weapons as a fighting style.) Hatchets show up sometimes in martial arts movies, but in the hands of mook gangsters. I guess you could argue Labrys from Persona 4 Arena as some precedent, but even there I'd see her moves as Melee + Evocations.<br /> <br /> I can certainly sympathize with feeling like your favorite weapon is getting overlooked (I felt that way with spears in 2E until the release of Crystal Chameleon), but I'm also not sure that checking boxes for the purpose of checking boxes is the way to go. What do you want to see from an axe martial art that you can't do with Melee Charms and weapon-specific Evocations? And what are you taking as inspiration for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T10:51:30-07:00","id":1225624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1225598#post1225598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could argue that the spear is more basic and more widespread <i>as a weapon</i> than the axe</div> </div> </div> </div>Though the ax is definitely more present in societies which are denied weapons or the right to hunt in their own lands; axes can\u2019t be denied because they are essential tools. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd love to hear examples if you've got them, but I can't think of much fictional or real-world precedent for stylish axe fighting. </div> </div> </div>Rachel from Monty Oum\u2019s Dead Fantasy videos and Darius from League of Legends show us how the axe can be used like a hook for pulling or throwing your enemies around with withering attacks; decisive attacks that bury the axe\u2019s blade in meat and bone could also transition into grapples. <br /> <br /> You can hook an axe\u2019s head around a shield or parrying weapon or limb to pull it out of the way, creating an oppening for attack with a second weapon. <br /> Perhaps even disarm your opponent. <br /> <br /> After hooking someone\u2019s legs out from under them to render them prone, you can deliver a more effective chopping attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although I'll admit that the Bloodstorm Blade Prestige Class in 3.5 D&amp;D's Tome of Battle did do returning thrown melee weapons as a fighting style </div> </div> </div>Imagine something like Air Dragon Style, but for throwing hatchets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hatchets show up sometimes in martial arts movies, but in the hands of mook gangsters. </div> </div> </div>Like knives in London, where owning weapons is illegal, so you need something small, cheap, and plausibly a tool for work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T12:15:03-07:00","id":1225652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1225624#post1225624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rachel from Monty Oum\u2019s Dead Fantasy videos and Darius from League of Legends show us how the axe can be used like a hook for pulling or throwing your enemies around with withering attacks; decisive attacks that bury the axe\u2019s blade in meat and bone could also transition into grapples.<br /> <br /> You can hook an axe\u2019s head around a shield or parrying weapon or limb to pull it out of the way, creating an oppening for attack with a second weapon.<br /> Perhaps even disarm your opponent.<br /> <br /> After hooking someone\u2019s legs out from under them to render them prone, you can deliver a more effective chopping attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm, I'll admit that using an axe as a hook for tripping / disarming would be a good angle for an axe-based MA. Also doable with hook swords, canes, umbrellas, etc, but it could be fun with axes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T09:53:33-07:00","id":1227691,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t believe I didn\u2019t think of this earlier, but I want an artifact moonsilver bow in the Lunar book.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting offers Lunars a lot of competing options with close-range artifact weapons, but no mundane animal forms offer ranged firepower on par with bows.<br /> <br /> Plus, archer-huntress moon goddess inspiration.<br /> <br /> So, I want to see a moonsilver bow specialized for extreme range sniping and/or bombardment. For the Lunar who wants to totally avoid engagement or who wants to really soften a target up before they close the distance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T10:18:04-07:00","id":1227694,"title":"","content":"I mean, technically there is already one. It's just not that good.<br /> <br /> But you are right about it being something that Lunars by themselves aren't very good at.<br /> And a bow seems more thematic than a crossbow or firewand. I can't really imagine what a moonsilver crossbow or firewand would be like.<br /> <br /> Of course, there is a reason, gameplay-wise, why Lunars haven't got much in the way of ranged attacks: the fact so many of them can fly. A Lunar flying up into the sky and shooting you with a long-range bow specialised in sniping is a very, very boring fight.<br /> <br /> So I'd prefer really some kind of closer-range weapon.<br /> A skirmisher's bow, a hunter's bow that specialises in sneaking, a bow that shoots arrows which turn into silver snakes, whatever, but not one that lets you get around the restrictions on sniping (ie the fact you need to aim to shoot at medium+ range).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-15-2018, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T10:20:09-07:00","id":1227695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1227694#post1227694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, technically there is already one. It's just not that good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about Moonlit Huntress? Because, I mean, Moonlit Huntress is pretty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T10:34:52-07:00","id":1227697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1227695#post1227695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you talking about Moonlit Huntress? Because, I mean, Moonlit Huntress is pretty good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you want to defend it in the thread where I laid out how horrible it was?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T10:41:10-07:00","id":1227698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1227695#post1227695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you talking about Moonlit Huntress? Because, I mean, Moonlit Huntress is pretty good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I was a bit reductionist. It's evocation is actually amazingly good (though you have to wait two stories to buy it), it just only has the one. I assume Sunder is asking for a full evocation tree, for someone who wants to be really invested in their moonsilver bow.<br /> <br /> For someone who wants to just dip into it, Moonlit Huntress is, as you say, pretty good.<br /> <br /> Also, re-reading it to double check, I found something I'd forgotten: Moonlit Huntress is actually <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">a moonsilver bow specialized for extreme range sniping and/or bombardment</div> </div> </div> </div>.<br /> If you have Initiative 15+, you can reflexively aim to be able to shoot people from medium or long range.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, to get back to my original point: there already is a Moonsilver bow specialised in sniping and/or bombardment (not extreme range, but I feel long range is long enough). While people may want one with a longer evocation tree, I'd rather see a differently-specialised moonsilver ranged weapon than a rehash of one we already had.<br /> <br /> I confess, I do quite want to see a moonsilver flamepiece, but I can't really think what it'd do. I just think that'd be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T15:51:31-07:00","id":1227775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1227697#post1227697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you want to defend it in the thread where I laid out how horrible it was?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T16:17:19-07:00","id":1227780,"title":"","content":"Then sufficient to say, it's a lackluster example in need of errata, and I'd like to see a proper alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T19:52:35-07:00","id":1228470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1227780#post1227780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then sufficient to say, it's a lackluster example in need of errata, and I'd like to see a proper alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if the moonsilver bow in fangs at the gate was moonlight huntress? But the evocation tree is based on a lunar wielder. And longer than one","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T20:01:27-07:00","id":1228479,"title":"","content":"So the subject of assuming the forms and powers of spirits came up in the Ask the Devs thread.<br /> <br /> \u200bPersonally, the idea of acquiring such powers was something that I was very cold towards up until the Third Edition core dropped, where things like Divine Mantle gave me a sense of how such things could be handled for Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut I'm still feeling a little bit of trepidations; concern that it might make animals feel as though they're the minor form that gets graduated from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T20:37:55-07:00","id":1228489,"title":"","content":"Current plans according to Vance are that the most you can ever get from hunting spirits is their Eclipse Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T05:08:23-07:00","id":1228548,"title":"","content":"Ahh yes, I remember that. I find it eminently sensible; a nice way of letting divine forms hang around the outskirts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T06:25:01-07:00","id":1228558,"title":"","content":"Anyone have any thoughts on what a 5-dot artifact moonsilver bow could be like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T06:35:52-07:00","id":1228563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1228558#post1228558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have any thoughts on what a 5-dot artifact moonsilver bow could be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about... something dedicated to pursuit of quarry or attacking from the shadows, in which sticking the target with arrows causes them to become embedded and mark the target as prey in a manner that inhabits them and empowers the archer.<br /> <br /> In particular, an effect of the embedded arrows virtually dragging the Hunter along, creating a mounting obsession with catching up.<br /> <br /> The pinnacle effect could have the bow's wielder merge with it to create some kind of abstract, berserk beast, that relentlessly tears through everything that may lie in between it and the marked target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T07:16:53-07:00","id":1228573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1228563#post1228563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about... something dedicated to pursuit of quarry or attacking from the shadows, in which sticking the target with arrows causes them to become embedded and mark the target as prey in a manner that inhabits them and empowers the archer.<br /> <br /> In particular, an effect of the embedded arrows virtually dragging the Hunter along, creating a mounting obsession with catching up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funnily enough, back when I was toying with the idea of making my own Lunar homebrew (this was before the release schedule changed, when we were slated to get Exigents first), I wanted to make these exact things native Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T08:00:48-07:00","id":1228586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1228558#post1228558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have any thoughts on what a 5-dot artifact moonsilver bow could be like?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shoot snakes at them!...okay, that might be a bit silly, but arrows that are alive and pursue their target even after the attack seem like an intreasting idea to me. Or that embed themselves, and explode out again later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T08:51:52-07:00","id":1228595,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m working on a bow so terrifying that people run away when you take aim at them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T09:38:57-07:00","id":1228606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1228573#post1228573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Funnily enough, back when I was toying with the idea of making my own Lunar homebrew (this was before the release schedule changed, when we were slated to get Exigents first), I wanted to make these exact things native Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the hands of an actual Lunar, it might wind up being something that would enhance a number of their own Charms...<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich actually seems a bit lesser than a 5-dot Artifact, at least as I envision them.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf it was a thing that I was actually writing up while having a new Lunar Charm set to hand, I'd probably be looking for ways to express the concept that distinguish themselves from what a Lunar can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T11:06:31-07:00","id":1228629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1228595#post1228595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m working on a bow so terrifying that people run away when you take aim at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Assuming you're doing it with moosilver, how are you presenting it? I would think that making it soulsteel would be much more direct (direct does not equate to better mind you) approach for a terrifying bow. Are you going with a 'terror that stalks the night' type of vibe with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T11:30:27-07:00","id":1228631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1228629#post1228629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. Assuming you're doing it with moosilver, how are you presenting it? I would think that making it soulsteel would be much more direct (direct does not equate to better mind you) approach for a terrifying bow. Are you going with a 'terror that stalks the night' type of vibe with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not a stealthy bow. Your target has to see you aiming at them for you to get a reflexive Threaten action against them.<br /> <br /> Other Evocations build upon this power, granting greater ability to inflict and exploit fear, as well as more ways to inflict it.<br /> <br /> Perhaps not enough about it is particularly moonsilver, yet. Even the slated Evocation to detect and track opponents intimidated by you could be appropriate to soulsteel.<br /> <br /> But there is a lot of potential for this bow to represent protection of allies and territory, exploiting the fear it creates to drive aggressors away from both. There\u2019s also the potential for mercy, in that opponents who flee are opponents who live.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T14:12:30-07:00","id":1228678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1228631#post1228631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there is a lot of potential for this bow to represent protection of allies and territory, exploiting the fear it creates to drive aggressors away from both. There\u2019s also the potential for mercy, in that opponents who flee are opponents who live.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a solid subset to tie to the Lunar charm set, given the mention of Lunars having domain/territory charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T15:50:59-07:00","id":1228697,"title":"","content":"I have two different Lunar Concepts I want to play that are arguably on the opposite sides of the spectrum of Lunarness, so I am hoping both will be playable.<br /> <br /> One is basically a pastiche of Dio Brando from JoJo's, across all his different incarnations. A charismatic velociraptor guy who grew up in luxury, who uses his powers to turn other people into velociraptors as well, or does things like throw flies that turn into mini velociraptors. I don't imagine this being against people's will or being brutal or uncaring; I'd be pulling more of his personality from Diego Brando then Dio, who was generally more affable and just kind of a dickbag instead of a literal monster.<br /> <br /> The other I'm imagining as some combination of Medusa and an Arrancar from Bleach. A Lunar whose Warform is so terrifying that it's literally sealed away inside her sword, and she only lets it out in deadly situations because she has a lot of trouble controlling it. In her normal times, she's a former child soldier of the South who runs an orphanage, taking care of kids that she rescues from the same armies she was a part of.<br /> <br /> I really hope both of these things are valid, because I'm excited to play them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T16:10:09-07:00","id":1228699,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m actually getting interested in Howl\u2019s titular Moving Castle, Yaga Baba\u2019s chicken-legged cabin, and the Striders of Anthem.<br /> <br /> Lunars who don\u2019t sail still have a keen interest in having some kind of truck or mobile home for carrying all of their most precious followers and possessions around with them, allowing them to retreat from Wyld Hunts and remain harder to locate.<br /> <br /> As a Lunar, I could direct my mobile home to travel to a specific rendezvous point as I fly off as a bird in another direction to go on an adventure completely unburdened by my extra stuff.<br /> <br /> It might even be a mobile manse that needs to periodically return to its demesne to recharge. Perhaps there are muiltple prepared demesnses it can move between, like train stations.<br /> <br /> Yes, I have given thought to an actual moonsilver train.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T11:55:50-07:00","id":1230071,"title":"","content":"I could see the moonsilver bow highlighting individuals with moonlight or marking them with tattoos and each attack increasing what the tattoos can do to the person. Or maybe the moonlight first causing them to illuminate then attract predators or lunar themed creatures to start hunting them lol. Kind of like Jake from Adventure Time calling snakes to Finn when he played the violin. A moonsilver train would be badass! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I kind of hope the book does focus more on the new lunars because the previous ones really are raid bosses. A player meets a baby eater or a man-goat rapist is probably going to have a very limited story there. I mean those kind of stories might not even make it to some player groups and definitely could prevent certain players from even picking up the game. I just hope there is a lot more infrastructure that players can work with in place. A lunar city, with a moonsilver train <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, that allows players to explore the setting sounds way better than bringing more info about NPCs you probably don't want to meet anyway/might be hard for a ST to roleplay in a way that isn't just roll initiative.<br /> <br /> I would also kind of like a lunar base in the wyld where lunars work with fair folk and local tribes. An actual place that stands as a testament to Lunar in game mechanics to resist being forced to play in creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24292-silverwake","name":"Silverwake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T10:05:08-07:00","id":1230575,"title":"","content":"Robert Vance seems to have plans for a \u201cThousand Swords Style\u201d practiced by Sublime Danger of the Thousand Daiklave Wings.<br /> <br /> No promise that we\u2019ll get it in this book, or that it will actually let you fight with a bunch of floating swords like RWBY\u2019s Penny Polendina, BlazBlue\u2019s Murakumo Units, or League of Legends\u2019 redesign of Irelia the Blade Dancer.<br /> <br /> But here\u2019s hoping!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T13:00:02-07:00","id":1230622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1230575#post1230575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Robert Vance seems to have plans for a \u201cThousand Swords Style\u201d practiced by Sublime Danger of the Thousand Daiklave Wings.<br /> <br /> No promise that we\u2019ll get it in this book, or that it will actually let you fight with a bunch of floating swords like RWBY\u2019s Penny Polendina, BlazBlue\u2019s Murakumo Units, or League of Legends\u2019 redesign of Irelia the Blade Dancer.<br /> <br /> But here\u2019s hoping!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not currently scheduled to appear in <i>Lunars: Fangs at the Gate</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T13:25:00-07:00","id":1230628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1230622#post1230622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not currently scheduled to appear in <i>Lunars: Fangs at the Gate</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shucks<br /> <br /> At least we\u2019ll get Swaying Grass Style for one flavor of dance-fighting. <br /> <br /> And this means one more Style that might instead use axes or hammers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.co