":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T12:53:03-07:00","id":1231184,"title":"","content":"Is &quot;Fangs at the Gate&quot; the official or possibly so subtitle for the book, or just something the OP came up with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 06-29-2018, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T13:09:15-07:00","id":1231190,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar186_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"186\" data-vbnamecard=\"186\">Morty</a> it is the confirmed subtitle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T13:38:36-07:00","id":1231211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1231184#post1231184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is &quot;Fangs at the Gate&quot; the official or possibly so subtitle for the book, or just something the OP came op with?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Lunars: Fangs at the Gate </b>is the official name of the book.<br /> <br /> We've also released the names of two other upcoming books, <b>Across the Eight Directions </b>and <b>Exigents: Out of the Ashes</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T15:45:33-07:00","id":1231237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1231190#post1231190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar186_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"186\" data-vbnamecard=\"186\">Morty</a> it is the confirmed subtitle.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1231211#post1231211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Lunars: Fangs at the Gate </b>is the official name of the book.<br /> <br /> We've also released the names of two other upcoming books, <b>Across the Eight Directions </b>and <b>Exigents: Out of the Ashes</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know, thanks. I like the title. Seems to capture 3E Lunars quite well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T16:12:53-07:00","id":1231245,"title":"","content":"Speaking of things that capture the new book well, the opening fiction for the first Lunar book still works extremely well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T18:08:09-07:00","id":1231275,"title":"","content":"I've been wondering how a spell for deleterious transformations might work in Exalted.<br /> <br /> I don't really know much about the mechanics of Dungeons and Dragons in any form, so I can't comment on how they might resolve the subject, but I feel as though for Exalted it would dance uncomfortably on the razor's edge between &quot;I win button&quot; and &quot;basically useless.<br /> <br /> That might be resolved a bit by it requiring a Ritual cost, but that also seems as though it would mean that something is being lost in the translation even if the ritual doesn't need to be very long; that in a lot of fiction featuring such transformations, they have a tendency to be quick, punchy things.<br /> <br /> Mind, it also brings up a bit of an awkward question surrounding the existence of those Solar Charms with the effect of modifying the effects of curses and forced transformations and things: namely, the Charms imply the existence of such powers, so is it valid to apply them against characters (including players) who lack defences against them? Or is it really only fair to use them against players who wouldn't take the full force of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T19:48:07-07:00","id":1231286,"title":"","content":"I mean there's not much in between. You either transform them into a harmless shape or strip them of permenant traits. Since i was rereading sidereals 1e. The most definitive shaping effect I've seen is pattern spider touch. <br /> <br /> The attack first requires you to hit the target. Then roll to shape them though. Shaping defenses automatically trump them as did lunar tattoos. <br /> <br /> Making a sorcerer shape a spell then having to touch them is a lot more fair than a single roll in 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T20:16:43-07:00","id":1231290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1231286#post1231286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You either transform them into a harmless shape or strip them of permenant traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking more about the process of resolution more than the end result.<br /> <br /> The end result being a whole other can of worms; one can devise the most fair and reasonable system for turning somebody into a duck imaginable, but the end result is still somebody being turned into a duck, and it leaves the question of where the narrative goes from there.<br /> <br /> Although... considering that Lunars, in and of themselves, represent an entire class of Exalted that can turn into ducks voluntarily, the system has kind of been designed around such things being playable.<br /> <br /> New idea: a Solar turned into a duck retains a reasonable amount of their consciousness and personality, and are capable of using Charms within reason; things like Brawl, Athletics and Awareness are in, Melee and Archery not so much, social Abilities are a bit dependent. Physically, the Solar is still probably weaker, and might have functionally lower health levels and soak (a few Resistance Charms might need to be adjudicated circumstantially). A major disadvantage is social (and more than just the resolution of the influence system); the Solar's capacity to communicate is probably severely impaired (unless they should have had Charms sufficient to cross virtually all barriers), and there's a matter of how seriously people can take them.<br /> <br /> Thus, such a transformation remains deleterious, but not to the extent of taking the character out of the game entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since i was rereading sidereals 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a weird sentence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T21:54:24-07:00","id":1231299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1231290#post1231290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm talking more about the process of resolution more than the end result.<br /> <br /> The end result being a whole other can of worms; one can devise the most fair and reasonable system for turning somebody into a duck imaginable, but the end result is still somebody being turned into a duck, and it leaves the question of where the narrative goes from there.<br /> <br /> Although... considering that Lunars, in and of themselves, represent an entire class of Exalted that can turn into ducks voluntarily, the system has kind of been designed around such things being playable.<br /> <br /> New idea: a Solar turned into a duck retains a reasonable amount of their consciousness and personality, and are capable of using Charms within reason; things like Brawl, Athletics and Awareness are in, Melee and Archery not so much, social Abilities are a bit dependent. Physically, the Solar is still probably weaker, and might have functionally lower health levels and soak (a few Resistance Charms might need to be adjudicated circumstantially). A major disadvantage is social (and more than just the resolution of the influence system); the Solar's capacity to communicate is probably severely impaired (unless they should have had Charms sufficient to cross virtually all barriers), and there's a matter of how seriously people can take them.<br /> <br /> Thus, such a transformation remains deleterious, but not to the extent of taking the character out of the game entirely.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Making the effects less binary does help. It could also help to make it gradual. Slowly losing their mind rather than instantly losing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> This is a weird sentence.<br /> </div> </div> </div>I was supposed to use a comma instead of a period. Unless you're asking why I was reading it. In which case, because it was a better setting for sidereals. 2e just ripped 1e wholesale, word for word in a lot of cases, then added a bunch of text to diminish the sidereal's role in creation. I started with 2e but upon reading 1e afterwards, whoever wrote sidereals 2e didn't like them. It shows in the writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T21:59:11-07:00","id":1231301,"title":"","content":"&quot;She turned me into a newt!&quot;<br /> <br /> *staring*<br /> <br /> &quot;*defensively* I got better.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Celestial Circle Spell for turning other people into animals against their will doesn't have to be <i>permanent. </i>And transforming / shackling the target's mind is worth a spell all to itself, and so would not be included in Baleful Polymorph's effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T08:44:16-07:00","id":1231376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1231301#post1231301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;She turned me into a newt!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> *staring*<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;*defensively* I got better.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> A Celestial Circle Spell for turning other people into animals against their will doesn't have to be <i>permanent. </i>And transforming / shackling the target's mind is worth a spell all to itself, and so would not be included in Baleful Polymorph's effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I could definitely see such a spell allowing the target to daily/weekly/monthly roll their Willpower against the sorcerer's willpower/essence/occult/threshold successes to retake their form. And maybe also have a conditional thing that must be contrary to the nature of the targets defining intimacies (to keep the whole &quot;I was cursed to turn into a frog because I didnt care about other people, as a lesson in humility&quot;). Maybe they need to erode that intimacy to minor/major level or get rid of it, if they dont succeed at the willpower roll?<br /> <br /> Now that I think, this is turning into quite an interesting spell <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10762-asoral","name":"Asoral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T13:06:40-07:00","id":1231426,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about a simple expiration date, honestly. Like, an hour or a day. Cursing someone more enduringly than that might require Solar Circle Sorcery or a sorcerous working. Definitely a sorcerous working if the curse is specially tailored for the target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T15:52:20-07:00","id":1231467,"title":"","content":"I need to look back at some of the spells at some point to see similar things for comparison, but a transformation with a sharp time limit feels somewhat toothless. I don't know, maybe it's a necessary concession just to be gameable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T22:45:19-07:00","id":1231532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1231467#post1231467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need to look back at some of the spells at some point to see similar things for comparison, but a transformation with a sharp time limit feels somewhat toothless. I don't know, maybe it's a necessary concession just to be gameable.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could just go with a season, which is three months. There's also the ability to go for a year and a day. If the spell will not be bought by PC's it could just be arbitrarily for one story. The span only matters by how fast or how slow the game goes. If there are months in between or if it's all on a day to day campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T07:58:58-07:00","id":1231584,"title":"","content":"In the case of instant/indefinite, on the other hand, I think Soul Mastery is probably a good benchmark for how hard it should be to pull off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T12:22:14-07:00","id":1231900,"title":"","content":"Expiration date=30 years, which is Exalted sounds like the rest of an NPCs life <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I hope to see lunar mechanics that play well with the wyld. I know Solar's have creation power but I'd love to see a &quot;use what's there&quot; power that allows a player to declare certain aspects or even control the flow of change in those areas. Also maybe some new, crazy martial arts style that works specifically in wyld regions or regions that lunars &quot;infect&quot; with wyld magic. I feel like a style like that would allow a player to take stunting to a new level <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24292-silverwake","name":"Silverwake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T15:38:28-07:00","id":1231960,"title":"","content":"Quicksilver Hand of Dreams would remain a Sidereal Martial Art, even if it returns in Third Edition.<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted are not the Wyld Exalted. That would sooner be the Dream-Souled.<br /> <br /> That said, Robert has assured us that Lunar Exalted will have stronger powers against the Wyld than Ritual of Lunar Stability, while of course not being as powerful as Solar Wyld Shaping Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T00:23:36-07:00","id":1232060,"title":"","content":"Lunars: Fangs at the Gate is now in redlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T06:53:16-07:00","id":1232106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1232060#post1232060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars: Fangs at the Gate is now in redlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forget what that means. Would you please remind me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T07:04:02-07:00","id":1232110,"title":"","content":"I believe that's the stage where the developers (?) go through the first draft and correct stuff they feel needs correcting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T07:12:37-07:00","id":1232112,"title":"","content":"So fast. I wonder if the kickstarter might begin this month in time for my birthday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T07:53:23-07:00","id":1232120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1232112#post1232112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So fast. I wonder if the kickstarter might begin this month in time for my birthday.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first instinct is to presume you're joking, but in case you're not, Second Draft tends to linger in hell for a long while (in my observed experience, it's the longest phase) and they also don't have any art, which they'll need for the Kickstarter and some preliminary layout for the images of the book. Calling this month optimistic would be very generous indeed. I'd be surprised (and delighted) to see the KS before 2019.<br /> <br /> Still, progress is pleasing and it's good to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T08:36:25-07:00","id":1232140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1232120#post1232120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Draft tends to linger in hell for a long while (in my observed experience, it's the longest phase) and they also don't have any art, which they'll need for the Kickstarter and some preliminary layout for the images of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not aware of that, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T08:55:34-07:00","id":1232148,"title":"","content":"We're very likely to have a Kickstarter for <i>Lunars</i>, but I wouldn't expect it until next year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T14:35:48-07:00","id":1232230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1232120#post1232120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My first instinct is to presume you're joking, but in case you're not, Second Draft tends to linger in hell for a long while (in my observed experience, it's the longest phase) and they also don't have any art, which they'll need for the Kickstarter and some preliminary layout for the images of the book. Calling this month optimistic would be very generous indeed. I'd be surprised (and delighted) to see the KS before 2019.<br /> <br /> Still, progress is pleasing and it's good to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that the reason they seem to linger in Second Draft interminably is because Onyx Path doesn\u2019t have separate sections for Third, Fourth, Fifth, etc. drafts so it just stays at Second until the Devs are certain they don\u2019t want the writers to rewrite anything else, which is when it goes to development.<br /> <br /> I may very well be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T14:49:06-07:00","id":1232234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1232230#post1232230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My understanding is that the reason they seem to linger in Second Draft interminably is because Onyx Path doesn\u2019t have separate sections for Third, Fourth, Fifth, etc. drafts so it just stays at Second until the Devs are certain they don\u2019t want the writers to rewrite anything else, which is when it goes to development.<br /> <br /> I may very well be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's my understanding as well. I probably ought to have elaborated as such, but now you've done it for me. All's well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T04:09:43-07:00","id":1232825,"title":"","content":"Be on the look out for a blog post with a Lunar charm preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T10:47:48-07:00","id":1232883,"title":"","content":"They already showed off a Protean-keyworded Charm or two with Eska of the Seven Blades, with her Charms that worked better in certain animal forms.<br /> <br /> Probably, they'll want to show off Protean Charms that work better in human forms, as well as a Totemic Charm that you can acquire through a different Attribute than it normally belongs to.<br /> <br /> A healing or crafting Charm would also be nice, as Lunar Exalted have traditionally suffered in those areas.<br /> <br /> And I wouldn't say no to seeing a Wyld-related Charm that finally exceeds things like &quot;Wyld Appraisal Method&quot;, &quot;Harmony with Reality Technique&quot;, and &quot;Ritual of Lunar Stability&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T06:29:43-07:00","id":1234611,"title":"","content":"A month, and a few pages, ago, you guys were talking about moonsilver bows. The only thing that kept coming to mind as the discussion was going on was the great bow from Dark Souls. Plant it, nock the arrow, pull way back, hold it forever, practically turn bow into a .50 caliber rifle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":24134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","user":"Inertial Frame","date":".  Too early in the day. 07-13-2018, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T06:42:25-07:00","id":1234613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1234611#post1234611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A month, and a few pages, ago, you guys were talking about moonsilver bows. The only thing that kept coming to mind as the discussion was going on was the great bow from Dark Souls. Plant it, nock the arrow, pull way back, hold it forever, practically turn bow into a .50 caliber rifle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically the bow equivalent of the Tusk of Ga-Maleah, since those bows were meant to slay giant dragons. <br /> <br /> Its pinnacle evocation could involve shooting an arrow to the moon as a prayer, and being answered by a tree-sized arrow shooting back from the sky to impale your prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T09:42:34-07:00","id":1234679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1234611#post1234611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that kept coming to mind as the discussion was going on was the great bow from Dark Souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of how I imagine the standard powerbow.<br /> <br /> The manner in which they're described, at least in the Third Edition core, makes them sound a lot bigger than they're typically depicted in art.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">hold it forever</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that help?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T10:09:12-07:00","id":1234691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1234679#post1234679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does that help?</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to recall the longer one holds the arrow ready to fire, it does more damage, right? Or maybe that's just my taking time to aim. Very. Carefully. It's been a while since I've played Dark Souls.<br /> <br /> Also, side note: I'm not exactly a player, or even a reader, of Exalted, but I am intrigued by the game. I should probably start a thread about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T10:18:29-07:00","id":1234692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1234691#post1234691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall the longer one holds the arrow ready to fire, it does more damage, right? Or maybe that's just my taking time to aim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the bow is doing something magical, any increased damage from holding it at full draw longer will come from increased aim. Bows work by converting the energy that you &quot;store&quot; by bending the bow limbs into kinetic energy to the arrow once it's released. Once you've bent the bow arms as far back as you can, you're not adding any more energy to the system holding it there. But time to aim is very important! Modern compound bows are designed so that it takes notably less energy to hold the bow at full extension than it does to draw it, for exactly this reason - it's much easier to aim the bow that way, taking a few seconds to line up your shot, when your arm isn't trembling and straining with the force necessary to hold the bow at full draw.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T10:37:15-07:00","id":1234699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1234692#post1234692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless the bow is doing something magical, any increased damage from holding it at full draw longer will come from increased aim. Bows work by converting the energy that you &quot;store&quot; by bending the bow limbs into kinetic energy to the arrow once it's released. Once you've bent the bow arms as far back as you can, you're not adding any more energy to the system holding it there. But time to aim is very important! Modern compound bows are designed so that it takes notably less energy to hold the bow at full extension than it does to draw it, for exactly this reason - it's much easier to aim the bow that way, taking a few seconds to line up your shot, when your arm isn't trembling and straining with the force necessary to hold the bow at full draw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it <i>is</i> a video game bow I was referencing, so it all depends on how they built the physics engine for the great bow. I'm all for what you said, but it always appeared that the longer I waited to fire it, even on enemies not moving directly toward me, I was getting better damage results. But again, it has been awhile, so I may just be remembering things as I thought happened, not as they actually happened.<br /> <br /> Also, the more I think about eventually maybe playing Exalted sometime in the (near or far, who knows?) future, the more I really like the concept of a great bow wielding archer as artillery/support on the battlefield as a basic concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T10:38:27-07:00","id":1234700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1234691#post1234691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I seem to recall the longer one holds the arrow ready to fire, it does more damage, right? Or maybe that's just my taking time to aim. Very. Carefully. It's been a while since I've played Dark Souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Dark Souls? It's definitely only because of aiming for critical spots.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, yeah, what Kelly said.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T11:31:55-07:00","id":1234718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1234699#post1234699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it <i>is</i> a video game bow I was referencing, so it all depends on how they built the physics engine for the great bow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can definitely believe a video game engine didn't perfectly replicate actual physics. :-) If I was justifying it in my head, I'd just assume it was taking into account increasing accuracy, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the more I think about eventually maybe playing Exalted sometime in the (near or far, who knows?) future, the more I really like the concept of a great bow wielding archer as artillery/support on the battlefield as a basic concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you do get into it, (which I encourage - Ex 3rd Edition, at least, is a very good game!), you'll find that there's a <i>lot</i> of support for that role. The Archery charms basically center around doing exactly that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T13:59:27-07:00","id":1234767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1234611#post1234611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A month, and a few pages, ago, you guys were talking about moonsilver bows. The only thing that kept coming to mind as the discussion was going on was the great bow from Dark Souls. Plant it, nock the arrow, pull way back, hold it forever, practically turn bow into a .50 caliber rifle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a 50 cal? This is Exalted. .50 BMG is not particularly impressive with divine weapons shooting or cutting through tanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T14:05:21-07:00","id":1234768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1234767#post1234767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just a 50 cal? This is Exalted. .50 BMG is not particularly impressive with divine weapons shooting or cutting through tanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be because that particular reference was with respect to the Dark Souls great bow in particular, not anything in Exalted. Which, based on what you say, is about average for an average* bow with no Charms used?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *I'm assuming there's &quot;average&quot; tier items in Exalted. There may not be, but I don't know that yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T14:18:00-07:00","id":1234773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1234768#post1234768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That'd be because that particular reference was with respect to the Dark Souls great bow in particular, not anything in Exalted. Which, based on what you say, is about average for an average* bow with no Charms used?<br /> <br /> *I'm assuming there's &quot;average&quot; tier items in Exalted. There may not be, but I don't know that yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exceptional/perfect quality used to be a thing, but it led to bad places, to EX3 scrapped it. If you have a well-made mortal weapon, it just looks nice. If you want something better, you need an artifact weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T14:27:44-07:00","id":1234778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist<