"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T14:35:17-07:00","id":1234781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1234778#post1234778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exceptional Equipment is still a thing--so I think exceptional weapons are still there? They give a +1?</div> </div> </div> </div>To the dice rolls of non-Attack Abilities, if I remember right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T14:40:20-07:00","id":1234783,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you can have an exceptional disguise kit, or smith's tools, but an exceptional sword just looks really nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T06:47:08-07:00","id":1234931,"title":"","content":"An exceptional weapon could give a bonus to things other than hitting people with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T07:13:11-07:00","id":1234941,"title":"","content":"Do you figure that the Lunar book may include Second Circle Demons, since Lunar Exalted can summon and bind those as a pretty strong and useful advantage against the Dragon-Blooded?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T07:59:37-07:00","id":1234956,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I assume not, because it's a Lunar book, not a demon book. The stats for more Lunar elders seem more likely, looking at the one previous example.<br /> But, saying that, it does sound like a good idea. And the Lunar book is unlikely to include 8 martial arts and 11 artefact weapons, so there may be room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T09:03:40-07:00","id":1234977,"title":"","content":"WFHW didn't have any 1cds, so probably not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T09:25:01-07:00","id":1234983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1234977#post1234977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WFHW didn't have any 1cds, so probably not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point.<br /> <br /> One little thing I'm looking forward to is a Lunar medical diagnosis Charm. Dragon-Blooded didn't used to have one either, but the current writers found an appropriate mechanic distinct from Flawless Diagnosis Technique's &quot;you can't botch&quot;. The Terrestrial diagnosis Charm doesn't prevent you from botching, but speeds up the diagnosis like the Solar Charm and, if you succeed, you gain a Specialty in treating the ailment. Which of course plays well with Dragon-Blooded dice-adding limits.<br /> <br /> I want Charms that help Lunars detect weaknesses; the better to help or destroy someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T10:11:05-07:00","id":1234995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://mustachedmrblender.tumblr.com/post/175838323758/bugs-bunny-could-singlehandedly-defeat-thanos-by\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mustachedmrblender.tumblr.com/post/175838323758/bugs-bunny-could-singlehandedly-defeat-thanos-by\" target=\"_blank\"> Not found. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mustachedmrblender.tumblr.com/post/175838323758/bugs-bunny-could-singlehandedly-defeat-thanos-by\" target=\"_blank\"> http://mustachedmrblender.tumblr.com/post/175838323758/bugs-bunny-could-singlehandedly-defeat-thanos-by </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> With the Lunar ability to become a battle-group, to assume different shapes, and to outright lie to someone and have them believe it, I feel like a high-level Lunar could pull this trick off if they wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:56:57-07:00","id":1236433,"title":"","content":"All right, I believe that this is the most appropriate place to continue this conversation:<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236425#post1236425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the lack of supernal will go a long way to making solars come out ahead in the early game.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1236152-on-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1236425#post1236425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Even if the charms are equal, lunars and sids will be limited by essence prerequisites. So a solar who can pull out essence 5 charms from the get go will be stronger. </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I speculate that part of the basis for comparison might be possible diversity in options that a Lunar might get for the same level of character investment, as well as some things that Solars simply don't do directly. I think a comparison between an Essence 1 Lunar and an Essence 1 Solar that has some Essence 3 or higher Charms in a combat Ability needs to account for the capacity of the former to turn into something small and fast and maybe capable of flight if a battle starts to go south.<br /> <br /> Applying a similar logic to the subject of what different characters might do when faced with the same problems, if the comparison isn't in the form of direct competition. A Supernal Larceny Solar might get earlier access to some powerful Charms for infiltration, subterfuge and disguise, while a Lunar gets things providing similar developments by default (which is also the case for every Lunar regardless of Caste, and encompasses a capacity to get things with, say, persistent bonus dice that don't cost motes).</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T09:12:50-07:00","id":1236436,"title":"","content":"Solars get Supernals.<br /> <br /> Lunars get shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m a mother ducking T-REX!\u201d<br /> <br /> Frankly, if the Solars didn\u2019t have Supernals, it just wouldn\u2019t be fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T09:18:49-07:00","id":1236440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1236436#post1236436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars get Supernals.<br /> <br /> Lunars get shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m a mother ducking T-REX!\u201d<br /> <br /> Frankly, if the Solars didn\u2019t have Supernals, it just wouldn\u2019t be fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shit, even turning into a bear <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/personal-experiences-1584-6-things-you-learn-being-mauled-by-bears.html\" target=\"_blank\">is enough to ruin someone's day.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-18-2018, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T09:51:57-07:00","id":1236449,"title":"","content":"Both I and another Lunar player I play with have often used bear forms for combat: it's a nice bonus to soak and damage, and they can fit into corridors and rooms, unlike tyrant lizards.*<br /> <br /> *And that's why the Night+Changing Moon's bedroom needed extensive work done. Also the room above. And below.<br /> <br /> But yeah, turning into various forms is a big power boost for a starting Lunar, but one that gets a bit less useful as you go up in XP and get better stats your self.<br /> So a bit like Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T09:54:42-07:00","id":1236450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1236449#post1236449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But yeah, turning into various forms is a big power boost for a starting Lunar, but one that gets a bit less useful as you go up in XP and get better stats your self.<br /> So a bit like Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on what the benefits of Protean Charms are, and how they play out as Essence grows. It may well be that shapeshifting produces a better result for a high-Essence Lunar than it does for a weaker one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T11:25:32-07:00","id":1236491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1236440#post1236440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shit, even turning into a bear <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/personal-experiences-1584-6-things-you-learn-being-mauled-by-bears.html\" target=\"_blank\">is enough to ruin someone's day.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Golden Kamuy is also full of extensively-researched Ainu lore on bears. Volume 2 also has the infamous &quot;guy gets face torn off like a swiveling door by bear mother's claw swipe&quot; scene, as well as mention of rikosinot, which is where a bear mauls someone and tosses them up into the air; they often end up disemboweled and strung along some high tree branches as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:20:05-07:00","id":1236533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1236450#post1236450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That depends on what the benefits of Protean Charms are, and how they play out as Essence grows. It may well be that shapeshifting produces a better result for a high-Essence Lunar than it does for a weaker one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite possibly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T02:05:59-07:00","id":1239229,"title":"","content":"Hmm,<br /> Ever since I read both Glories of the Most High: TUS/Luna, I've been asking myself &quot;Why is the *Lunar* MA not lunar-phase focused, when the Solar style Arms of the Unconquered Sun managed to be solar-phased conceptually, just by dint of the Solar castes?&quot;<br /> <br /> White Reaper NEVER thrilled me. Maybe that was because it was so singularly not-useful. (An MA that specializes on greasing soft-targets, in order to blow its built-up wad in one shot, misses entirely the point why someone would be using a Celestial MA). While I don't dispute its validity as a conceptual style, I HATED the idea of White Reaper as THE Lunar MA-style. Thematically, the fact there isn't a moon-phase based MA feels like a major oversight to me.<br /> <br /> Disregarding the 2E strength-level of Arms of the Unconquered Sun, the thing I really loved about it was the alternate-Form Type Charms. The idea of different Form-types for the lunar phases essentially allows the MA to split for the Castes, who can all stamp their influence on it. (I don't know a great deal about EX3, but I DO know there has not yet been an MA in Exalted I could really say was Lunar-oriented, before anything else. Even the Animal styles have seemed fairly well dominated by the Solars.<br /> <br /> Thematically, does anyone else think a moon-phase themes MA might be a nice idea for a Lunar MA?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T10:00:46-07:00","id":1239350,"title":"","content":"Doesn't grab me, but seems fine.<br /> <br /> Certainly it's more &quot;Lunar-y&quot; than White Reaper. I never really got why White Reaper was the &quot;Lunar style&quot;. There's nothing particularly Lunar-y about it (other than it has some charms based on physical attributes, so they're reasonably good at it).<br /> <br /> Honestly though, if any styles should be the &quot;Lunar styles&quot;, I feel it should be the animal styles.<br /> <br /> (I'm also fine with there not being any distinctly Lunar styles. Or Solar styles.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T10:05:04-07:00","id":1239353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239229#post1239229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm,<br /> Thematically, does anyone else think a moon-phase themes MA might be a nice idea for a Lunar MA?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, could be pretty cool.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T10:52:40-07:00","id":1239371,"title":"","content":"I tried to write one back in Second Edition, after Glories. Tried.<br /> <br /> It was a dualistic Style, drawing inspiration from Luna as a hunter and seductress. Either you were retreating from your enemies and luring them blindly after you, or you were chasing them down and attacking without any possibility of escape.<br /> <br /> Or someone could just learn Dreaming Pearl Courtesan and Tiger Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T11:46:56-07:00","id":1239387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239350#post1239350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't grab me, but seems fine.<br /> <br /> Certainly it's more &quot;Lunar-y&quot; than White Reaper. I never really got why White Reaper was the &quot;Lunar style&quot;. There's nothing particularly Lunar-y about it (other than it has some charms based on physical attributes, so they're reasonably good at it).<br /> <br /> Honestly though, if any styles should be the &quot;Lunar styles&quot;, I feel it should be the animal styles.<br /> <br /> (I'm also fine with there not being any distinctly Lunar styles. Or Solar styles.)</div> </div> </div> </div>White Reaper's been associated with Lilith since First Edition, which is probably why it was included in Glories: Luna. I'm not sure whether <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zaraborgstrom/SadIvoryDeath\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna invented the name</a> or if it appeared somewhere else; I don't think it shows up in <b>Exalted: the Lunars</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T12:41:05-07:00","id":1239406,"title":"","content":"It doesn't. It remarks on First Age battle techniques she invented and used on a Ahn-Ahru and Jorst. With white cape furling. But the first mention of White Reaper came from that Jenna Moran forum post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T12:43:37-07:00","id":1239409,"title":"","content":"Huh, I didn't know that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T13:45:59-07:00","id":1239428,"title":"","content":"How's this:<br /> Not going to try doing an MA write-up here, but Five Faces of Luna seems like a lovely name. The Glories stuff on Luna's aspects is a treasure trove both thematically and to inform Charm design. The Bloody Huntress for the hurt-em Charms, the Walker at the Crossroads for some Gambit-related action, the White Navigator for the obligatory precision-related stuff. For increased thematic utility, one could always dig into the alternate-Lunas mentioned.<br /> <br /> The Animal-style stuff gets dominated by the general wuxia theme. They're never going to be something identifiable as &quot;Lunar-y&quot;...I think an argument I read somewhere was &quot;Why would Lunars try to pretend to be animals with their MA, when they can become animals?&quot; Conceptually, I can kind of see the point here. It's too....obvious, to make the Lunar MA any one animal. The reason I like going back to Luna is how well she embodies the protean nature of the Lunars. Plus, I could totally see such an MA retained by Elder Lunar priests and priestesses of Luna, and passed on as a means of memorializing Castes that aren't coming back. I've heard a lot about how the Lunars have moved on from their old castes, and I don't object to that, but there would be individuals who yearned for the days of yore. An MA that embodies what was, can express that longing, without being indicative of any push to bring it back. The MA itself would be an IC argument not to try. &quot;We retained the best of what was in our art, and now we are free to decide anew what shall be.&quot;<br /> <br /> I also DESPERATELY want something &quot;civilized&quot; isn't the right word, &quot;refined&quot; maybe? Something spiritual, with antique roots, as a call-out to the days when Lunars WEREN'T as savage as they are now. It wouldn't be exceptionally popular in iconoclast circles, but White Reaper was supposed to be an ancient and almost-vanished art from the First Age. The cultural and spiritual connections provide a good argument for why it hasn't gone the way of White Reaper.<br /> <br /> Edit: The thing I didn't like about White Reaper was called out pretty well in the unofficial Lunar Castebooks. The story where Desus has Lilith enter the Heaven and Earth Invitational, getting her to throw her match for a vote in the Deliberative. Lilith objects, saying her White Reaper style isn't a dueling style. It's meant to make a martial artist a one-man-army. The developers linked it to the Swords of Luna, giving essentially hobgoblin masses as the premier target the MA was used on, but I wanted something more than &quot;Anti-Faerie Mooks MA.&quot; Especially in the signature Lunar style. I get that MA isn't the Lunar focus, but adaptability is, and this is a wuxia world. One means of adaptation is definitely having your own MA. More importantly, Celestial MA finds the most practical use against singular, or at most small groups of &quot;hard&quot; targets. When you think of the times you were playing, when did your character want their ass-kicking to be at its peak? The idea an entire group of Celestial Exalts in a wuxia-theme Creation never developed their own &quot;dueling&quot; style boggles my mind, frankly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","user":"Wyldwraith","date":". 07-27-2018, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T14:09:38-07:00","id":1239433,"title":"","content":"Paraphrasing Minton a bit from Discord. There isn't a general MA culture among Lunars because that's a PC route to create one of your own. A young Lunar seeking to re-establish Five Faces of Luna Style definitely sounds like a grand endeavor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T15:47:53-07:00","id":1239464,"title":"","content":"Eh I disagree with the fact that no general culture means no native Style.<br /> Someone like Ingosh Silverclaws as an ancient Priest of Luna acting as the wellspring from which the Style flowed into the hands of younger Lunars gives the Style a legacy cachet. I am inherently opposed to the Lunars retaining nothing meaningful of their past. White Reaper doesn't do the job, because frankly it isn't a good MA. A mechanical redesign that greatly increases its utility does nothing to make it feel more &quot;Lunar-y.&quot;<br /> <br /> Some of us Lunar guys/gals already aren't in love with the tribal tag the Exaltation can't seem to escape. A MEANINGFUL relic from the past would go a long way towards sweetening the bitter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:23:48-07:00","id":1239486,"title":"","content":"I just had the epiphany that a Lunar Elder Chimera, with Squid and Pterodactyl totems, would be a hella good Cthulhu stand in. And am now making that a character at some point. (Elder for the power.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24378\" data-vbnamecard=\"24378\">Wyldwraith</a> I'd agree...if anyone had native styles these days. White Reaper's good--man I've seen some murders with it, since 'team up on him' is a good way to take down most opponents--but also, no one in my 3e group made the connection to Lunars. Five Faces is a good name---I kinda wanna see it use crescent weapons? Scimitars, sabres, etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:30:59-07:00","id":1239487,"title":"","content":"I don't see the point of non-sidereal celestials getting into Martial arts at present. Brawl seems like a way better investment for celestials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:33:01-07:00","id":1239490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239487#post1239487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the point of non-sidereal celestials getting into Martial arts at present.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Black Claw Style is cool.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:37:43-07:00","id":1239492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239490#post1239490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because Black Claw Style is cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a fine style but without hero styles, MA feels like you kind of gimp yourself to brawl. It kind of sucks that there aren't any custom MA charms for celestials.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:37:51-07:00","id":1239493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239487#post1239487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the point of non-sidereal celestials getting into Martial arts at present. Brawl seems like a way better investment for celestials.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've enjoyed MA's usually for case by case reasons or character statements.With Solar Brawl (I haven't read DB Brawl in a bit), there isn't that sense of <i>style</i> for lack of a better word, and mechancially the unarmed effects, stacked on top of each other, can be terrifying (I'm lead to believe--Tiger+Some White Reaper+Snake looks damn scary from over here).<br /> <br /> I enjoyed my brawl character partly to eschew elegance, and just be brutal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:42:34-07:00","id":1239497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239486#post1239486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Elder for the power.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that being insanely-old is probably more significant for the <i>perspective</i> that such advanced age and prolonged exposure to a vast world that doesn't give a shit about humanity provides. Having become more than a little detached from the notions we mayfly beings hold so dear to, <i>that</i> seems more key to the whole notion of cosmic horror than putting a 6 on the Essence part of their character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:45:17-07:00","id":1239499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239493#post1239493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've enjoyed MA's usually for case by case reasons or character statements.With Solar Brawl (I haven't read DB Brawl in a bit), there isn't that sense of <i>style</i> for lack of a better word, and mechancially the unarmed effects, stacked on top of each other, can be terrifying (I'm lead to believe--Tiger+Some White Reaper+Snake looks damn scary from over here).<br /> <br /> I enjoyed my brawl character partly to eschew elegance, and just be brutal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the benefit of it is that you can stunt it as any kind of style. Stacking MA is an issue for me because it has the same disjointed feeling. How many MA you can practice before it just feels like whatever?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:49:21-07:00","id":1239501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239497#post1239497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that being insanely-old is probably more significant for the <i>perspective</i> that such advanced age and prolonged exposure to a vast world that doesn't give a shit about humanity provides. Having become more than a little detached from the notions we mayfly beings hold so dear to, <i>that</i> seems more key to the whole notion of cosmic horror than putting a 6 on the Essence part of their character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair! Big C lacks visible effects to reference. But given that we are getting Lunars at E6, I'd peg him there for similair reasons (I'd make him old by First Age standards...a veteran of the Niobaaran war maybe?)<br /> Mini Cthulhu is my first lunar now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:50:16-07:00","id":1239502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcod