user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:57:45-07:00","id":1239504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239502#post1239502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean....Solar Brawl won't let me poison people with my essence fangs or do pressure points. I think this might be a different threat topic though...</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose my point was that lunars seem to have less incentive than solars to get into MA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T18:00:28-07:00","id":1239505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239504#post1239504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose my point was that lunars seem to have less incentive than solars to get into MA.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Back on topic--I do wonder how Brawl-y charms will look, especailly since Lunars can add their attribute excellency to their attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T18:17:34-07:00","id":1239508,"title":"","content":"My desire for something like the suggested Five Faces of Luna isn't simply a mechanical one. Some of us Lunar-centric folks are NEVER going to love the core take on Lunars as in-opposition-to Exalts. The tribal stuff gets equally tiresome, and primal howls in their souls plays right into the Lunars-as-savages that seems the inescapable fate of Lunars from a setting-point perspective. Fine, do that with your general design stuff, but give us dissenters some relics from the more civilized times, because some of us really DON'T want to have anything to do with the Ma-ha-suchi model of Lunar.<br /> <br /> In seven years playing Exalted, leaving aside persona-details, I can tell you that over ninety percent of actual Lunar PCs I've been Storyteller for (admittedly only among fourteen people, fifteen including myself) have had something in common. Prey's Skin Disguise, Flickering Star Infusion, and Evading the Spider's Eye. Why? Sidereal-repellent, so one could actually play a Lunar somewhere besides the wilderness of the deep (insert Direction). Why? Because mixed groups that are primarily Solar PCs don't want to be focused at the edges of Creation, or in some specific territory to the exclusion of widely traveling.<br /> <br /> Don't mistake me, I love the concept of the Lunar Dominions. I've been saying their like should've existed since 1E. There's just always been this Lunars = Wilderness calculation, when in my experience, many of the people most interested in Lunars AREN'T interested in wilderness. I am NOT saying the focus of the splat should be altered to tastes of what's likely a minority, but I believe a few nods to those of us not interested in Primal Scream Lunars won't kill things for others.<br /> <br /> Relics of the civilized past don't threaten the present of Lunar focus. They can exist side by side with the contemporary elements without threatening them, and at the same time, give those of us who want to roleplay more urban, civilized Lunars something to anchor characters to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T23:27:48-07:00","id":1239576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239464#post1239464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh I disagree with the fact that no general culture means no native Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly disagree with any idea that it means one couldn't or shouldn't have chosen/developed Martial Arts Styles that would be particularly evocative of the character archetypes that people buy the Lunars book to play.<br /> <br /> People want to play Sun Wukong? Give them Monkey Style. But that's not happening for some reason.<br /> <br /> People want to play Conan and other Hulking Barbarian Warriors? Or at least provide their Dragon-Blooded games with antagonists straight out of <i>Warcraft's</i> Horde of Shaman Orcs and Shapeshifting Tauren Druids? Give Lunars one of those rare, <i>rare</i> Martial Arts Styles that uses two-handed heavy-weight weapons, especially axes and hammers.<br /> <br /> People want to play the Drunken Oni? Well, we <i>might</i> be getting Seven Drunken Gods Style.<br /> <br /> People want to play a former slave who escaped or rose up against her captors? We <i>will</i> be getting Swaying Grass Style, and while Blanka's connection to capoeira has always been thin, someone out there might have always wanted to play an Elena who can turn into animals. And we can't forget <i>Magi's</i> Morgana.<br /> <br /> I suppose Centipede Style is for assassins, if the Single Point Shining into the Void, Tiger, Snake, Ebon Shadow, Black Claw, White Veil, and Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Styles didn't already cover some particular flavor of assassin. (Air Dragon, too, and to some extent Wood Dragon.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Other than the fully-official debut of Swaying Grass and Centipede Styles, and some &quot;new but not entirely&quot; Style that might be Seven Drunken Gods (as the descendant of the defunct Orgiastic Fugitive Style), we know there's going to be one totally new animal-based Style.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's Wolf Style, that emulates the ripping teeth of a wolf pack with throwing hatchets?<br /> <br /> Maybe it's Tyrant Lizard Style, that uses a two-handed axe or hammer to emulate the weighty head and horrifying jaws of the Tyrant Lizard while maybe incorporating kicks and stomps as the Tyrant Lizard does with its talons and tail?<br /> <br /> Maybe it's Bear or Elephant or Rhinoceros Style, or whatever animal it takes to use a weapon more weighty and also more widespread than hook swords and seven-section staves.<br /> <br /> Whatever it is, it will be at least somewhat compatible with Centipede Style. Which, in Second Edition, used... hook swords and seven-section staves. The later of which I could see, but the former of which made no fucking sense.<br /> <br /> But hey, I don't see why Snake Style uses hook swords instead of spears, either. I mean, the Style doesn't emphasize or support disarming gambits -- it would rather paralyze your arm than go directly for your weapon. Also, an awkward hook cannot possibly be as natural to the Style's extreme focus on extremely fast, accurate, soak-piercing, jabbing attacks. A spear would also fit with &quot;striking from outside of your opponent's reach&quot;, which is what Uncoiling Serpent Prana does. Javelins and spears could be thrown, and the Style distinct encourages an investment in Dodge (and thus Disengaging) through Serpentine Evasion and the Terrestrial version of Crippling Pressure-Point Strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T23:46:26-07:00","id":1239580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239576#post1239576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People want to play Sun Wukong? Give them Monkey Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just curious here, have you read <i>The Journey to the West</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T00:58:41-07:00","id":1239596,"title":"","content":"While I'd be fine with Monkey style going in the book (though I don't think it's as interesting as Centipede style, or some other potential styles), Alucard is right, Sun Wukong doesn't fight like someone using Monkey style at all.<br /> He fights with a size-changing wrackstaff, plus powers like making copies of himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T01:56:28-07:00","id":1239603,"title":"","content":"Getting down to brass tacks,<br /> Lunars shouldn't have to &quot;make do&quot; with an MA we can sort of squint and fudge into a concept. Yes, yes, I have heard all the live-long-day how MA is the Sidereal Thing (tm). They get an entire level of Reality Haxx-Bullshit MA. That makes the MA-is-Sidereal-first position, period, and moving ON. Am I mistaken that Solars will AGAIN be getting into the Sidereal cookie jar? If so, they're taken care of. Why do Lunars have to be the red-headed step-sisters with regards to MA in a wuxia-dominated game?<br /> <br /> Now I'm hearing it's possible SIDEREALS will be better at SORCERY than Lunars this Edition? I refuse to even get mad about that blasphemy, because it will simply never be reality in any game I have anything to do with. The Lunars-as-Lowest of Celestial Exalts...it gets old, it really does.<br /> <br /> Where is this coming from? I want you to actually look at the difference in quality that went into Arms of the Unconquered Sun, versus White Reaper, last edition. Lunars have had to deal with the &quot;anything you can do, we can do better, except shape-shifting, but hey, form-lock.&quot; I KNOW rescue is on the way in many ways, this edition, and I'm OVERJOYED.<br /> <br /> I just don't think I'm asking too much, when I ask someone actually design an MA style conceptually to FIT Lunars, that any other Splat can take. Some MA-love, for ONCE, in Wuxia-Land, would feel really, really nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T02:54:17-07:00","id":1239613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239603#post1239603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting down to brass tacks,<br /> Now I'm hearing it's possible SIDEREALS will be better at SORCERY than Lunars this Edition? I refuse to even get mad about that blasphemy, because it will simply never be reality in any game I have anything to do with. The Lunars-as-Lowest of Celestial Exalts...it gets old, it really does.<br /> <br /> Where is this coming from? I want you to actually look at the difference in quality that went into Arms of the Unconquered Sun, versus White Reaper, last edition. Lunars have had to deal with the &quot;anything you can do, we can do better, except shape-shifting, but hey, form-lock.&quot; I KNOW rescue is on the way in many ways, this edition, and I'm OVERJOYED.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so pound for pound lunars and sidereals are gonna be equal at sorcery in terms of what they can actually do, <i>but</i> lunars don't get favoured abilities, which means they can't get spells at a discount like sidereals can, which means they're <i>arguably </i> a <i>little </i>worse at it.<br /> <br /> On the other hand they are gonna get necromancy up to the second circle (placing them narrowly behind solars in that for the same reason they're narrowly behind sids in sorcery) and also apparently a couple of charms that let them multi task while casting and store sorcerous motes to use later. <br /> <br /> As for MA, it helps if you realise that a lunar taking a martial art but no charms in it is in an almost identical situation to a lunar who takes brawl or melee. The only difference is that they can then buy <i>additional </i>charms to use to fight things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T03:30:42-07:00","id":1239616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239492#post1239492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a fine style but without hero styles, MA feels like you kind of gimp yourself to brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you <i>read</i> Single Point Shining Into the Void's Mastery effects?!<br /> <br /> Solars get the Mastery keyword, Lunars will probably get some variation on the unique capacity to combo their Attribute combat Charms with Martial Arts, and Sidereals will get whatever neat thing is coming to them (in addition to Sidereal Styles).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T03:32:16-07:00","id":1239617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239596#post1239596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alucard is right, Sun Wukong doesn't fight like someone using Monkey style at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>While both of these clauses <i>are</i> correct, I didn't say that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T03:32:23-07:00","id":1239618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I refuse to even get mad about that blasphemy</span></i></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>This is really weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T04:41:27-07:00","id":1239627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239613#post1239613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so pound for pound lunars and sidereals are gonna be equal at sorcery in terms of what they can actually do, <i>but</i> lunars don't get favoured abilities, which means they can't get spells at a discount like sidereals can, which means they're <i>arguably </i> a <i>little </i>worse at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Have the devs said that? Because not favouring abilities never stopped them getting the favoured/caste discount on spells in the previous edition. Why would it?<br /> (My 2nd ed No Moon Celestial sorcerer had Int 4 and Occult 3. I think he favoured Brawl.)<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I may well just start the game with like 12 spells at character creation anyway, which is frankly enough (as the Lunar charms isn't out for a while, but spells are) but I'd be a little miffed if I have to pay more than Sidereals for Celestial spells. It doesn't make a huge difference, as honestly there's not that many Celestial spells I really want (unless a whole bunch of cool ones come out in Lunars, which I guess they probably will), but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-28-2018, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T05:07:38-07:00","id":1239630,"title":"","content":"Given the overall mystical bent of Sidereals, I wouldn't find it out of place for them to have a few Occult Charms that interact distinctly with sorcery in a similar manner to Terrestrials. Lunars might not have such.<br /> <br /> Histrionic anxiety over this constituting some kind of slight to Lunars or their players is still uncalled for; having certain things that they're not the best at does not constitute them being patently inferior, and their shapeshifting alone already constitutes a number of improved benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T05:24:45-07:00","id":1239637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239603#post1239603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do Lunars have to be the red-headed step-sisters with regards to MA in a wuxia-dominated game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how many prominent, powerful figures in the setting are redheads, from Rudhira to the Scarlet Empress, I'd think that the stereotypes regarding red-haired people would be drastically different in Creation.<br /> <br /> (Also, considering how the single most dominant culture in Creation is both matriarchal and matrilineal\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T06:16:50-07:00","id":1239653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239627#post1239627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? Have the devs said that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they have. It's still subject to change though. <br /> <br /> From the podcast previews, it does seem like what lunars do get are a number of sorcery-like effects in their native charm set. They can make clothes that grant you a mutation when you wear them, for example, which is even usable by mortals because it costs a WP. For any other splat that would probably be require a working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T06:22:18-07:00","id":1239656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239653#post1239653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the podcast previews, it does seem like what lunars do get are a number of sorcery-like effects in their native charm set. They can make clothes that grant you a mutation when you wear them, for example, which is even usable by mortals because it costs a WP. For any other splat that would probably be require a working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh yes, I remember a few other things like that. Granting mutations, or forcibly turning people into things as well, I think. Probably playing up some of the &quot;witchcraft&quot; angle.<br /> <br /> Mind, Sidereals probably also get Charms that are a bit sorcerous in their aspect, but in a different manner and direction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T06:57:47-07:00","id":1239665,"title":"","content":"They also have charms that directly interact with Sorcery like what DBs have. One that lets you store sorcerous motes in your anima, and another that lets you flurry a non-attack action with a shape sorcery action as you allow your shadow to cast the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T07:50:16-07:00","id":1239680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239630#post1239630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Histrionic anxiety over this constituting some kind of slight to Lunars or their players is still uncalled for; having certain things that they're not the best at does not constitute them being patently inferior, and their shapeshifting alone already constitutes a number of improved benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not, like, furious about it, but it just seems odd to me that No Moon sorcerers should pay more XP for spells than the Chosen of Secrets. I'd expect them to pay the same.<br /> I suppose there's the same issue with Martial Arts, which presumably also don't get any reduction anymore. But then, Martial Arts combines with Lunar charms in a way that it doesn't with Sidereal/Solar brawl or melee charms. I'm not seeing an obvious combo between Lunar charms and sorcery.<br /> <br /> Saying this, I'd probably prefer to take a bunch of weird magical sorcery-esque Lunar charms than many spells, because I've seen a lot of the spells before, often. It just, I don't know, seems weird to me that No Moons have to pay more for spells than they do for Intelligence charms. And it'd certainly discourage me from playing a Lunar sorcerer when Lunar charms are cheaper than spells (which is awkward, as I already have a Lunar sorcerer waiting around for rules, but then, I'm not sure I want to bring him back anyway), at least without being a bit shenanigan-y and just starting with all the Terrestrial spells I'd ever want (since you don't really need a ton: my old sorcerer had 7 terrestrial spells and 4 celestial spells).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-28-2018, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T08:03:11-07:00","id":1239687,"title":"","content":"Aren't spells more expensive than Solar Charms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T08:15:17-07:00","id":1239691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239680#post1239680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not, like, furious about it, but it just seems odd to me that No Moon sorcerers should pay more XP for spells than the Chosen of Secrets. I'd expect them to pay the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably to compensate for the fact that a Chosen of secrets has less occult charms to get. I mean even if you doubled it, a No Moon will have way more occult charms than a sidereal. Especially due to a closed charmset.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T08:30:41-07:00","id":1239699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239687#post1239687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't spells more expensive than Solar Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean, for Solars? No, they're the same. For Solars, charms, Martial Arts and spells are all 10, or 8 if favoured. Evocations are just 10 though, you can't favour them.<br /> Spells cost more for Dragonblood though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's probably to compensate for the fact that a Chosen of secrets has less occult charms to get. I mean even if you doubled it, a No Moon will have way more occult charms than a sidereal. Especially due to a closed charmset. </div> </div> </div>Sidereals have infinity times more Occult charms than Lunars.<br /> <br /> If you mean charms that use Occult in the dice roll, I have no idea who'll have more. I don't really see what that has to do with sorcery anyway. I mean, there's sorcery-specific charms I guess, of which Lunars have two. <br /> (The same number as Dragonblood have, actually. I wouldn't like to read a pattern into it, but I wouldn't be surprised if Sidereals had 1-3 sorcery-buffing charms.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T08:41:09-07:00","id":1239701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239699#post1239699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals have infinity times more Occult charms than Lunars.<br /> <br /> If you mean charms that use Occult in the dice roll, I have no idea who'll have more. I don't really see what that has to do with sorcery anyway. I mean, there's sorcery-specific charms I guess, of which Lunars have two.<br /> (The same number as Dragonblood have, actually. I wouldn't like to read a pattern into it, but I wouldn't be surprised if Sidereals had 1-3 sorcery-buffing charms.)</div> </div> </div> </div> In 2e they had 5 actual charms and 2 circles of sorcery for a total of 7 charms. Even if you doubled or tripled the sidereal charmset you'd still get a faction of what the other Charmsets get. I doubt Sidereals will get that many sorcery buffing charms but who knows with the current speed bump charm approach 3e has. Either way a lunar has got to have way more options than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T09:06:57-07:00","id":1239708,"title":"","content":"Tbh, I'm expecting Sidereals to get just as many charms in their book as everyone else. Perhaps still with the rule against custom charms, but I'd be very surprised if the devs wrote a lot less Occult charms for Sidereals than they did for Dragonblood.<br /> So I cannot see that Lunars will have more sorcery-boosting charms than Sidereals. Even if they did, it'd be 1-2 more, because they have 2 sorcery-boosting charms. That's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T09:20:20-07:00","id":1239709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239708#post1239708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh, I'm expecting Sidereals to get just as many charms in their book as everyone else. Perhaps still with the rule against custom charms, but I'd be very surprised if the devs wrote a lot less Occult charms for Sidereals than they did for Dragonblood.<br /> So I cannot see that Lunars will have more sorcery-boosting charms than Sidereals. Even if they did, it'd be 1-2 more, because they have 2 sorcery-boosting charms. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be surprised if the devs ruined the sidereal charmset by adding a bunch of inelegant speed bump charms. The sideral charmset is supposed to not only be closed but efficient to make up for the lack of growth. It should be a lot tighter and smaller than the rest of the charmsets, to make up for it's lack of growth. An open charmset, means that you can easily expand on sorcery boosting charms various ways. Lunars should have sorcery boosting charms that are much weirder and unique to them. They aren't just limited to 1-2 charms. That's the luxury of an open charmset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T09:32:44-07:00","id":1239713,"title":"","content":"Well I don't imagine writers approach any charmset with the intention of adding inelegant speed bump charms. The Dragonblood charmset, for example, has 24 Occult charms. I don't really think any of them are inelegant speed-bump charms, to be honest. Some aren't that powerful, but then, they are Dragonblood.<br /> I'd be very shocked if Sidereals still only had like 7 Occult charms. I'd be rather surprised if they had less than 15, honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T09:38:19-07:00","id":1239714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239713#post1239713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I don't imagine writers approach any charmset with the intention of adding inelegant speed bump charms. The Dragonblood charmset, for example, has 24 Occult charms. I don't really think any of them are inelegant speed-bump charms, to be honest. Some aren't that powerful, but then, they are Dragonblood.<br /> I'd be very shocked if Sidereals still only had like 7 Occult charms. I'd be rather surprised if they had less than 15, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be surprised the opposite way. However, my point is lunars can still just build on what they have or branch out in more directions. I think that makes up for having to pay slightly more for spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 07-28-2018, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T09:42:51-07:00","id":1239717,"title":"","content":"Just because you don't like the way a thing is presented doesn't make it a speed bump, nor does its addition necessarily ruin something. <br /> <br /> I would never bite into a yellow onion like an apple, but thin saut\u00e9ed slices of it make a great addition to an omelette or sandwich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-28-2018, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T09:44:55-07:00","id":1239719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239714#post1239714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, my point is lunars can still just build on what they have or branch out in more directions. I think that makes up for having to pay slightly more for charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely don't.<br /> <br /> But... there's not really much for us to discuss there. It's just a matter of opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T09:47:29-07:00","id":1239720,"title":"","content":"Well, I think the idea is that custom sidereal charms get retconned into canon such that they always existed, or else there's some sort of bureaucratic process involving the maidens to add a newly designed one to the set.<br /> <br /> Either way, in practice what sidereals don't have is <i>unique, personal</i> charms. A solar can do a thing, and it could be that no other solar can copy them. But if a sidereal has a charm, then <i>all</i> sidereals can get that charm.<br /> <br /> In fact, the only real way a sid can get a unique &quot;charm&quot; is via evocations, which they are notably bad at. Which sort of reinforces the theme even more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T10:11:38-07:00","id":1239722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239720#post1239720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think the idea is that custom sidereal charms get retconned into canon such that they always existed, or else there's some sort of bureaucratic process involving the maidens to add a newly designed one to the set.<br /> <br /> Either way, in practice what sidereals don't have is <i>unique, personal</i> charms. A solar can do a thing, and it could be that no other solar can copy them. But if a sidereal has a charm, then <i>all</i> sidereals can get that charm.<br /> <br /> In fact, the only real way a sid can get a unique &quot;charm&quot; is via evocations, which they are notably bad at. Which sort of reinforces the theme even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really isn't part of the topic just that Lunars will definitely have advantages towards magic sidereals don't. Just by dint of the ability to improve on them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T10:22:01-07:00","id":1239723,"title":"","content":"I never liked the five personae of Luna from Second Edition. I felt that, first of all, Luna would have WAY many more interpretations by the mortals of Creation than those five, and secondly, she would be far more variable about her appearance and demeanor when appearing to each of her new Chosen.<br /> <br /> Since Luna is expected to appear only once in most Lunar games, and then only if you roleplay your Exaltation experience, this seemed like a waste of wordcount and artwork to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T10:23:22-07:00","id":1239725,"title":"","content":"Isn't it supposed to represent the phases of the moon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 07-28-2018, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T10:46:44-07:00","id":1239730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239725#post1239725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it supposed to represent the phases of the moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which ones? There's anywhere from five to nine to 30, depending on how you look at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T10:50:17-07:00","id":1239733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239730#post1239730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which ones? There's anywhere from five to nine to 30, depending on how you look at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, people use 5 though sometimes 9 is used. I've never seen 30.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T11:42:04-07:00","id":1239743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239733#post1239733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, people use 5 though sometimes 9 is used. I've never seen 30.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we just have the Full Moon, or the Waxing Full Moon, the Full Full Moon, and the Waning Full Moon? Followed by the waxing, waning, and &quot;exact&quot; forms of each of the other eight general phases? One phase for each day/night cycle of the lunar month.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T17:57:37-07:00","id":1239856,"title":"","content":"An argument based on more necromancy for inferior sorcery doesn't fly. Necromancy has never been a major part of anything Lunar, and for that matter, Necromancy has never been as good as sorcery, period. The fact that Lunars could have more of something many won't want, in exchange for inferior access to something many will, won't be much comfort to many Lunar players. The Celestial &quot;ranking&quot; has always done its best to maintain a &quot;Solars/Solar-derivatives 1st, Sidereals/Lunars equal-yet-different&quot; and that's where things should remain.<br /> <br /> Sidereal MA versus Lunar Shapeshifting. Leave &quot;general&quot; areas of endeavor out of it entirely, because the very acts of trying to create a balance-point will result in unhappy players. Personally, I feel Sidereals and Lunars should be precisely equal when it comes to sorcery and necromancy. It isn't an area that will benefit from a couple dozen &quot;we tweak X element up, for Sidereals, X down for Lunars, Y up for Lunars, down for Sidereals.&quot; The instant you get into design-choices like that, you're short-changing every Lunar player who values X over Y, and every Sidereal player who values Y over X.<br /> <br /> Balancing Sidereals Vs Lunars has always been the mechanically most difficult element of all things Celestial Exalt design. Creating additional permutations just makes a difficult process moreso.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T18:08:55-07:00","id":1239857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239856#post1239856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An argument based on more necromancy for inferior sorcery doesn't fly. Necromancy has never been a major part of anything Lunar, and for that matter, Necromancy has never been as good as sorcery, period. The fact that Lunars could have more of something many won't want, in exchange for inferior access to something many will, won't be much comfort to many Lunar players. The Celestial &quot;ranking&quot; has always done its best to maintain a &quot;Solars/Solar-derivatives 1st, Sidereals/Lunars equal-yet-different&quot; and that's where things should remain.<br /> <br /> Sidereal MA versus Lunar Shapeshifting. Leave &quot;general&quot; areas of endeavor out of it entirely, because the very acts of trying to create a balance-point will result in unhappy players. Personally, I feel Sidereals and Lunars should be precisely equal when it comes to sorcery and necromancy. It isn't an area that will benefit from a couple dozen &quot;we tweak X element up, for Sidereals, X down for Lunars, Y up for Lunars, down for Sidereals.&quot; The instant you get into design-choices like that, you're short-changing every Lunar player who values X over Y, and every Sidereal player who values Y over X.<br /> <br /> Balancing Sidereals Vs Lunars has always been the mechanically most difficult element of all things Celestial Exalt design. Creating additional permutations just makes a difficult process moreso.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your intial premise of &quot;this always sucked, so it must suck&quot; is....weird for necromancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T18:52:36-07:00","id":1239864,"title":"","content":"My valuation isn't mechanical, it's conceptual:<br /> Sorcery is, by its nature, focused on many things. Necromancy is focused on death. Many more concepts are going to riff off &quot;many things&quot; than &quot;death&quot; in my experience. A decreased facility in &quot;affecting many things&quot; isn't made up for (in my mind) by an increased facility with affecting death.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that, conceptually, I don't care for associating Lunars more closely with death than anyone save Deathknights.<br /> I have no idea mechanically what third edition Necromancy will look like. I wouldn't care if Necromancy was 10x the better tool for killing things than sorcery. There are a lot of things I might want characters to focus on that will all fall beneath the aegis of sorcery. ESPECIALLY now that Workings widen sorcery so much. The Underworld, ghosts, etc...Not often things I think of when building a Lunar.<br /> <br /> Especially since on the rare occasion my interest shifts to the Underworld and Necromancy, there are Deathknights for that.<br /> <br /> Edit: That's not to say I can't imagine a Lunar Necromancer. The Marked Wolf, from the unofficial Lunar Castebooks, is a very interesting, very compelling character...but the Marked Wolf's take on Necromancy happens to mirror mine. It's something the occasional Lunar will get into, but that doesn't mean it's a GOOD thing for Lunars to get into.<br /> <br /> If Lunars can just be that easily linked to Necromancy, then flip it around. Give the Sidereals more Necromancy, and the Lunars the superior command (in comparison) of sorcery.<br /> <br /> Why do I have a deep and abiding suspicion that wouldn't be taken well?<br /> <br /> One could make the argument that Lunar adaptability hews more closely to the broader sorcery, whereas Sidereals actually have a full fifth of their number conceptually influenced by death and the endings of things. I don't know how Lunar castes will look for EX3, but up until now, we've had an entire Caste heavily focused on sorcery. To date, the Sidereal association with Necromancy is stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","user":"Wyldwraith","date":". 07-28-2018, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T21:27:32-07:00","id":1239895,"title":"","content":"Conceptually?<br /> <br /> 1) Saying &quot;Necromancy is focused on death&quot; and then looking at the Maiden of Endings is missing key context. The death of the Maiden of Endings is the death of Creation when it was functioning as designed, woven into Fate and reincarnation. The death of necromancy is the death of the Neverborn, the Underworld outside Fate. Insofar as Sidereals have a connection to death, it is a connection directly antithetical to necromancy.<br /> <br /> 2) Lunars in 2e were already the co-inventors of necromancy with Solars as part of the Black Nadir Concordat. With the Black Treatise saying things like &quot;Necromancy is the birthright of the Lunar Exalted&quot;, and &quot;necromancy is part of the Lunar heritage&quot;. That's a direct, close association with necromancy that even justifies Lunars having equal access to the circles Solars have.<br /> <br /> 3) Lunars are beings of edges, boundaries, the wild and scary. Necromancy fits that. Sidereals are beings of the system, secret masters of the world. Necromancy doesn't fit that.<br /> <br /> In any case, Lunars aren't going to be any worse at Workings than Sidererals. The whole &quot;better at sorcery&quot; thing comes down to, &quot;right now, some but not all Sidereals will have a discount on buying spells because they do or can favor Occult, while Lunars won't&quot;. Which is simply a mechanical accident of Lunars being Attribute Exalts for whom favoring an Ability fits poorly and for which the devs haven't been able to decide on another shim they like (that they've disclosed to us), not a deliberate conceptual choice to make Lunars worse sorcerers as part of tweaking inter-splat matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T01:22:17-07:00","id":1239932,"title":"","content":"Well, as I said, they got discounts on spells before. I paid a discounted rate for my 11 spells on my No Moon sorcerer (which isn't really an absolute ton of spells for an Essence 4 character). That'd be 22xp more without it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's also the fact that, conceptually, I don't care for associating Lunars more closely with death than anyone save Deathknights. </div> </div> </div>Firstly, giving them Labyrinth Circle necromancy doesn't associate them with death more than Solars, Infernals (who also have it at Labyrinth circle) and maybe Sidereals... (I can't remember what level they had it at, and whether they'll still have it at that level).<br /> <br /> But saying that, there are tons of animals associated with death. Ravens, crows, owls, dogs, cats, vultures, hyenas, bats, moths, black rams, etc. So there's plenty of scope for Lunar necromancers. Not as strong as Abyssals of course, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T02:01:22-07:00","id":1239945,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Lunars helped invent necromancy. They're associated with the night, and crossing boundaries, and they can do gory shit like eating things to steal their powers.<br /> <br /> Claiming that they have no basis for association with necromancy or death is... wrong. Just categorically untrue.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile endings be like<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/000/070/976/PEOPLE_DIE_IF_THEY_ARE_KILLED.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T04:19:45-07:00","id":1239976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239932#post1239932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as I said, they got discounts on spells before. I paid a discounted rate for my 11 spells on my No Moon sorcerer (which isn't really an absolute ton of spells for an Essence 4 character). That'd be 22xp more without it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Firstly, giving them Labyrinth Circle necromancy doesn't associate them with death more than Solars, Infernals (who also have it at Labyrinth circle) and maybe Sidereals... (I can't remember what level they had it at, and whether they'll still have it at that level).<br /> <br /> But saying that, there are tons of animals associated with death. Ravens, crows, owls, dogs, cats, vultures, hyenas, bats, moths, black rams, etc. So there's plenty of scope for Lunar necromancers. Not as strong as Abyssals of course, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals only could get the first level of necromancy so they almost never bothered with it. They also are one of the few exalts who just have a nuke undead button. It only works on weak ones but they're fundamentally against the undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T16:35:32-07:00","id":1240240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1239976#post1239976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals only could get the first level of necromancy so they almost never bothered with it. They also are one of the few exalts who just have a nuke undead button. It only works on weak ones but they're fundamentally against the undead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Dipping back into 2e's <i>The Black Treatise</i> again, Sidereals learned the Iron Circle &quot;when they receive positions that take them into the Underworld, or to better qualify for such positions should a Sidereal actively seek one.&quot; And &quot;The capable Sidereal necromancer can look forward to a future of Underworld-related assignments as his colleagues in Yu-Shan seek to keep him away from them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, that's 2e material, yes, so it can and will be tossed out in favor of better ideas if the Devs have them. And it was all &quot;fluff&quot;, since Lunars and Sidereals had the same mechanical access. But insofar as we have continuity of concepts . . .<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, I'm going to point out that I'm not a fan of all Lunars having to pay more for spells than some Sidereals. I personally suggested up-thread a couple alternatives, one of which was to give <i>all</i> Lunars favored-cost access to spells. But I don't think it's a particularly huge deal.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T17:13:33-07:00","id":1240254,"title":"","content":"I didn't say Lunars didn't have an association with death. I said the Sidereal association was stronger. Arguing the cosmology of the Maiden of Endings is (a little) disingenuous when 1E gives us Reckoners with titles like &quot;Ender of Royal Lines.&quot; When you make sure something does, or does not, die, it's a death association. As for the whole &quot;Lunars are creatures of the edges of things, insert X&quot; I don't like that argument when it's used to try to persuade that Lunars should have more of X, and less when it's used to argue less.<br /> <br /> If it doesn't turn into more than an XP-number thing, I really won't mind. I've long since grown accustomed to needing to rework pretty much everything to do with experience points in Exalted (with the odd, yet notable exception of suggested XP points, and point-spending for Age Group A/B/C/D/E in 2E Core), across two and a half editions. I didn't waste a tiny fraction of an instant on the idea third would get the matter right. I'm much warier of imagery, setting-points and concept prioritization.<br /> <br /> After all, it wouldn't even FEEL like Exalted if everything worked right straight off the page <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I get that Necromancy is inherently Outside Fate, and as stated, in that way sort of antithetical to the maintain-Fate Sidereal association, but taking that notion to its logical conclusion says sorcery is probably the one single thing an Exalt can do most likely to wreck fate in a truly singular way.<br /> <br /> It might just be simpler to say I have found myself so disinterested by Necromancy in the past, that I've played exactly one Necromancer. Out of fourteen-fifteen people I've ST'd for more than 3+ sessions, I've had exactly two more Necromancer-PCs in my games. Versus over 90% of all my PCs, across Exalt-types, having sorcery as some part of their concept, and at least 50% of the PCs of my players across types were sorcerers. I'm in possession of a definite &quot;Sorcery = Vital, Necromancy = Peripheral&quot; bias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","user":"Wyldwraith","date":". 07-29-2018, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T17:28:19-07:00","id":1240258,"title":"","content":"Again, the type of death the maiden of endings brings is that of finality. The undead and necromancy in general is a violation of that sanctity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T14:37:04-07:00","id":1240589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240254#post1240254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say Lunars didn't have an association with death. I said the Sidereal association was stronger. Arguing the cosmology of the Maiden of Endings is (a little) disingenuous when 1E gives us Reckoners with titles like &quot;Ender of Royal Lines.&quot; When you make sure something does, or does not, die, it's a death association. As for the whole &quot;Lunars are creatures of the edges of things, insert X&quot; I don't like that argument when it's used to try to persuade that Lunars should have more of X, and less when it's used to argue less.<br /> <br /> If it doesn't turn into more than an XP-number thing, I really won't mind. I've long since grown accustomed to needing to rework pretty much everything to do with experience points in Exalted (with the odd, yet notable exception of suggested XP points, and point-spending for Age Group A/B/C/D/E in 2E Core), across two and a half editions. I didn't waste a tiny fraction of an instant on the idea third would get the matter right. I'm much warier of imagery, setting-points and concept prioritization.<br /> <br /> After all, it wouldn't even FEEL like Exalted if everything worked right straight off the page <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I get that Necromancy is inherently Outside Fate, and as stated, in that way sort of antithetical to the maintain-Fate Sidereal association, but taking that notion to its logical conclusion says sorcery is probably the one single thing an Exalt can do most likely to wreck fate in a truly singular way.<br /> <br /> It might just be simpler to say I have found myself so disinterested by Necromancy in the past, that I've played exactly one Necromancer. Out of fourteen-fifteen people I've ST'd for more than 3+ sessions, I've had exactly two more Necromancer-PCs in my games. Versus over 90% of all my PCs, across Exalt-types, having sorcery as some part of their concept, and at least 50% of the PCs of my players across types were sorcerers. I'm in possession of a definite &quot;Sorcery = Vital, Necromancy = Peripheral&quot; bias.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolf has known the secret of death and traveling among the dead since early W:tA. At least now it's something that Exalted acknowledges in the thematic seeds of the splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T15:39:32-07:00","id":1240612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240254#post1240254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say Lunars didn't have an association with death. I said the Sidereal association was stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that the Sidereal association with death is of such a nature that it <i>does not equal</i> an association with necromancy.<br /> <br /> Your logic on Sidereals and necromancy is running something like, &quot;Tesla is a carmaker, cars are associated with the use of gasoline, therefore Tesla is associated with the use of gasoline.&quot; It is not actually a response to &quot;Tesla's cars don't run on gasoline, so the association isn't transitive&quot; to reiterate &quot;But Tesla is a carmaker!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T16:13:49-07:00","id":1240627,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, does anyone else feel extremely meh about any connection between Lunars and beastfolk? Given that Lunars are shapeshifters, it seems like, if Lunars are giving out distinctly Lunar blessings, it feels like the capacity to shapeshift into an animal would be more resonant than permanently blending the subject with the features in question. It just seems like there's been so much baggage from the Minotaur Origin Story of prior editions that a clean cut and replacement would be preferable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T16:24:41-07:00","id":1240630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240627#post1240627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, does anyone else feel extremely meh about any connection between Lunars and beastfolk? Given that Lunars are shapeshifters, it seems like, if Lunars are giving out distinctly Lunar blessings, it feels like the capacity to shapeshift into an animal would be more resonant than permanently blending the subject with the features in question. It just seems like there's been so much baggage from the Minotaur Origin Story of prior editions that a clean cut and replacement would be preferable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer it if they were more like alex mercer myself but it feels like this edition is definitely going to cleave greatly with beastfolk. .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T16:57:34-07:00","id":1240640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240627#post1240627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, does anyone else feel extremely meh about any connection between Lunars and beastfolk? Given that Lunars are shapeshifters, it seems like, if Lunars are giving out distinctly Lunar blessings, it feels like the capacity to shapeshift into an animal would be more resonant than permanently blending the subject with the features in question. It just seems like there's been so much baggage from the Minotaur Origin Story of prior editions that a clean cut and replacement would be preferable.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you think of a lunar, do you not picture someone in their hybrid form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:01:32-07:00","id":1240641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240640#post1240640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you think of a lunar, do you not picture someone in their hybrid form?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I think about them, they have the ability to change out of it after tearing up faces. Fluidity is more important, especially since the vast majority of beastfolk in EX3 are completely independent of Lunars in origin and society.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, a number of other beings can assume similar forms - gods, elementals, demons, Fair Folk... Lunars are far from alone in having the capacity to look like beastfolk. They do, however, as a matter of course, have the capacity to change their forms readily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 07-30-2018, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:28:11-07:00","id":1240647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240630#post1240630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer it if they were more like alex mercer myself but it feels like this edition is definitely going to cleave greatly with beastfolk. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm positive Liminal Exalted of the Flesh Aspect will come closest to fulfilling your desires for a [Prototype] experience.<br /> <br /> Is it not about playing a monster born from the corpse of a dead man, driven by his desires for revenge, and guided by his memories? Flesh Aspect Charms are the ones that speed up and facilitate the process of incorporating the bodies of others into your own... perhaps even to the point of consuming them utterly and fluidly assuming their appearance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240641#post1240641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I think about them, they have the ability to change out of it after tearing up faces. Fluidity is more important,</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> When I think of a Lunar, I think of Bellcross, the kaijuu. But I also think of Age, the human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:33:59-07:00","id":1240649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240627#post1240627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, does anyone else feel extremely meh about any connection between Lunars and beastfolk? Given that Lunars are shapeshifters, it seems like, if Lunars are giving out distinctly Lunar blessings, it feels like the capacity to shapeshift into an animal would be more resonant than permanently blending the subject with the features in question. It just seems like there's been so much baggage from the Minotaur Origin Story of prior editions that a clean cut and replacement would be preferable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:43:03-07:00","id":1240652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240649#post1240649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not both?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the very least, we might be able to craft Ulfhednar hooded wolf-skin cloaks such as those that Sigmund and Sinfjotli found in the woods one day, with the power to turn them into wolves when donned.<br /> <br /> Well, wolf-<i>men</i>, at least, by applying some appropriate mutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:50:38-07:00","id":1240656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240649#post1240649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not both?</div> </div> </div> </div>The permanent blending seems comparatively non-magical, if that makes any sense. Beastfolk are basically normal people in Exalted, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T18:00:28-07:00","id":1240660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240647#post1240647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm positive Liminal Exalted of the Flesh Aspect will come closest to fulfilling your desires for a [Prototype] experience.<br /> <br /> Is it not about playing a monster born from the corpse of a dead man, driven by his desires for revenge, and guided by his memories? Flesh Aspect Charms are the ones that speed up and facilitate the process of incorporating the bodies of others into your own... perhaps even to the point of consuming them utterly and fluidly assuming their appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>At a terrestrial level, so not at the level i want it to be. Objectively weaker than him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T18:03:48-07:00","id":1240662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240660#post1240660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At a terrestrial level, so not at the level i want it to be. Objectively weaker than him.</div> </div> </div> </div>What could you possibly be basing this on, except for an inherent preconception as to what 'Terrestrial' means.<br /> <br /> Wait until we actually get some idea of what their capabilities are before you shit all over them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T18:09:36-07:00","id":1240663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240662#post1240662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What could you possibly be basing this on, except for an inherent preconception as to what 'Terrestrial' means.<br /> <br /> Wait until we actually get some idea of what their capabilities are before you shit all over them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean out side of the ones in 2e. I'm not a fan of t