"value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T18:49:04-07:00","id":1240674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240670#post1240670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, they weren't a thing in 2e. Except as a footnote.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I was confused how you 'didn't like the new ones', if their weren't old ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T19:05:39-07:00","id":1240679,"title":"","content":"Fundamentally,<br /> My reason for even involving myself related to an objection to the notion of &quot;Necromany increase, as justification for less-Sorcery-anything.&quot; I place a near-zero value on Necromancy. It's useful for antagonists, but my players seldom choose to portray Deathknights, and during my all-too-rare opportunities to play, I tend strongly towards playing something I know I'll enjoy. I get enough grimdark when Storytelling, so I'm not eager for more when I get to frisk about, unyoked from the ST-plow. No Moon all-in Sorcerers, or intelligent Full Moon dabblers make up six or seven of my all-time top ten favorite PCs. ::shrugs::<br /> <br /> There was a sort of underlying point to my statements as well. Other than the maintaining of the Solar Primacy requirements, (including obviously Void Necromancy for DKs), I tend to apply an &quot;Equal sub-Solar access&quot; mindset. Were it up to me, Sorcery and Necromancy both would be access-exact for both Lunars and Sidereals, with the DBs being screwed into last-place, as usual. I dislike even the concept of trying to enact a &quot;different but equal&quot; balance for Lunars &amp; Sidereals when it comes to Sorcery and Necromancy.<br /> <br /> I've heard the Lunars being Attribute-based makes it difficult argument. I've even heard Lunar shapeshifting somehow justifies various forms of &quot;More of X, for Sidereals.&quot; Which puzzles me, in the face of Sidereal MA and Sidereal Astrology.<br /> <br /> I don't see a positive to be had, having the access/facility/XP costs differ. I would like to emphasize I'm not, in the slightest, not even a shadow of an implication to that effect, trying to make any sort of &quot;Up Lunars, Down Sidereals!&quot; argument. When I say I'd like them to be equal on Sorcery and Necromancy, that's exactly what I mean. Making the comment &quot;Let the Sidereals have the Necromancy&quot; was sort of designed to make the point most people are going to be far more interested in Sorcery than Necromancy, and that what happens with Sorcery is considered far more pivotal than Necromancy's fate by some.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T19:36:24-07:00","id":1240691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240679#post1240679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see a positive to be had, having the access/facility/XP costs differ. I would like to emphasize I'm not, in the slightest, not even a shadow of an implication to that effect, trying to make any sort of &quot;Up Lunars, Down Sidereals!&quot; argument. When I say I'd like them to be equal on Sorcery and Necromancy, that's exactly what I mean. Making the comment &quot;Let the Sidereals have the Necromancy&quot; was sort of designed to make the point most people are going to be far more interested in Sorcery than Necromancy, and that what happens with Sorcery is considered far more pivotal than Necromancy's fate by some.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue here is that Sidereals get lower necromancy not because some sidereals wouldn't want it, such as black ice shadow, but because it's contrary to what they are. They have more anti-necromancy tools than solars. It's not even a question as to how much goes against what the maiden of endings does.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T23:45:40-07:00","id":1240736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240679#post1240679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a sort of underlying point to my statements as well. Other than the maintaining of the Solar Primacy requirements, (including obviously Void Necromancy for DKs), I tend to apply an &quot;Equal sub-Solar access&quot; mindset. Were it up to me, Sorcery and Necromancy both would be access-exact for both Lunars and Sidereals</div> </div> </div> </div>And I don't have any objection to you having that as your preference. <i>De gustibus non disputandum est</i>, to coin a phrase. I just don't think it (or Sidereal superiority) actually is a consequence of the conceptual natures of Necromancy, Lunars, and Sidereals.<br /> <br /> As far as treating it as a matter of equality between Celestial Exalted, well, Sidereals are already better at Martial Arts, and Lunars are already better at Evocations (<i>Arms of the Chosen</i> establishes Sidereals are resonant with starmetal and dissonant with everything else, while Lunars are resonant with moonsilver and neutral with everything else). To my taste, with parity <i>already</i> broken blatantly in two of the three areas of cross-Exalted magic powers, the better thing to do is to follow conceptual consequences rather than try to force symmetry in the area of spells.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, a suggestion I made way earlier in the thread was that <i>all</i> Lunars get spells at Favored cost, instead of some or none. Which would make Lunars-in-general better than Sidereals-in-general at Sorcery in addition to making them way better at Necromancy. So you can accuse <i>me</i> of &quot;Up Lunars, Down Sidereals!&quot; if you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T00:58:53-07:00","id":1240752,"title":"","content":"...How would you feel if it turned out that the dragonblooded spell cost was actually the standard, lunars *did* get it at favoured costs and solars actually got it super-cheap, reflecting their oft-quoted position as &quot;masters of sorcery&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T01:18:17-07:00","id":1240761,"title":"","content":"I take absolutely no issue with Solar Primacy in Sorcery. My only concern when you say &quot;super cheap&quot; is not knowing how cheap is too cheap, not its &quot;cheaper than&quot; figure. The only issue I ever had with Solar Primacy conceptually is actually in &quot;defense of&quot; Sidereals. I always found it rather unfair giving Solars access to Sidereal MA, because it let Solars creep onto the Sidereal Special Button, whereas you didn't see Solars shapeshifting. Saying they couldn't teach any Sidereal MA they learned never seemed like any balance to that, really.<br /> <br /> So far as Solars with Sorcery, as the only top-tier Sorcery-users ever, it seems reasonably they'd be best at it across the board. Of course I'd then say it follows they could take Necromancy right up top too, unless third wants to retain the whole &quot;Solars go to top tier Sorcery, second-tier Necromancy, DKs are vice versa.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not having seen them, I have no idea where Exigents, Liminals and Getiminians should fall in the splat balance. I would imagine Exigents can't be more powerful than DBs, or the DBs would be screaming Anathema at them, but otherwise...<br /> <br /> Edit: Keeping in mind I haven't played a Solar in...hmm, five almost six years. Though I've played three Infernals, if you're concerned I might possess a Solar-bias. Trust me, I don't.<br /> <br /> Double Edit: And again, I would advocate that the Lunar rate should be the same as the Sidereals....I have incredibly limited experience with Alchemicals, so don't feel qualified to say anything about them, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","user":"Wyldwraith","date":". 07-31-2018, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T01:45:30-07:00","id":1240766,"title":"","content":"Exigents can very much be more powerful than dragon blooded. That is definitely a thing. <br /> <br /> They don't go screaming &quot;anathema&quot; at them because, well, the Immaculate Texts don't say they're anathema. They are generally on thin ice though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T03:40:09-07:00","id":1240784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240660#post1240660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At a terrestrial level</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you need to re-evaluate your perspective on what a Terrestrial level is, given their new Charms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T04:01:45-07:00","id":1240791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240784#post1240784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you need to re-evaluate your perspective on what a Terrestrial level is, given their new Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen the charms and while DB's are better this edition they are no where near a solar. I don't think that's a bad thing but there is a sheer level of diffeeence between them. Celestials too will have a clear level of difference. It's the difference between being able to threaten a small town and being able to threaten nexus with that kind of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T04:51:01-07:00","id":1240799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240791#post1240791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they are no where near a solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Alex Mercer is?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the difference between being able to threaten a small town and being able to threaten nexus with that kind of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, the kind of power that can threaten the whole of Nexus in a single action (assuming that none of its supernatural denizens and benefactors are in opposition to you) is generally at Essence 5 for Solars as well, even if they have a capacity to acquire those abilities earlier if they have the right Supernal Ability.<br /> <br /> But assuming an Essence 5 Dragon Blood under circumstances where they're the only game in town, I absolutely think that they can wield powers that can devastate a large community. Maybe a bit longer, over the course of a couple of days rather than an instant, but hey, that the firebombing of Tokyo was more ordnance intensive than the atomic bombing of Hiroshima didn't mean that it killed any fewer people. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T05:11:47-07:00","id":1240806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240799#post1240799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Alex Mercer is?</div> </div> </div> </div>He was capable of killing hundreds if not thousands of people, with them having no chance to fight back. All the while climbing the highest skyscrapers and powerbombing back down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Strictly speaking, the kind of power that can threaten the whole of Nexus in a single action (assuming that none of its supernatural denizens and benefactors are in opposition to you) is generally at Essence 5 for Solars as well, even if they have a capacity to acquire those abilities earlier if they have the right Supernal Ability.<br /> <br /> But assuming an Essence 5 Dragon Blood under circumstances where they're the only game in town, I absolutely think that they can wield powers that can devastate a large community. Maybe a bit longer, over the course of a couple of days rather than an instant, but hey, that the firebombing of Tokyo was more ordnance intensive than the atomic bombing of Hiroshima didn't mean that it killed any fewer people. </div> </div> </div>A DB and a solar are just not at the same level and a DB will often not have more issues against gods and other exalts compared to a solar. There are just inherent limitations with Dragon blooded that Celestials don't have to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T05:44:52-07:00","id":1240817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240806#post1240806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was capable of killing hundreds if not thousands of people, with them having no chance to fight back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that statement generally goes for unarmed civilians in the middle of a warzone.<br /> <br /> Certainly, the tanks and gunships and troops armed with heavy and high explosive weaponry had a chance to fight back, I died to them enough times.<br /> <br /> And if it's an argument of &quot;even if you blow him up, he can come back from the remains&quot;, that actually does apply to Liminals to a certain degree as well. <br /> <br /> I mean, maybe some modern military technology will be incidentally incendiary enough to prevent that, but if we're talking about somebody like Alex Mercer in the actual setting, then your slings and arrows and javelins probably won't get the job done all the way.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it's like... the abstraction of battle groups still conveys an idea of cinematically killing improbably large numbers of people, and people in a scene that would constitute non-combatants or trivial opponents are still rather squishy.<br /> <br /> It all depends on what kind of area-of-effect attacks you think Liminals might have, or observe that Dragon Blooded do have.<br /> <br /> Because really, being able to kill large numbers of defenceless people at a time strikes me as less of a mark of power than being able to effectively fight against powerful individuals.<br /> <br /> Barring things such as the Solar Lore Charms to call natural disaster down upon a location, but that's apparently a scale <i>above</i> what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the while climbing the highest skyscrapers and powerbombing back down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that Terrestrial Exalted are slouches in the areas of climbing things and then falling off of them either. They've got some reasonably impressive Athletics Charms to cover both; one even gives them a kind of explosive impact effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A DB and a solar are just not at the same level and a DB will often not have more issues against gods and other exalts compared to a solar. There are just inherent limitations with Dragon blooded that Celestials don't have to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is technically correct, but still doesn't suffice as an argument against the idea that the parameters you're describing are well within Dragon Blooded capabilities, and conceivably within Liminal. You're not asking Alex Mercer to do anything like shape reality from the nascent chaos, permanently kill a spirit or wrestle with something ten times larger than him.<br /> <br /> Besides, this all feels like a rather simplistic take on transplantation; as if to say that you would want to play somebody who was everything Alex Mercer was but the name and the hoodie. That certainly would not have happened if Lunars were like that under any circumstances, and can't really in any other part of the system or genre, so it becomes a question of where the important lines of compromise lie. What is preferable; Alex Mercer powers that somehow need to emerge out and live alongside of Moon mythology and bestial shapeshifting and invocation, or Alex Mercer powers that need to jump through a few hoops and still probably be scaled back a bit for the big ticket powers that play a bit differently in a mutual storytelling game rather than a free-roaming sandbox?<br /> <br /> (Those latter ones being concerns for Solars as well, mind; some of the more destructive effects can be used less frequently than it probably takes to recharge Mercer's murder meter)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T06:12:11-07:00","id":1240823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240817#post1240817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What is preferable; Alex Mercer powers that somehow need to emerge out and live alongside of Moon mythology and bestial shapeshifting and invocation, or Alex Mercer powers that need to jump through a few hoops and still probably be scaled back a bit for the big ticket powers that play a bit differently in a mutual storytelling game rather than a free-roaming sandbox?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer that lunars be able to shapeshift into any form or mode like luna and not just limited to set shapes. They are supposed to be mercurial. This implies that they can transform in a bunch of ways that defy normal convention. This just feels like downgrade for lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T06:39:29-07:00","id":1240834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240823#post1240823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer that lunars be able to shapeshift into any form or mode like luna and not just limited to set shapes. They are supposed to be mercurial. This implies that they can transform in a bunch of ways that defy normal convention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's the Moon mythology?<br /> <br /> There was a thread a while back in which I ranted at length on how many competing ideas there were about what Lunars were &quot;supposed&quot; to be, and how those formed largely in the blank space provided by their development problems. I've ranted elsewhere about the legitimacy some people try to give their preferences by talking about what something is &quot;supposed&quot; to be, rather than just what they want it to be.<br /> <br /> Because no, no they <i>weren't</i> supposed to be mercurial. If somebody wants to give their idea of Lunars legitimacy with an appeal to authority, it probably has to go back to what they were like in First Edition, and that was <i>far</i> from mercurial. That was so far from mercurial that you needed to buy a Charm just to have your totem animal.<br /> <br /> There are a couple of other things to note, such as how they would never actually get freeform shapeshifting, being limited to what shapes would be provided by the Charms a given Lunar has (unless one is suggesting that they should have such wide-ranging shapeshifting as an innate power, which seems terribly imbalanced), and that even in Glories, Luna was actually written as only ever turning into distinct things, with maybe the exception of the exceptional and rarely used Chtonic Baara. Indeed, she seems to be written specifically to <i>not</i> have turned into &quot;any form or mode&quot;; she was written as being able to shapeshift like Lunars were, as though she had the Heart's Blood of everything in existence, and all Lunar Knacks, just without a Tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This just feels like downgrade for lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, probably less of a downgrade and more going in a direction other than some people's speculations and desires; Second Edition veered in a lot of directions with Lunars, but they still never got to the point of actually being written as what you're talking about here.<br /> <br /> It also kind of depends on how powerful your abnormal conventions are, or at least on the implicit assumption that a {whatever they would actually turn into} is a superior choice just because it's not a thing that will exist.<br /> <br /> Lunars will still be able to transform into spirits, and to use Charms with the Eclipse keyword. Lunars will transform into animals, that are now being written with special Merits and maneuvers, further enhanced by combination with their own Charms, and with improved dice pools functioning as a kind of free Excellency. And Lunars will still have their Charms, doing a variety of things beyond turning into animals (I noticed one reference to a defensive Charm in a kind of form to make their insides into a heavy weight), and things that don't have to do with personal transformation at all, such as cursing folks.<br /> <br /> They're not being downgraded, and they're not merely turning into animals the way that Second Edition wrote them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T06:57:05-07:00","id":1240836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240834#post1240834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, probably less of a downgrade and more going in a direction other than some people's speculations and desires; Second Edition veered in a lot of directions with Lunars, but they still never got to the point of actually being written as what you're talking about here.<br /> <br /> It also kind of depends on how powerful your abnormal conventions are, or at least on the implicit assumption that a {whatever they would actually turn into} is a superior choice just because it's not a thing that will exist.<br /> <br /> Lunars will still be able to transform into spirits, and to use Charms with the Eclipse keyword. Lunars will transform into animals, that are now being written with special Merits and maneuvers, further enhanced by combination with their own Charms, and with improved dice pools functioning as a kind of free Excellency. And Lunars will still have their Charms, doing a variety of things beyond turning into animals (I noticed one reference to a defensive Charm in a kind of form to make their insides into a heavy weight), and things that don't have to do with personal transformation at all, such as cursing folks.<br /> <br /> They're not being downgraded, and they're not merely turning into animals the way that Second Edition wrote them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are still all structured forms when they should be able to turn into non-structured forms. So I personally just find it a downgrade instead of letting them stretch arms and and use twisted forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T07:29:47-07:00","id":1240849,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lunars-preview-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\">GUYS HOLY FUCK</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T07:31:18-07:00","id":1240851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240836#post1240836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are still all structured forms when they should be able to turn into non-structured forms. So I personally just find it a downgrade instead of letting them stretch arms and and use twisted forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, that presupposes that being able to do those things is superior (being able to turn into a bird that can fly doesn't exactly seem like a downgrade compared to stretchy limbs).<br /> <br /> I don't actually think that stretching arms is out of the current Lunar wheelhouse, and feel free to ask in the playtest thread in which people who have actually seen the Charms are doling out information about them. As for twisted forms, well, that's both a very broad category that doesn't precisely exclude what Lunars might be able to turn into (<a href=\"https://<br /> &#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/Uran_EskaoftheSevenBlades.png]this</a> can be somebody's beast person form now[/url]), and raises the question of what it would actually do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T07:32:27-07:00","id":1240852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240849#post1240849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lunars-preview-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\">GUYS HOLY FUCK</a></div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't talking about that in the playtest thread? I just saw it while I was trying to find a link to that image of Eska, and assumed...<br /> <br /> Well anyway, time to have a look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T07:36:45-07:00","id":1240856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240849#post1240849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lunars-preview-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\">GUYS HOLY FUCK</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> * makes note to self about buying Lunars when it comes out, and any Exalted 3E books currently out once money comes in","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T07:46:19-07:00","id":1240861,"title":"","content":"So yeah, a lot of those Charms are neat. There seems to be a recurring theme of Lunars engaging with non-existent Intimacies, and I like the idea of a Strength Charm as a method of a kind of psychic attack (plus the idea of benefits to taking the shape of somebody else that has already put in the work to be greatly feared. I'm a little bit unclear on how the cost of Flowing Body Evasion works, but it's otherwise a nicely distinct form of defence.<br /> <br /> Also quite like the one for gaining memories associated with Intimacies, and messing around with people's memories.<br /> <br /> It's a good start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T07:47:26-07:00","id":1240862,"title":"","content":"Memory-Drinking Mediation: How you know when people were asking &quot;If Lunars didn't <i><b>perfectly </b></i>mimic their target in a social setting would there be a vanishingly small chance they would be revealed?&quot; Robert Vance and Eric Minton were actually just sitting there laughing their asses off.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, Steel Paw Style. I.e. With this and like one or two more Charms, I can finally play that Giant Sloth Strength/Stamina monster Martial Artist and laugh at Dex. Woohoo!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 07-31-2018, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T08:11:41-07:00","id":1240875,"title":"","content":"Magpie's Nest Resourcefullness is also very cool for a gadgeteer.<br /> <br /> Less grand than what Ever-Ready Innovation Discipline can accomplish, but way cheaper and can be used once per scene, as opposed to a couple times per story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T08:17:00-07:00","id":1240880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240875#post1240875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magpie's Nest Resourcefullness is also very cool for a gadgeteer.</div> </div> </div> </div>{checks again}<br /> <br /> Ah, I had misread it as something mostly for bargaining, I hadn't taken in how it was about pulling out a small but useful object in any situation.<br /> <br /> Good way to do Lunar versatility, anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T10:22:07-07:00","id":1240932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars will still be able to transform into spirits</div> </div> </div> </div>Will they? I thought that was gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Magpie's Nest Resourcefulness is a nice way to do a Lunar craft charm: you can use it for craft, but also for other things.<br /> It's also a bit similar to the &quot;Here's one I made earlier&quot; Craft charm in Miracles. I'm glad, because this is the sort of charm that extends what you can do with Craft, rather than just giving you more dice/slots/craft XP.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm glad to see that Adder Fang is one of the Totemic charms, because I think there's a lot of concepts based on poisonous animals that don't really seem like they'd favour Stamina (as a lot of poisonous or venomous animals are not noted for their toughness). Hopefully, that's generally how Totemic is used in the set.<br /> <br /> I also like how simple these charms are. I mean, they're Exalted charms, they're not incredibly simple, but there's no particularly complex new mechanics or anything. Protean and Totemic are pretty simple keywords really.<br /> <br /> I also particularly like Devil-Pleasing Chiminage, because firstly it's a good example of a non-social-attribute shamanic charm, but secondly I always thought that introducing a fact about the things a spirit likes or dislikes is very appropriate for an occultist; it makes perfect sense to see, say, a rare and obscure demon and have the party's occultist go &quot;Aha, I read that this kind of demon is deathly afraid of white cats!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Overall, I'm very pleased. Not Silver Solars. Not protean blobs. Generally well-written and clear, straightforward charms that let you <i>do</i> new things rather than just get some bonus (the kind of charms I enjoy, and the reason in 2nd ed I enjoyed playing Lunars more than Solars)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There seems to be a recurring theme of Lunars engaging with non-existent Intimacies</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you say a bit more about this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T11:12:08-07:00","id":1240961,"title":"","content":"With Devil-Pleasing Chiminage... I didn't notice at first glance it works on &quot;Spirits and Rakhsa&quot;, meaning that it works on Ghosts and Demons.<br /> Now I want to build a Lunar who's trying to save their Solar Mate who became an Abyssal. Using this charm on a Deathlord seems like fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T13:12:39-07:00","id":1241004,"title":"","content":"Huh...<br /> Hey, remember recently when people were complaining about how massive the Ability prereqs are for Solars and Dragonblood, and how it encourages everyone to have a few huge stats so they can actually get decent charms? And how this was weird for the game/setting?<br /> <br /> Look at the prereqs on these:<br /> Appearance 3<br /> Charisma 4<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Dexterity 3<br /> Intelligence 3<br /> Intelligence 4<br /> Manipulation 3<br /> Perception 3<br /> Stamina 2<br /> Stamina 3<br /> Strength 4<br /> Wits 2<br /> <br /> And bear in mind that Lunars have 9/7/5 for their attributes, from what was said before.<br /> So a fully min-maxed character has 5/5/2/5/4/1/5/1/1<br /> And with as non-min-maxed stats as possible 4/4/4/4/3/3/3/3/2.<br /> Essentially, as a Lunar you'll have 3 in anything you didn't deliberately choose as your character's weakness, which probably aren't charm trees you'll be buying from anyway (especially as Totemic also helps with the prereqs, for example a Snake-totem Lunar could get a bunch of poison charms off either Wits or Stamina).<br /> <br /> Admittedly, most of these are low-essence charms (the Dex 5 is Essence 3, everything else is 1-2).<br /> But while some of them are at the base of charm trees, but others have some prereqs so are a charm or three up the tree.<br /> <br /> So overall, it looks like at low-essence, you don't need to try at all to min-max your character's stats to ensure you can reach the Attribute prereqs you need. <br /> <br /> You don't seem to really need 5s at all as a Lunar until higher essence (from the sample we've got, which is admittedly not huge).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T13:23:28-07:00","id":1241006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240932#post1240932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you say a bit more about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>A few Charms let the Lunar use situations as Intimacies, where people don't actually have them.<br /> <br /> Like that lets you declare an entity likes an object an if you use that object as an offering, that offer is like an Intimacy to the entity.<br /> <br /> Or the the one that lets you treat anyone belonging to the society you have an Intimacy towards as also having an Intimacy to an aspect of their culture.<br /> <br /> Or the one that lets you use innuendo to sow doubt and use that doubt as Intimacy for social leverage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T13:42:17-07:00","id":1241008,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if it's a Lunar thing, because there's a few of them in the Dragonblood book too.<br /> <br /> The DB book had way more &quot;treat them as having this intimacy&quot; or indeed inflicting intimacies (more than just supplementing instill rolls) than the Core's Solar charms, or so it seemed to me. I think it may just be because the DB+Lunar charms have different writers to the Solar charms.<br /> <br /> Not that the reason matters too much: either way, it's good. I find the DB social charms actually more useful than a lot of the Solars ones (which often end up with you rolling a ton of successes, and then them just spending a wp), and these look useful for the same reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T14:28:09-07:00","id":1241019,"title":"","content":"Stalking Nightmare Hunter I predict right now will be a Charm that sees very, very little use. A human-only target limitation, for 10m AND a willpower? Uh uh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T14:38:05-07:00","id":1241020,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but it's a good way to get human forms without killing people.<br /> All you have to do is scare them a lot*, and then make a fairly easy roll (Str+your highest combat ability vs their Resolve, which is going to be lowered by their Major intimacy of Fear), and then you've got their form.<br /> <br /> *Which kind of means how good this charm is depends on how many Lunar charms there are that make you good at scaring people. They need a Major intimacy of Fear, which is hefty, but might be easy if this part of a intimidation-tree.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, if you stick a major intimacy of Fear on a whole bunch of people in a town by, say, going DBT, standing on top of a big building, and roaring at everyone, then you've just got access to a ton of potential forms.)<br /> <br /> <br /> The 10m, 1wp is actually a pretty small cost, because you do it at night from the comfort of your own house/den, rather than in the middle of a stressful or dangerous situation. Then sleep for 8 hours, and you've got it back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-31-2018, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T14:42:01-07:00","id":1241021,"title":"","content":"You can take someone's form, after scarying them and then haunting their dreams. That is pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> Any Lunar infiltrator/spy/socialite would be wise to take this charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T14:51:33-07:00","id":1241024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241008#post1241008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if it's a Lunar thing, because there's a few of them in the Dragonblood book too.<br /> <br /> The DB book had way more &quot;treat them as having this intimacy&quot; or indeed inflicting intimacies (more than just supplementing instill rolls) than the Core's Solar charms, or so it seemed to me. I think it may just be because the DB+Lunar charms have different writers to the Solar charms.<br /> <br /> Not that the reason matters too much: either way, it's good. I find the DB social charms actually more useful than a lot of the Solars ones (which often end up with you rolling a ton of successes, and then them just spending a wp), and these look useful for the same reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't stop willpower spending though. A solar can just break a target while DB and lunars have to finesse it a bit and still lose.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T15:13:56-07:00","id":1241034,"title":"","content":"A few of the DB ones actually do (I checked with Vance). And a lot of them make Instill or Inspire attempts require a Decision Point to break. That's actually really powerful, because that means they're going to need 2 different intimacies to resist (since one gets used to pump their Resolve). And one of them has to be strong enough to oppose the level of intimacy you're instilling.<br /> Normally, Decision Points are only for Persuade, but Persuade requires them to already have an intimacy that supports your intimacy.<br /> <br /> Whereas, with a DB using Dragon Warlord's Convocation, I walk past some random fisherman, tell him &quot;Come and follow me!&quot; and make an instill roll to give him a Major Tie of loyalty. I make my social roll, and if he doesn't have two intimacies that oppose him getting a Tie of loyalty to me (one of which needs to be major), then if I beat their Resolve there's no way to resist. (And even if he does have 2 opposing intimacies, including a Major one, it's 2wp to resist instead of 1). He'll become my loyal follower, probably abandoning his fishingboat to become my disciple (but it's only Major, so he might abandon me if I get captured and crucified. But up to that he's loyal. Also it's best to use on childless widowers so they don't have Defining Intimacies to their families).<br /> <br /> Outside of mind-control effects, Solars are actually not great at being able to make social attacks that can't just be ignored for 1wp*. If they've found a way to make such a social attack, they're amazing at it. But they're not that great at getting the opportunity to do so.<br /> This is the problem our Zenith has; sure, he can regularly roll 25 successes on his social attacks, but people can just spend 1wp and bounce off the intimacy he's trying to inflict,** and he can't persuade people without them already having an intimacy that supports what he wants.<br /> <br /> *Fulminating Word lets you raise it to 2. It's one of the best charms in Solar Presence. But it doesn't work on Instill, so doesn't help you Persuade someone who lacks a strong enough intimacy already. And it's expensive if you fail. And for non-mind control, you might be able to use Mastery of Small Manners to treat people as having a minor intimacy to you, but that's pretty much the only way to persuade people when they don't already have appropriate intimacies. <br /> <br /> **Obviously regular mortals tend not to do this, but at persuading people who are significantly opposing us, it's an issue. Also, trying to convince other PCs to make peace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-31-2018, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T15:20:13-07:00","id":1241037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241008#post1241008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if it's a Lunar thing, because there's a few of them in the Dragonblood book too.<br /> <br /> The DB book had way more &quot;treat them as having this intimacy&quot; or indeed inflicting intimacies (more than just supplementing instill rolls) than the Core's Solar charms, or so it seemed to me. I think it may just be because the DB+Lunar charms have different writers to the Solar charms.<br /> <br /> Not that the reason matters too much: either way, it's good. I find the DB social charms actually more useful than a lot of the Solars ones (which often end up with you rolling a ton of successes, and then them just spending a wp), and these look useful for the same reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realised after writing this, that according to the playtesters Appearance is full of charms that create or count as intimacies, so maybe you're right Isator, and this is a particularly Lunar thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T15:34:15-07:00","id":1241044,"title":"","content":"I wrote this up for myself, but thought you guys might be interested to see it. It's a charm list for Lunars, consisting of charms we've heard/read so far, including in Eska of the Seven Blades' write-up. I haven't included stuff from the Lunar antagonists in the Core though, as they might have changed too much.<br /> I was going to also include the rules for the charms, but I realised not everyone has bought Eska of the Seven Blades, so it's just the names.<br /> <br /> If there's a ..., that means there might be prerequisite charms, but I don't know what they are. If there's two charms on the same line, the second is a prerequisite of the first.<br /> There's some charms I guess are prerequisites of others, but I'm not sure, so just left them.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know the name of the charm for attacking with Strength? Was that mentioned?<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u>Excellencies</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Caste and Favoured Excellencies are free at Attribute 3+, other are free at Attribute 4+ or with 2 Charms bought</span> </span></span><br /> <br /> <u>Not Sure</u><br /> ... Deadly Beastman Transformation (I guess Strength, but might be Wits with HBR as a prereq, maybe with Str Totemic)<br /> Hybrid Body Rearrangement (I guess Wits or Strength)... Changing Face Transformation<br /> Silken Grasp (I'm guessing Dex or Wits. Might well have the Totemic tag for spider-totems.)<br /> Chimera Soul Expression<br /> \u2026 Behemoth Inhalation Prana (I guess Strength or Stamina)<br /> \u2026 Beast Mind Metanoia (I guess Wits)<br /> \u2026 Towering Beast Form, Mountainous Spirit Expression, Undaunted Behemoth Avatar (I guess Strength)<br /> \u2026 Creation-Spanning Passion (social attribute obviously)<br /> <br /> <u>Strength </u><br /> \u2026 Terrifying Predator Consumption, Stalking Nightmare Hunter<br /> \u2026 Mighty Ram Smash, Fatal Stryx Flight, Swooping Hybroc Death Strike<br /> <br /> <u>Dexterity</u><br /> \u2026 Sensing the Deadly Flow, Flowing Body Evasion<br /> \u2026 Instinct-Driven Beast Movement<br /> \u2026 Predator Grace Method, Swift Killer Style<br /> \u2026 Sinuous Striking Grace<br /> \u2026 Coiled Serpent Strikes<br /> \u2026 Gleaming Crescent Block<br /> \u2026 Octopus and Spider Barrage<br /> <br /> <u>Stamina</u><br /> Steel Paw Technique<br /> \u2026 Scorpion and Toad Absolution (Totemic), Adder Fang Method (Totemic)<br /> \u2026 Halt the Scarlet Flow<br /> \u2026 Den Warden Method<br /> <br /> <u>Charisma</u><br /> \u2026 Herd-Strengthening Invocation, Herd-Reinforcement Stance<br /> \u2026 Dream-Weaving Voice<br /> \u2026 Lion's Roar Rebuke<br /> <br /> <u>Manipulation</u><br /> \u2026 Tale-Spinning Mastery, Uncertain Sky Ambiguity<br /> <br /> <u>Appearance</u><br /> Heart-Drinking Allure<br /> \u2026 Guiding The Flock, Wasp and Termite Dance (Totemic)<br /> <br /> <u>Perception</u><br /> \u2026 Heightened Sense Method, Echo-Drinking Awareness<br /> \u2026 Sense-Sharpening Change<br /> <br /> <u>Intelligence</u><br /> Memory-Drinking Meditation<br /> \u2026 Ardent Prayers Fulfilled, Devil-Pleasing Chiminage<br /> <br /> <u>Wits</u><br /> \u2026 Squirrel\u2019s Cunning Technique, Magpie's Nest Resourcefulness<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T15:39:05-07:00","id":1241046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241008#post1241008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if it's a Lunar thing, because there's a few of them in the Dragonblood book too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would need to look back at that book. When a lot of them are bunched together like this, it feels like a trend.<br /> <br /> (Yes, I've seen your follow-up post about the Appearance Charms)<br /> <br /> Mostly, I would like it if it <i>was</i> a prominent aspect of them, because I think it would play well into the trickster and outsider thing. Certainly, I find the idea of them being empowered by iconoclasm in the form of being able to exploit, perhaps powerfully, the groupthink of others.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T15:41:25-07:00","id":1241049,"title":"","content":"Yes, I thought that was quite an interesting way to do that charm, especially when you compare it to the similar yet different way Mastery of Small Manners takes advantage of people's culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T15:58:01-07:00","id":1241056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1240862#post1240862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Memory-Drinking Mediation</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking back at this Charm, I realised something interesting and kind of messed up about how it works.<br /> <br /> So, you don't only get the memories, you get the Tie that came with them. That becomes a part of your personality, and something that you can be influenced through. There's no reference to it only being when you're in the shape; as long as you're carrying the memories, you'll feel how the person felt about them. You <i>have</i> to, because if you act in a manner inconsistent with that (i.e. allow the Intimacy to decay), you'll lose the memories.<br /> <br /> So if you want to pass yourself off as a person that you've just killed, you won't only know about their spouse, children and friends, you'll have the same feelings about them. Apart from what that might do to a Lunar's personality, there's also the moral effect that it might have upon them; it's got to be kind of weird to suddenly fall in love with somebody, have the memory of having loved them for a while, and consider that you've actually murdered somebody that your loved one loved.<br /> <br /> And then, what, you're going to abandon him when your interests take you elsewhere? But you love him! I wouldn't find it unbelievable that there are a few Lunars that stole a person's shape and life for some pragmatic or ruthless reason, and then kind of abandoned that reason and spent the length of a mortal lifetime in that position because of the feelings that came with it. How's <i>that</i> for mercurial! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And then from the other side, well, it depends on how strong the Intimacy was natively. It may be that the spouse or children notice a certain cooling in the affections. Perhaps that will improve over time.<br /> <br /> This is more horrible than the Solar persona Charms, and I love it. This is the kind of thing that I was talking about wanting when I abandoned the playtest thread.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T16:29:25-07:00","id":1241064,"title":"","content":"I was more focused on the human-only target limitation. I'm inherently not a fan of mortal-target-only social Charms, because it creates an incentive to choose a less-limited alternative. A PC's player likes the idea, hates it only works on mortals, so here comes the Custom Charm for 15m, 1WP that does the same thing without the restriction, Prereq'd by this Charm, and this one becomes naught but a speedbump that's only utility is as a -5m discount when the target is human.<br /> <br /> I'd much rather the developers simply hike the price, and ditch the human-only tag. Taking human forms generally falls into two broad categories during play. 1) Not You: The point isn't who you are, it's simply not being recognized as yourself. Most PCs will keep two, maybe three such everymen/everywomen, and reuse as needed. 2) Specific impersonation: While there is a very significant minority of times the target-to-be-impersonated is human, IME it's a minority compared to the number of times a Dragon Blooded got eaten and replaced, or a Raksha. Supernatural entities tend to be at or near the top of any organization, and they're the ones tending to create the incentive to impersonate. The Guild WOULD be a major exception to this, except for the fact they've spent centuries creating security procedures precisely to prevent this kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","user":"Wyldwraith","date":". 07-31-2018, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T16:32:16-07:00","id":1241066,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that the Lunar only gets it as a Minor Tie, instead of the Major or Defining Tie that the target had. So, there is still definitely an emotion there, but I doubt it is as intense as you're describing there. Maybe not &quot;love&quot; as in head over heels, but possibly &quot;affection&quot; or &quot;fondness&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T16:41:45-07:00","id":1241069,"title":"","content":"Query are Dragonblooded still considered as &quot;Human&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T16:43:22-07:00","id":1241070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241034#post1241034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of mind-control effects, Solars are actually not great at being able to make social attacks that can't just be ignored for 1wp*. If they've found a way to make such a social attack, they're amazing at it. But they're not that great at getting the opportunity to do so.<br /> This is the problem our Zenith has; sure, he can regularly roll 25 successes on his social attacks, but people can just spend 1wp and bounce off the intimacy he's trying to inflict,** and he can't persuade people without them already having an intimacy that supports what he wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I agree. I'd have to reread the DB charms because I can't parse to many at a time, but the lunar charm just suppliments a roll as a minor tie. Which while it makes it harder to resist doesn't make it impossible. Last time I checked Solars had a bunch of psyche effects in performance and socialize just lets you understand and prey on any intimacy as you wish. I'd still have to reread it all. I will say the major problem with all these charms is how often you could parse through them. I used to know the old charmsets pretty well but that was when they were a fraction smaller than this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T16:51:23-07:00","id":1241073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241069#post1241069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query are Dragonblooded still considered as &quot;Human&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were last time I checked. Along with other Exalted, God-Blooded, and beastmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T18:15:25-07:00","id":1241096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241056#post1241056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looking back at this Charm, I realised something interesting and kind of messed up about how it works.<br /> <br /> So, you don't only get the memories, you get the Tie that came with them. That becomes a part of your personality, and something that you can be influenced through. There's no reference to it only being when you're in the shape; as long as you're carrying the memories, you'll feel how the person felt about them. You <i>have</i> to, because if you act in a manner inconsistent with that (i.e. allow the Intimacy to decay), you'll lose the memories.<br /> <br /> So if you want to pass yourself off as a person that you've just killed, you won't only know about their spouse, children and friends, you'll have the same feelings about them. Apart from what that might do to a Lunar's personality, there's also the moral effect that it might have upon them; it's got to be kind of weird to suddenly fall in love with somebody, have the memory of having loved them for a while, and consider that you've actually murdered somebody that your loved one loved.<br /> <br /> And then, what, you're going to abandon him when your interests take you elsewhere? But you love him! I wouldn't find it unbelievable that there are a few Lunars that stole a person's shape and life for some pragmatic or ruthless reason, and then kind of abandoned that reason and spent the length of a mortal lifetime in that position because of the feelings that came with it. How's <i>that</i> for mercurial! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And then from the other side, well, it depends on how strong the Intimacy was natively. It may be that the spouse or children notice a certain cooling in the affections. Perhaps that will improve over time.<br /> <br /> This is more horrible than the Solar persona Charms, and I love it. This is the kind of thing that I was talking about wanting when I abandoned the playtest thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m sure this pretty much brands me as a monster, but you could take that Sorcery initiation and Shaping Ritual that lets you burn Intimacies for motes if you want to quickly shake off the lingering feels you have from a successful infiltration mission. <br /> <br /> Maybe summon a Neomah or three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T00:34:03-07:00","id":1241193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241066#post1241066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that the Lunar only gets it as a Minor Tie, instead of the Major or Defining Tie that the target had. So, there is still definitely an emotion there, but I doubt it is as intense as you're describing there. Maybe not &quot;love&quot; as in head over heels, but possibly &quot;affection&quot; or &quot;fondness&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how the degrees of Ties work. Hell, in the core book, examples of Minor Ties of Love are actually given.<br /> <br /> The degree is simply about how far you're willing to go and what you're willing to sacrifice for the Tie, which is fair enough. I'm sure that most actual people who truly and deeply love their spouses and children aren't actually willing to, say, kill for them. I wouldn't doubt that the love of my parents is not real if there's no possibility of me convincing them to pull off a bank job to help me out of a jam.<br /> <br /> Really, how would that work if a Lunar was aping somebody's Defining Ties? There's no reason to assume that the emotional context of it changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T00:36:13-07:00","id":1241194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241096#post1241096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m sure this pretty much brands me as a monster, but you could take that Sorcery initiation and Shaping Ritual that lets you burn Intimacies for motes if you want to quickly shake off the lingering feels you have from a successful infiltration mission.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you could if you wanted to get a return out of it, but it's not necessary; just drop the mote commitment.<br /> <br /> Doing either thing still robs you of the memories, so it varies by circumstance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T01:03:39-07:00","id":1241196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241194#post1241194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, you could if you wanted to get a return out of it, but it's not necessary; just drop the mote commitment.<br /> <br /> Doing either thing still robs you of the memories, so it varies by circumstance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does dropping the commitment remove the tie? If so, can you later recommit the motes for the memories again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T01:13:27-07:00","id":1241199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241064#post1241064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was more focused on the human-only target limitation. I'm inherently not a fan of mortal-target-only social Charms, because it creates an incentive to choose a less-limited alternative. A PC's player likes the idea, hates it only works on mortals, so here comes the Custom Charm for 15m, 1WP that does the same thing without the restriction, Prereq'd by this Charm, and this one becomes naught but a speedbump that's only utility is as a -5m discount when the target is human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalts are humans. If it only worked on mortals, that's what would it say.<br /> It just doesn't work on animals, spirits, ghosts, Dragon Kings, Mountain Folk, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T01:38:30-07:00","id":1241200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241070#post1241070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if I agree. I'd have to reread the DB charms because I can't parse to many at a time, but the lunar charm just suppliments a roll as a minor tie. Which while it makes it harder to resist doesn't make it impossible. Last time I checked Solars had a bunch of psyche effects in performance and socialize just lets you understand and prey on any intimacy as you wish. I'd still have to reread it all. I will say the major problem with all these charms is how often you could parse through them. I used to know the old charmsets pretty well but that was when they were a fraction smaller than this.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, they do have some mind control charms (and not that many, like 2 in Presence), but other than that there's hardly anything that helps either be able to Persuade people at all, or stops people just spending 1wp to bounce off your Instill.<br /> (The one exception is seduction)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, after seeing other people play Solar social characters, and re-reading the social trees a few times, I've just stayed away. I buy a decent Presence score to convince mortals of stuff, Wise-Eyed Courtier Method to find out people's intimacies, and that's it. For simply making social attacks (which, except against other Exalts, I tend to find aren't that hard to get enough successes on) I find most of the Presence and Performance trees not very useful. My friend is quite bored of his amazing preacher, because he can convince mortals to join his Cult but has no luck convincing Exalts of, well, anything.* <br /> <br /> Unlike DB Presence, which is chock full of useful social charms that do things like count people as having intimacies, restrict the intimacies people can use to defend, make Instill or Inspire rolls require Decision points rather than just a WP to resist, etc.<br /> For DBs, getting enough successes might not be such a certainty, but you do more than bounce off their WP and wonder what the point of buying all those dice-trick charms was.<br /> <br /> *Admittedly, he accidentally convinced the Dawn to invade the Eclipse's kingdom. It was very embarrassing, as he was trying to get them to make peace.<br /> <br /> I actually re-read the Presence and Performance charms since we were talking about, and I did find a Performance charm I'd not noticed before (it's at the top of a pretty generic tree) that makes social influence much harder to resist, Soul-Bracing Momentous Power. I might advise my friend to get it, though I'm not sure how much of the prereqs he has.<br /> However, there really is hardly anything beyond Hypnotic Tongue (which is both blatant mind-control) that lets you persuade people when they don't already have an intimacy strong enough to align with what you want. <br /> <br /> Whereas the DBs have plenty, and the single Lunar charm we've seen so far already lets you walk up to people and count them as having a certain minor intimacy, which you can then make Persuade attempts off of.<br /> It's only minor, so it's not amazing, but it is only 1 charm we've seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T01:43:13-07:00","id":1241201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241196#post1241196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does dropping the commitment remove the tie?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an Indefinite Charm; by definition, its effects are only sustained if you maintain the mote commitment for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, can you later recommit the motes for the memories again?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say no, since it says that it needs to be used upon completion of a sacred hunt. If you lose that Intimacy or drop the mote, there's probably no getting it back.<br /> <br /> I had actually not recalled a certain detail before, though; it <i>does</i> say that you only have the memories while assuming the shape that held them originally.<br /> <br /> I'll also note something I realised about my previous statement: a Minor Tie can still be love, but that it's limited in what you can be compelled to or are likely to give up for it means that there are probably not many situations in which a Lunar actually <i>would</i> drop what they're doing for it. Not unless what they were doing would only mildly inconvenience them to leave.<br /> <br /> A given Lunar might personally elect to for whatever reason (perhaps especially if doing so would be consistent with an already existing and higher levelled Intimacy, such as a Principle related to familial obligations). I would also say that it can be a reasonable foundation for the Intimacy growing organically, if they interact extensively with the new family, or similar people.<br /> <br /> But being a Minor Tie does mean that there's a lot that you won't give up for it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T05:43:38-07:00","id":1241257,"title":"","content":"Funny thought: A Lunar could use Memory-Drinking Meditation to see what the prey knows about the Lunar herself, or at least the face by which he knows her.<br /> <br /> Pretty thoroughly reveals whether or not he has discovered her secrets or conceals a plan to betray her.<br /> <br /> Of course I\u2019m assuming that she hunted him with Heart-Drinking Allure, so that he is still alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-01-2018, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T07:15:23-07:00","id":1241296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241193#post1241193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how the degrees of Ties work. Hell, in the core book, examples of Minor Ties of Love are actually given.<br /> <br /> The degree is simply about how far you're willing to go and what you're willing to sacrifice for the Tie, which is fair enough. I'm sure that most actual people who truly and deeply love their spouses and children aren't actually willing to, say, kill for them. I wouldn't doubt that the love of my parents is not real if there's no possibility of me convincing them to pull off a bank job to help me out of a jam.<br /> <br /> Really, how would that work if a Lunar was aping somebody's Defining Ties? There's no reason to assume that the emotional context of it changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I had to refamliarize myself with the Intimacy rules. Still, as a Minor Tie it is something that has much less impact on the Lunar's actions as compared to a Major or Defining Tie.<br /> <br /> But still, it does show that there is an interesting &quot;weakness&quot; in this Charm requiring you to maintain a Minor Tie in that it allows an avenue for your Lunar to be swayed in their actions similarly to how the person they're using the shape of could be swayed. Remember though that Minor Intimacies are defined as &quot;Minor Intimacies are notable relationships or beliefs that have some influence over a character's actions without being an integral part of who he is.&quot; I think if a Lunar had the Minor Tie of &quot;My Kids (Love)&quot; due to eating their mother, it's possible the Lunar could be influenced to balk at harming the kids while the Lunar is maintaining that Minor Tie. Beyond situations directly involving the kids, though, that wouldn't really be a useful Intimacy for someone else to really take advantage of that I can see...<br /> <br /> Edit: And just caught up to where you're noting that... I should really go through the entire thread before replying to something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 08-01-2018, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T07:24:11-07:00","id":1241298,"title":"","content":"Interesting use case for Memory-Drinking Meditation. It's not a Charm that really requires opposition or a sense of being an antagonist to really make use of.<br /> <br /> Let us say that there is someone that you care about. By taking their shape through a non-lethal means, you can acquire Minor Ties to the Intimacies that they have Major or Defining Ties to, granting you their knowledge and memories about those Ties, to better inform you as to what kind of activities they would want to have happen in regards to those Ties. Through this, you can better capability to be a greater influence over their goals in seeing them through fruition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T07:45:53-07:00","id":1241303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241296#post1241296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if a Lunar had the Minor Tie of &quot;My Kids (Love)&quot; due to eating their mother, it's possible the Lunar could be influenced to balk at harming the kids while the Lunar is maintaining that Minor Tie. Beyond situations directly involving the kids, though, that wouldn't really be a useful Intimacy for someone else to really take advantage of that I can see...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind, I'm suddenly thinking about circumstances in which somebody could use Instil actions to make the Tie stronger. I haven't looked at those rules in a while, but I think... that evidence is only a necessity and a help for persuade actions, and that Instilling stronger Ties requires a complementary Intimacy?<br /> <br /> That brings me back to a question that I've had a few times in the past; how deliberate certain kinds of social action necessarily need to be. I think there's a case to be made for the social interaction system being descriptive rather than proscriptive, and that it's valid to use it to model occasions in which somebody just being themselves is resolved by rolling appropriate actions. You're in the presence of some earnest charity worker who's just doing their thing and talking about their own passion for it, and they're not <i>looking</i> to influence you, but it still gets rolled as Charisma + Presence or Socialize and, if successful, your feelings change or you start doing a thing.<br /> <br /> I absolutely think that the new system is better than the old one, but there's still a niggling doubt that it rests too much on everybody trying to work an angle, and this is a point that might put it to rest.<br /> <br /> In which case, it might leave a scenario in which the Lunar's existing personality is amenable, and the kids just being themselves constitute actions that strengthen your Tie to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T07:53:49-07:00","id":1241306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241303#post1241303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind, I'm suddenly thinking about circumstances in which somebody could use Instil actions to make the Tie stronger. I haven't looked at those rules in a while, but I think... that evidence is only a necessity and a help for persuade actions, and that Instilling stronger Ties requires a complementary Intimacy?<br /> <br /> That brings me back to a question that I've had a few times in the past; how deliberate certain kinds of social action necessarily need to be. I think there's a case to be made for the social interaction system being descriptive rather than proscriptive, and that it's valid to use it to model occasions in which somebody just being themselves is resolved by rolling appropriate actions. You're in the presence of some earnest charity worker who's just doing their thing and talking about their own passion for it, and they're not <i>looking</i> to influence you, but it still gets rolled as Charisma + Presence or Socialize and, if successful, your feelings change or you start doing a thing.<br /> <br /> I absolutely think that the new system is better than the old one, but there's still a niggling doubt that it rests too much on everybody trying to work an angle, and this is a point that might put it to rest.<br /> <br /> In which case, it might leave a scenario in which the Lunar's existing personality is amenable, and the kids just being themselves constitute actions that strengthen your Tie to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm all for making the system more flexible. But... It's hard to see how the system can really effectively model that. I mean... Do you really expect children to have sufficient Charisma + Presence or Socialize to really strengthen the Intimacy of an Exalt?<br /> <br /> Might be better to disengage from that system and work it from the angle of the Exalt's Player and the Storyteller both needing to agree that a Minor Intimacy gets strengthened to Major or Defining based on interaction with the kids. It doesn't necessarily need dice rolls for it, just the agreement between Player and ST that &quot;This might be fun to play out.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T08:37:15-07:00","id":1241323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241306#post1241306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm all for making the system more flexible. But... It's hard to see how the system can really effectively model that. I mean... Do you really expect children to have sufficient Charisma + Presence or Socialize to really strengthen the Intimacy of an Exalt?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what Intimacies the Exalt already has, what their Resolve actually is, and their general disposition.<br /> <br /> It's not the kind of thing where I would say that being unexpected or unconscious means you don't get to use Resolve bolstering Charms, but my inclination is to assume that there's a reasonable number of situations in which an Exalt will not really want to close themselves off so thoroughly.<br /> <br /> That can include situations where they don't expect to be moved by interactions with children, and surprise themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be better to disengage from that system and work it from the angle of the Exalt's Player and the Storyteller both needing to agree that a Minor Intimacy gets strengthened to Major or Defining based on interaction with the kids. It doesn't necessarily need dice rolls for it, just the agreement between Player and ST that &quot;This might be fun to play out.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure that's an angle that can work as well, but I warrant that part of the fun of such things literally falling on the roll of the dice is the uncertainty around it, and how that can lend a degree of credibility and verisimilitude to the idea of a character being influenced despite what they would have expected.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T08:51:24-07:00","id":1241328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241323#post1241323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on what Intimacies the Exalt already has, what their Resolve actually is, and their general disposition.<br /> <br /> It's not the kind of thing where I would say that being unexpected or unconscious means you don't get to use Resolve bolstering Charms, but my inclination is to assume that there's a reasonable number of situations in which an Exalt will not really want to close themselves off so thoroughly.<br /> <br /> That can include situations where they don't expect to be moved by interactions with children, and surprise themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure that's an angle that can work as well, but I warrant that part of the fun of such things literally falling on the roll of the dice is the uncertainty around it, and how that can lend a degree of credibility and verisimilitude to the idea of a character being influenced despite what they would have expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you really want the random factor of the dice determining such a thing... I dunno. I can't say I'm really comfortable enough with the system to really judge how to work out this kind of a use-case. <br /> <br /> But if you figure something out, I'd be interested in hearing about it! ^.^<br /> <br /> Also, isn't it really interesting that you don't lose the Minor Intimacy when you let Memory-Drinking Meditation go? That uh... Would actually make me less apt to make use of it willy nilly... I could see a Lunar making an utter emotional wreck of themselves by using MDM too much...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:37:21-07:00","id":1241345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241328#post1241328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, isn't it really interesting that you don't lose the Minor Intimacy when you let Memory-Drinking Meditation go? That uh... Would actually make me less apt to make use of it willy nilly... I could see a Lunar making an utter emotional wreck of themselves by using MDM too much...</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't lose the intimacy, but I can't see any reason why you can't just choose to degrade it as normal. However, I can see also wanting to keep the Tie - depending on how you read the charm, I think keeping the tie could possibly allow you to re-activate Memory-Drinking Meditation for that particular intimacy at a later time, preserving the possibility of memory access.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:39:38-07:00","id":1241346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241345#post1241345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't lose the intimacy, but I can't see any reason why you can't just choose to degrade it as normal. However, I can see also wanting to keep the Tie - depending on how you read the charm, I think keeping the tie could possibly allow you to re-activate Memory-Drinking Meditation for that particular intimacy at a later time, preserving the possibility of memory access.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Dev supported that... Saying that you have to activate the Charm at the time you gain the shape. But still...<br /> <br /> Yes, you can degrade the Minor Intimacies as normal... But that still takes time and effort to do. My point being, this would probably not be a very stable seeming Lunar. But, doesn't that also fit into the mercurial themes of the moon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:57:59-07:00","id":1241357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241346#post1241346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you can degrade the Minor Intimacies as normal... But that still takes time and effort to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much of either, though. As long as the ST agrees it's appropriate, you can degrade a minor intimacy away at the end of a scene, without rolling or anything. As an ST, I'd allow a Lunar to drop the intimacy created through MDM at the end of a scene they dropped the commitment to it, or at the end of the next scene at the very latest.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T19:05:47-07:00","id":1241624,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> If social influence began working as you described, Ie: The charity worker's passion influencing others unconsciously, wouldn't that create a sort of implicit change in characters' understanding of their world? Where can you model the line of what amounts to the level of mechanical understanding of the social dynamic at work? If unconscious influence and conscious influence were using the same &quot;system&quot; in effect, how does that change the perceptions of say, someone who doesn't WANT to be tugged in different directions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T14:57:29-07:00","id":1243034,"title":"","content":"I had a notion:<br /> <br /> It may never actually be elaborated upon, but until such time as it is (and, in the absence of it ever being so), that conflict between Solars and Lunars that created the Bond?<br /> <br /> I'm going to assume that was a fight over the fate of the Caul.<br /> <br /> Specifically, a fight in the manner that I suggested when I first read the Caul preview; that the Solars (along with the Sidereals) were a bit squirrelly about a place sacred to a Primordial, even one that was on their side, enduring in the world, and advocating for its destruction, set against objections from the Lunars and Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> For the time being, I'm going to assume that it didn't take very long for that argument to come to a head, and a cabal of Solars, Sidereals and associated troops landed on the shores of the Caul with that intent, and the Lunars (basically all of them) completely lost their shit over it. Many lineages and nations of Dragon Blooded went with them, but the major thing would have been that there were a lot of Solars who saw what the utmost wrath of the Lunars looked like when it was pointed at them, and a significant number of those Solars blinked.<br /> <br /> \u2026 I'm not sure if this works if the Bond works out as something that favours the Solars... for the time being, I'm going to assume that it benefits the Lunars enough, with an edge of saving the Caul being something worthwhile enough to accept a major compromise to get such a threat to back off.<br /> <br /> Performing a pilgrimage to the Last City when it opened for the Lunar shrines was not <i>necessary</i> to effect that transformation in the Lunars that did it, but it helped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T19:58:43-07:00","id":1243099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241624#post1241624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> If social influence began working as you described, Ie: The charity worker's passion influencing others unconsciously, wouldn't that create a sort of implicit change in characters' understanding of their world? Where can you model the line of what amounts to the level of mechanical understanding of the social dynamic at work? If unconscious influence and conscious influence were using the same &quot;system&quot; in effect, how does that change the perceptions of say, someone who doesn't WANT to be tugged in different directions?</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who works in the interpersonal and social sciences, I think that the social system models reality fairly well in this regard. I have, over the course of my career, bought several dots of Socialize, Presence, and Performance, and as a result of my regular use of those Abilities, I tend to see the world through a lens that enables their use. It isn't that I'm always expressly trying to convince people of my worldview--it's that I now consciously recognize the extent to which I am often unconsciously trying to spread my worldview. By consistently being myself (the person who has decent ratings in these Abilities), I the character may sometimes make social influence rolls that I didn't consciously choose. In the narrative of my life, this choice often rests in the hands of my player or in prompts from the Storyteller (e.g. &quot;I'd like to ask you to roll Charisma + Performance to see what kind of impact this impassioned speech has on the listeners.&quot;).<br /> <br /> The perception of someone who doesn't want to buy into my (or anyone else's) worldview may be that I'm spouting a party line or that I've been brainwashed by my psychology training or that what I'm saying makes sense but conflicts with a valued relationship, all of which is reflected by Intimacies that would bolster their Resolve. All human communication is, on some level, an attempt to express, reify, and get feedback on a worldview, consciously or not, so few people consciously view these unconscious social influence rolls as conscious manipulation. Unless they're deeply distrustful of people in general (which is itself an Intimacy) they're more likely to view my casual influence as a series of memes and information to sift through and either accept into their worldview or reject on its own merits, relatively unconscious of the effects that, say, my Appearance has on the perceived merits of said memes/information. When my influence appears more conscious, that may affect whether they spend Willpower or apply different Intimacies.<br /> <br /> I've been writing all day and am kind of dazed from low blood sugar, so hopefully that all made sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T05:19:36-07:00","id":1243173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241064#post1241064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was more focused on the human-only target limitation. I'm inherently not a fan of mortal-target-only social Charms, because it creates an incentive to choose a less-limited alternative. A PC's player likes the idea, hates it only works on mortals, so here comes the Custom Charm for 15m, 1WP that does the same thing without the restriction, Prereq'd by this Charm, and this one becomes naught but a speedbump that's only utility is as a -5m discount when the target is human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted that we're entirely absent of full details at this point, but I do expect to houserule away that kind of limitation, or to put some paths around it. That's because my anticipated stories would include Malfean and Spirit Court interactions. Having a situation where a fraction of your stuff stops working isn't what I'd want to work around or burn fun time on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T05:32:42-07:00","id":1243175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1241201#post1241201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an Indefinite Charm; by definition, its effects are only sustained if you maintain the mote commitment for it.<br /> <br /> [snip]</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Lunar is acting out the Intimacy, would that begin to sustain it, even if the motes were dropped?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T06:46:44-07:00","id":1243195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1243175#post1243175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Lunar is acting out the Intimacy, would that begin to sustain it, even if the motes were dropped?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Devs corrected. That Intimacy sticks around even if the motes are dropped. Its a permanent part of your character until you get rid of it the usual way. (I recommend Neomah hookers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T06:52:23-07:00","id":1243196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1243195#post1243195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I recommend Neomah hookers).</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer Neomah courtesans. More sex-positive, that way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-06-2018, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T07:27:03-07:00","id":1243204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1243195#post1243195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Devs corrected. That Intimacy sticks around even if the motes are dropped. Its a permanent part of your character until you get rid of it the usual way. (I recommend Neomah hookers).</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. That seems like a good way to accumulate a lot of ... baggage.<br /> <br /> I'm almost pondering that being an influence on Lunar Limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T20:09:49-07:00","id":1243380,"title":"","content":"I'm also kinda interested in the prospect of the Lunar intentionally fostering an Intimacy in their intended prey so that the Lunar can then access the related memories when they eventually steal the human's shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T20:14:46-07:00","id":1243381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1243380#post1243380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also kinda interested in the prospect of the Lunar intentionally fostering an Intimacy in their intended prey so that the Lunar can then access the related memories when they eventually steal the human's shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that logic works.<br /> <br /> Unless you mean that you inspire someone to love or hate someone else, so that they seek to learn as much about that person as possible, effectively becoming your unwitting spy, with you taking their Heart's Blood working as an information drop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T21:09:22-07:00","id":1243390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1243381#post1243381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you mean that you inspire someone to love or hate someone else, so that they seek to learn as much about that person as possible, effectively becoming your unwitting spy, with you taking their Heart's Blood working as an information drop.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> I'm talking more where Lunar Carlos might want to get in with Dynast Alice by taking Dynast Bob's shape, but realizes Bob hasn't actually seen Alice in twenty years, and has allowed the Intimacy to fade; Carlos socially maneuvers Bob into remembering &quot;the good old days&quot; with Alice, mechanically represented with an Instill action; their connection rekindled in Bob's heart, Carlos then thrusts his moonsilver claws into Bob's chest; later, when Alice visits, &quot;Bob&quot; remembers the Wyld Hunts they went on together with perfect clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T05:09:47-07:00","id":1243459,"title":"","content":"Regarding the prior two posts: GetBoth.jpg","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T06:07:03-07:00","id":1243473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1243459#post1243459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the prior two posts: GetBoth.jpg</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Get Both&quot; doesn't quite work when one of the two options is to specifically exclude the other.<br /> <br /> \u200bI can't order a burger &quot;with ketchup&quot; and &quot;with mustard <i>but no ketchup</i>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T06:09:43-07:00","id":1243477,"title":"","content":"I think he\u2019s saying that each application is just as valid, and I would agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T06:24:03-07:00","id":1243479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1243477#post1243477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he\u2019s saying that each application is just as valid, and I would agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>But yours was saying that the logic on mine doesn't work, suggesting yours as an alternative. Have you since changed your mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-07-2018, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T06:30:18-07:00","id":1243482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1243477#post1243477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he\u2019s saying that each application is just as valid, and I would agree.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>[Two-handed Burger Conquering Attitude]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1+ Resources ; <b>Mins:</b> Stamina 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous, Delicious<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The Lunar's quarry has momentarily evaded his doom, and her hunger knows no limit. She pauses for a lunch, becoming a whirlwind of comestible destruction. Alternating bites from the foodstuffs in each hand, the Lunar refuels herself, and strikes terror (and splatter) upon those who stand too near. This Charm augments an attempt to persist in the Lunar's endeavors: Add one success to any attempt to perform a feat of endurance, and reroll any &quot;1&quot; appearing on this attempt, up to a number equal to Resources spent on the Lunar's lunch break. Additionally, this Charm has the side effect of instilling an emotion of terror (watching a hungry Lunar eat) or disgust (condiments splattering in all directions) on anyone watching who does not already have a positive Intimacy toward the Lunar herself. Use of this Charm doubles a Stunt's Willpower reward (if it is eligible for one) if the player gets the Storyteller something from the kitchen while they're up. If the player actually brought food for the group this session, use of this Charm triples the Willpower reward instead.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T06:57:07-07:00","id":1243489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1243380#post1243380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also kinda interested in the prospect of the Lunar intentionally fostering an Intimacy in their intended prey so that the Lunar can then access the related memories when they eventually steal the human's shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know... if they didn't have an Intimacy before, how many memories do they have of the subject, and are they even worth stealing? It seems kind of circuitous to me.<br /> <br /> Hmmm...<br /> <br /> Okay, looking at your follow up example, I guess there's something in the idea of a sufficiently long-lived person gaining and dropping Intimacies, but... it feels like a bit of an edge case. For one thing, it raises the question of whether or not the desired memories might be associated with another Intimacy that is still fresh (if the character has a Principle connected to the Wyld Hunt in any way, that would cover those interactions). Also the matter of whether or not its necessary to acquire memory of something incidental in a character's life to pass off as them. Or there's something assumed to be in the memories themselves that the Lunar wants to learn, and needs to cultivate an avenue to access them (which is still not covered by a more fresh Intimacy). <br /> <br /> {checks again}<br /> <br /> Wait, no, the forgotten Dynast herself is the target, and it's about finding a way to access her while also wanting to ensure that you get actual information... and I guess that anybody that is part of her life at the moment is not a convenient target? Mind, it seems to me that when the connection is that lapsed, it's not very difficult to use the same kind of trickery that con artists regularly use to convince strangers that they attended school together, where any gaps can be attributed to having forgotten in the intervening time. Not unless Dynast Alice (or Bob, technically) has a reputation for having the infallible memory that some Dragon Blooded powers can afford.<br /> <br /> I suppose if one wants to play a Lunar that is being especially meticulous, but it does feel like a very specific circumstance, and a bit of a solution looking for a problem.<br /> <br /> {reflects}<br /> <br /> Hmm, that might be a bit of pedantic nitpickery on my own part, there. If I'm thinking more objectively, I can see that part of the fun of magic can be coming up with curious or novel applications and reverse engineering them into scenarios that call for it.<br /> <br /> I don't ultimately have a point here, it's just my train of thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T17:41:24-07:00","id":1243653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1243479#post1243479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yours was saying that the logic on mine doesn't work, suggesting yours as an alternative. Have you since changed your mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, yes, you showed me how your method worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:50:40-07:00","id":1245897,"title":"","content":"Woop woop, Lunars in 2nd draft. Any speculations how long from that until we see things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10762-asoral","name":"Asoral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:55:19-07:00","id":1245935,"title":"","content":"The Dragonblood book reached 2nd draft in July 2017, and the kickstarter (with the raw text released to backers) was in March 2018.<br /> <br /> So maybe a similar timeframe.<br /> <br /> However, I suspect they won't want to do the Lunar Kickstarter at the same time as they release the Dragonblood book, I expect they'll want to stagger them a bit. But I'm no expert in driving RPG sales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:57:54-07:00","id":1246006,"title":"","content":"As much as I understand the desire to extrapolate from available information, I'm not sure it's gonna produce any results here that are anywhere near accurate. The two books have had very different life cycles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T12:06:34-07:00","id":1246012,"title":"","content":"Hey, Vance, what happens if a Lunar kills someone or something they don't have the right Charms to acquire the form for yet? Is it lost forever, or can they assume that form after they finally get the Charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T12:28:38-07:00","id":1246021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1246012#post1246012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Vance, what happens if a Lunar kills someone or something they don't have the right Charms to acquire the form for yet? Is it lost forever, or can they assume that form after they finally get the Charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only situations that might apply to are animals with Legendary Size or Minuscule Size. In those cases, you still take their heart's blood, you just can't shift into their forms until you have the appropriate Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T12:40:53-07:00","id":1246025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1243482#post1243482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>[Two-handed Burger Conquering Attitude]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1+ Resources ; <b>Mins:</b> Stamina 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous, Delicious<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The Lunar's quarry has momentarily evaded his doom, and her hunger knows no limit. She pauses for a lunch, becoming a whirlwind of comestible destruction. Alternating bites from the foodstuffs in each hand, the Lunar refuels herself, and strikes terror (and splatter) upon those who stand too near. This Charm augments an attempt to persist in the Lunar's endeavors: Add one success to any attempt to perform a feat of endurance, and reroll any &quot;1&quot; appearing on this attempt, up to a number equal to Resources spent on the Lunar's lunch break. Additionally, this Charm has the side effect of instilling an emotion of terror (watching a hungry Lunar eat) or disgust (condiments splattering in all directions) on anyone watching who does not already have a positive Intimacy toward the Lunar herself. Use of this Charm doubles a Stunt's Willpower reward (if it is eligible for one) if the player gets the Storyteller something from the kitchen while they're up. If the player actually brought food for the group this session, use of this Charm triples the Willpower reward instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disgust at <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qnF_P4U7xBU\" target=\"_blank\">witnessing a meal</a>, you say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T12:46:38-07:00","id":1246026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1246006#post1246006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I understand the desire to extrapolate from available information, I'm not sure it's gonna produce any results here that are anywhere near accurate. The two books have had very different life cycles.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T18:40:30-07:00","id":1246146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1246025#post1246025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Disgust at <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qnF_P4U7xBU\" target=\"_blank\">witnessing a meal</a>, you say?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know fully well that everything exists on the internet. Yet, I stand amazed that you found something so apropos to the discussion!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T19:06:11-07:00","id":1246151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1246146#post1246146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know fully well that everything exists on the internet. Yet, I stand amazed that you found something so apropos to the discussion!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hijikata's preoccupation with mayo is fertile ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T06:33:28-07:00","id":1249370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/20067-ask-a-question-get-an-answer?p=1249355#post1249355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tamuse and Lilit disagree with you. OK, it was a brainwashing charm, but the very point that the charm was created specifically against Lunars (and no against another Exalted) is symptomatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Btw, is there new information about Lunar concept as a whole? Both &quot;burn-rape-and-pillage'-savages and 'progresors-creators of new societies' seems to be a fail. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T06:34:55-07:00","id":1249371,"title":"","content":"Guess I'll repost what I wrote in the other thread here:<br /> <br /> 3e lunars are engaged in guerrilla war against the realm. They're not trying to tear down civilisation in general, just one specific civilisation they have a longstanding beef with. And then they plan to build something better in it's place. They also go around marshalling various barbarian tribes against the realm as part of this. The tribes might fall, and often do, but by then the Lunar is off training another one. It's like, a constant war of attrition. And there are established lunar kingdoms here and there. They basically control 90% of the caul, which the dragonblooded really want back.<br /> <br /> Oh, side note: apparently they are getting spells at a discount if they favour intelligence now, so that's neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T06:42:15-07:00","id":1249374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249371#post1249371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then they plan to build something better in it's place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that they do. I think they're just looking to be free from Wyld Hunts and the lingering mystical attachment to something calling itself the Realm, at which point it will just become a matter of being able to go where they want and do as they please as the mightiest beings upon the Earth.<br /> <br /> Because the other thing to see about Lunars, as they were presented in the core book, is that they have a big thing about escaping the confines that society would place upon them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T06:47:01-07:00","id":1249376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249374#post1249374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that they do. I think they're just looking to be free from Wyld Hunts and the lingering mystical attachment to something calling itself the Realm, at which point it will just become a matter of being able to go where they want and do as they please as the mightiest beings upon the Earth.<br /> <br /> Because the other thing to see about Lunars, as they were presented in the core book, is that they have a big thing about escaping the confines that society would place upon them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Lunars always got backlash about their 'idea-less'. But if you ask me, it should be an option for them to enchance and wide Wild. Not Raksha chaos, but exactly Wild, as their second home.<br /> Also, I hate the idea of them as subordinates to Solars. Look, everyone is subordinate, but 2E Lunars (by design) seems to be a personal slaves in contrast with Siderials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 08-28-2018, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T06:55:05-07:00","id":1249378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249376#post1249376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you ask me, it should be an option for them to enchance and wide Wild. Not Raksha chaos, but exactly Wild, as their second home.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can likely do things like that, and I would imagine plausible character concepts of people whose friction with society leads to rejection and a kind of hermitage. But I doubt they would be limited to it, or specifically about it.<br /> <br /> There are going to be a number of things about lurking within society as well. A more diverse array of methods for acquiring human shapes. More things that can be done with those shapes (an Intelligence Charm to acquire their information, Protean Charms to harness other people's Intimacies towards the shape). At least one Charm to manipulate societies by playing off of social mores that many Lunars are likely separate from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I hate the idea of them as subordinates to Solars. Look, everyone is subordinate, but 2E Lunars (by design) seems to be a personal slaves in contrast with Siderials.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are supposed to be Lunars who hate the idea as well, but I get the impression that your feelings are strong enough that some of what will come up will end up disappointing you.<br /> <br /> Barring the option to play one of the Lunars that never had a bond.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T07:05:38-07:00","id":1249385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249378#post1249378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can likely do things like that, and I would imagine plausible character concepts of people whose friction with society leads to rejection and a kind of hermitage. But I doubt they would be limited to it, or specifically about it.<br /> <br /> There are going to be a number of things about lurking within society as well. A more diverse array of methods for acquiring human shapes. More things that can be done with those shapes (an Intelligence Charm to acquire their information, Protean Charms to harness other people's Intimacies towards the shape). At least one Charm to manipulate societies by playing off of social mores that many Lunars are likely separate from.</div> </div> </div> </div>You speak about methods, not the purpose of Lunars. And they should have one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 08-28-2018, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T07:10:00-07:00","id":1249387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249378#post1249378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are supposed to be Lunars who hate the idea as well, but I get the impression that your feelings are strong enough that some of what will come up will end up disappointing you.<br /> Barring the option to play one of the Lunars that never had a bond.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just hate idea for Lunars to be inferior to Solar (well, more than Siderials were). And with old nod, they clearly were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T07:11:05-07:00","id":1249389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249385#post1249385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You speak about methods, not the purpose of Lunars. And they should have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> I mean, I expect the purpose of Lunars is to be people that struggled against various kinds of bondage and confinement who, with the grace of Luna, are provided with the means to pursue and achieve their own ultimate freedom, but I believe you mean something more outwardly focused.<br /> <br /> Mind, in this Edition, they had a function in the First Age as guardians of the Realm, but that was still less intrinsic to their own powers and more a function adopted by how they had bonded to the Solars and the Realm. And it's a function that broke with the fall of the Old Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T07:14:06-07:00","id":1249391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249387#post1249387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hate idea for Lunars to be inferior to Solar</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what to tell you. The Solars are still the strongest of the Exalted, and had the highest rank in the First Age. It actually kind of goes further now than it ever did, since Solars have the unique capacity to use Charms in a specific Ability above their current Essence level, and Martial Arts have a keyword denoting superior use by Solars.<br /> <br /> I think the most important thing to focus on is Lunars being impressive and formidable and providing a distinct play experience in their own right, rather than the fact that Solars still form the upper limit of what the Exalted can do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T07:28:51-07:00","id":1249397,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve spent maybe 15 years trying to think of some unique purpose or contribution to humanity that Lunars could have apart from any other kind of Exalt.<br /> <br /> I failed.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s fine. Especially now that we have Liminal and Getimian and Exigent and numerous other Exalted. <br /> <br /> Luna wanted to make Exalted to fight for her in the War of the Gods, and she Chooses mortals that she wants to adopt as children, or take as lovers. There doesn\u2019t need to be more to it than that.<br /> <br /> Indeed, not having purpose beyond that could be what makes them unique among Exalted. Luna didn\u2019t make them to do anything, she made them to love them.<br /> <br /> The Lunars have always called themselves Luna\u2019s Beloved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T07:31:36-07:00","id":1249399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249391#post1249391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know what to tell you. The Solars are still the strongest of the Exalted, and had the highest rank in the First Age. It actually kind of goes further now than it ever did, since Solars have the unique capacity to use Charms in a specific Ability above their current Essence level, and Martial Arts have a keyword denoting superior use by Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this and that's not the my point. My point that Lunars in very worst situation comparing to Sidereals (another world second finest). Not in Age of Sorrow but at al,l by design. Siderials were not directly conected to Solars which indicates their superior nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T07:33:41-07:00","id":1249400,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... while Supernal is a very potent effect, I suspect Lunars will still end up being closer to Solar power than they were in 2nd ed. Though I think they'll also be a bit less comparable, by virtue of being more different than in 2nd ed (where they had a large number of charms that were just nerfed Solar charms).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249385#post1249385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You speak about methods, not the purpose of Lunars. And they should have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the purpose of Solars? To defeat the Primordials.<br /> What's the purpose of Dragonblood? To defeat the Primordials.<br /> What's the purpose of Sidereals? To defeat the Primordials.*<br /> What's the purpose of Lunars? To defeat the Primordials.<br /> They all had the same purpose, only their methods differed.<br /> <br /> You'll notice this has already been done.<br /> <br /> After the Primordial War, the Exalted were given a new purpose of course; to rule humanity (partly as a reward, partly so the Gods didn't have to).<br /> But that was pretty unspecific, and they weren't <i>designed</i> to rule humanity. They just happened to be fairly skilled at it, because they were superhumans, and things like the super-power of being really good at organising an army can be translated to being really good at an organising a kingdom (though there are issues with that, but I'm not going to go into that now).<br /> <br /> *To be fair, Sidereals were given a specific purpose by their Creators after the end of the Primordial War. But the others were not.<br /> <br /> What's the purpose of Liminals? There isn't one. Exigents? It varies. Alchemicals? In 2nd ed it was just to be prototype Exalted, don't know if that would still be true. Getimians? I don't know, but as they were sealed away and only found and released later to fight Heaven, I'm not sure that is their original purpose, tbh.<br /> <br /> Only Abyssals and Infernals have a single purpose that they actually, generally, fulfilling (revenge), because they're new. They were designed for the Age of Sorrows, the other Exalts weren't, they were designed for the Primordial War. Charms for doing extra damage to Dragonblood would be far more useful to the Solars than Charms for doing extra damage to demons, but they were designed to fight demons, not Dragonblood, so anti-demon charms is what they have.<br /> <br /> So Lunars don't need to have a current purpose. It may be that many of them have a similar purpose (that's why about a lot are in the Silver Pact; their purpose is to destroy the Realm), but that's not something built into them (which is why many are not trying to destroy the Realm, they're doing other things).<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, this is all an in-game explanation.<br /> Out-of-game? The purpose of Lunars is to let you play certain kinds of character that the other Exalts are not great at. Monstrous anti-heroes, were-creatures, trickster-spirits, shapeshifters, heroes with a totem animal, shamans, bestial berzerkers, semi-human freaks, etc. But that doesn't require a specific in-game purpose, and in fact a specific in-game purpose can be detrimental and sometimes odd.<br /> <br /> For example, in 2nd ed the Lunars' purpose was the Thousand Streams River Project. Which a lot of people thought was ridiculous (I didn't, but I could see that it distracted from the themes of the game), and it did dissuade you from having Lunar Beast-King PCs or NPCs, which was a pity.<br /> <br /> If their purpose was destroy the Realm, that'd be weird if your game was set really deep in the Threshold. If their purpose was to defend Creation from the Raksha (which is something Luna does), that'd be weird if your game was set in, say, the Deshan Slave States, on the coast opposite the Realm.<br /> <br /> So they need to be able to fit into multiple kinds of games, with multiple STs wanting to run varied plots.<br /> <br /> <br /> This does, of course, also mean their purpose can't be &quot;Solar's no.2&quot;. That wouldn't work if there's no Solars in your game, not many Solars, or they just don't fit together well (I tried using Solar-Lunar mate pairs in 2nd ed, and honestly it didn't work well. Some players are into it, most aren't).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-28-2018, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T07:40:01-07:00","id":1249406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249400#post1249400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... while Supernal is a very potent effect, I suspect Lunars will still end up being closer to Solar power than they were in 2nd ed. Though I think they'll also be a bit less comparable, by virtue of being more different than in 2nd ed (where they had a large number of charms that were just nerfed Solar charms).<br /> <br /> <br /> What's the purpose of Solars? To defeat the Primordials.<br /> What's the purpose of Dragonblood? To defeat the Primordials.<br /> What's the purpose of Sidereals? To defeat the Primordials.*<br /> What's the purpose of Lunars? To defeat the Primordials.<br /> They all had the same purpose, only their methods differed.<br /> <br /> You'll notice this has already been done.<br /> <br /> After the Primordial War, the Exalted were given a new purpose of course; to rule humanity (partly as a reward, partly so the Gods didn't have to).<br /> But that was pretty unspecific, and they weren't <i>designed</i> to rule humanity. They just happened to be fairly skilled at it, because they were superhumans, and things like the super-power of being really good at organising an army can be translated to being really good at an organising a kingdom (though there are issues with that, but I'm not going to go into that now).<br /> <br /> *To be fair, Sidereals were given a specific purpose by their Creators after the end of the Primordial War. But the others were not.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, this is all an in-game explanation.<br /> Out-of-game? The purpose of Lunars is to let you play certain kinds of character that the other Exalts are not great at. Monstrous anti-heroes, were-creatures, trickster-spirits, shapeshifters, heroes with a totem animal, shamans, bestial berzerkers, semi-human freaks, etc. But that doesn't require a specific in-game purpose, and in fact a specific in-game purpose can be detrimental and sometimes odd.<br /> <br /> For example, in 2nd ed the Lunars' purpose was the Thousand Streams River Project. Which a lot of people thought was ridiculous (I didn't, but I could see that it distracted from the themes of the game), and it did dissuade you from having Lunar Beast-King PCs or NPCs, which was a pity.</div> </div> </div> </div>But can they just be Keepers and protectors of Creation from Fair Folks? Lunars always were the less popular splat and the absence of idea seems to be the reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T07:57:51-07:00","id":1249411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249406#post1249406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But can they just be Keepers and protectors of Creation from Fair Folks? Lunars always were the less popular splat and the absence of idea seems to be the reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mean absence of identity, not idea. I\u2019m new to exalted\u2014I started really in 3e, but lurked in 2e. And except for my least favorite splat(Sids), exalted don\u2019t...have roles or purposes. They have identities\u2014motifs, core ideas, concepts. And as the many fights over lunars has shown, lunars in 2e did not have one. Lunars in 3e seem to have a strong identity: they are animal based shapeshifters, skinwalkers, witches and shamans.<br /> Lunars might be less popular than solars but my general understanding is that _everyone but Dragonblooded_ are. I think Lunars are bit more out there than solar: their more different from your standard adventuring party, and so they don\u2019t attract as much. Oh and they have been mechanically screwed over twice as I understand it.<br /> Now the solar bond...uh, there\u2019s one charm that solars have that effects Lunars in a negative way(survival one, where it lowers their bond mates resolve I think? It\u2019s based on animals). Given the lack of dB charms that don\u2019t work on solars bc lol fuck you DBs, I doubt \u201chorribly one sided bond slavery\u201d will be a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T07:59:25-07:00","id":1249412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249400#post1249400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the purpose of Liminals? There isn't one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is - policing the boundaries between life and death, typically by hunting restless dead loose in Creation - but they're not bound to it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to the regularly scheduled Lunar thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T08:02:29-07:00","id":1249414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249400#post1249400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Alchemicals? In 2nd ed it was just to be prototype Exalted, don't know if that would still be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not about to go hunt down the quote but I'm about 90% certain that it's been stated that Alchemicals are no longer a prototype of anything. It wouldn't even really make sense for them to be since we've moved away from the idea that Autochthon contributed <i>anything</i> to the creation of any exalted but the Alchemicals. TUS made the Solars, Luna made the Lunars etc. <b>full stop</b>. No additional help required.<br /> <br /> With that being the case, the Alchemicals actually <i>do </i>have a specific purpose. Precisely what that is is a little fuzzy but they were created only after the escape into elsewhere and well after the war of the gods was over (assuming that that part of canon hasn't changed anyway). Could be they're meant to help humans survive inside Autochthonia. Could be their ultimate purpose is a kind of cybernetic life-support system for Autochthon himself. Exactly what Autochthon wanted when he started the process isn't specifically pinned down but there's plenty of purpose for them currently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T08:05:24-07:00","id":1249416,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I edited my post after you posted without realising, so you probably missed my edit where I addressed that.<br /> <br /> As I said, their purpose being to fight Fair Folk is not much use if your game doesn't feature Fair Folk.<br /> In none of the games I've played, did Fair Folk feature much. A bit, but not much.<br /> The only game where we had Fair Folk a fair bit was the one where a Raksha was the boyfriend of a Solar PC (then a Lunar PC, now another Solar PC), and another Raksha is a member of the party.<br /> So if the Lunar PCs' purpose was defending vs Raksha, it'd be pretty awkward.<br /> <br /> I'll also say that a lot of our group has played Lunars, and when people have not played Lunars, it's because a)their concept didn't feature shapeshifting, b)Solars are more powerful, or c)it was a DB game.<br /> If your character concept is &quot;general&quot; or &quot;swordsman&quot; or &quot;ninja&quot;... that's probably a Solar. It's not a Lunar. It doesn't involve a totem or shapeshifting. You could of course make it &quot;general who is also a werewolf&quot; or &quot;cat-swordsman&quot; or &quot;rat-ninja&quot;, but that's changing the basic concept.<br /> When people wanted to play a shapeshifter*, or a character with an animal theme, they played a Lunar.<br /> And you can't really change that; if people don't want to play a shapeshifter (even occasionally) then playing a Solar and not a Lunar is fine.<br /> <br /> *Except when one guy played a Slayer who could turn into a massive 30ft monster. But he only did that occasionally, shapeshifting wasn't really a thing.<br /> <br /> Now saying this, the one thing that did put people off Lunars, which 3rd ed can fix, was the power level. They were just a lot worse than Solars at everything that wasn't a)being really tough, or b)being really pretty, or c)shapeshifting.<br /> Now, it's not a big issue if they're a little worse, shapeshifting makes up for that. But if your concept was &quot;sorcerer&quot;, and their excellencies were way worse than Solars, and they paid more XP than Solars, and they had less starting spells than Solars... you're probably not going to play a Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T08:06:00-07:00","id":1249417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249411#post1249411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now the solar bond...uh, there\u2019s one charm that solars have that effects Lunars in a negative way(survival one, where it lowers their bond mates resolve I think? It\u2019s based on animals). Given the lack of dB charms that don\u2019t work on solars bc lol fuck you DBs, I doubt \u201chorribly one sided bond slavery\u201d will be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know there is no such charm in 3E. I played a survival supernal for a good while and don't remember anything like this. <br /> <br /> You're not thinking of Spirit-Tied Pet where it creates an unbreakable bond with a familiar are you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T08:22:45-07:00","id":1249420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249406#post1249406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But can they just be Keepers and protectors of Creation from Fair Folks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, not this again.<br /> <br /> \u200bCreation is vast. The area it covers is almost two hundred <i>million</i> square miles; that's comparable to Earth. If you set each of the Lunars (which are said to number somewhere between 300 and 400, I'm gonna use 375) on <i>just</i> the borders of Creation, spaced apart as evenly as possible, and magically compelled them to eternally patrol for Fair Folk to keep them out, each Lunar would have to protect something like <i>one hundred and fifty miles</i> of border. Land <i>and</i> sea. Full-time. Non-stop. And this does <i>nothing</i> about the Fair Folk that are already <i>in</i> Creation.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Also, I'd be remiss to ignore the fact that the Fair Folk are no longer supposed to represent some existential threat to Creation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T08:36:35-07:00","id":1249424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249420#post1249420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, not this again.<br /> <br /> \u200bCreation is vast. The area it covers is almost two hundred <i>million</i> square miles; that's comparable to Earth. If you set each of the Lunars (which are said to number somewhere between 300 and 400, I'm gonna use 375) on <i>just</i> the borders of Creation, spaced apart as evenly as possible, and magically compelled them to eternally patrol for Fair Folk to keep them out, each Lunar would have to protect something like <i>one hundred and fifty miles</i> of border. Land <i>and</i> sea. Full-time. Non-stop. And this does <i>nothing</i> about the Fair Folk that are already <i>in</i> Creation.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Also, I'd be remiss to ignore the fact that the Fair Folk are no longer supposed to represent some existential threat to Creation.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So? They are DEMIGODS or who they are? They potentially able to create new countries, nations and bioms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T08:37:22-07:00","id":1249425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249417#post1249417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know there is no such charm in 3E. I played a survival supernal for a good while and don't remember anything like this.<br /> <br /> You're not thinking of Spirit-Tied Pet where it creates an unbreakable bond with a familiar are you?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, the one in Miracles--I think the Apperance buffer? One sec...(I was AFB when posting)<br /> <br /> Elemental Sculpted Avatar! It gives one bonus die to sooth or comfort Lunar Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T09:18:03-07:00","id":1249436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249425#post1249425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, the one in Miracles--I think the Apperance buffer? One sec...(I was AFB when posting)<br /> <br /> Elemental Sculpted Avatar! It gives one bonus die to sooth or comfort Lunar Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that one! <br /> <br /> Huh, I'd forgotten about that effect. I will point out that it has nothing to do with the lunar bond specifically. I think it's supposed to be allowing you to better relate to the lunar's beastial nature (though this has potentially insulting undertones to it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T09:34:58-07:00","id":1249444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249424#post1249424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>So</i> the idea is absurdly impractical. Individual Lunars can absolutely decide to declare eternal enmity for Fair Folk and seek to eliminate their influence wherever they detect it, but we shouldn't be trying to force <i>the entire splat</i> into that niche.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249424#post1249424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are DEMIGODS or who they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Demigods still have to eat, shit, and sleep; more importantly, they still have the capacity to decide that when Luna gave them the power to break their chains, it represented a freedom to pursue their goals, as opposed to putting on a new set of chains that say &quot;Fuck Raksha.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249424#post1249424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They potentially able to create new countries, nations and bioms.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're certainly not getting Wyld-Shaping Technique in 3e, and even if they were, remaking a dissolved Creation is <i>very</i> different from protecting an existing one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T09:40:44-07:00","id":1249447,"title":"","content":"I think he means that they can forge new anti-Raksha polities with human armies to fight Raksha, and so on. And they can make new biomes using workings.<br /> <br /> But I agree with you about the main point: forcing all Lunars to be the &quot;anti-Raksha splat&quot; sounds like a bad idea.<br /> <br /> I'm okay with that being a thing Lunars are good at, and have some charms for. But most games don't feature the Raksha all that much. It's not much good to have Lunars be the anti-Raksha splat if your game is about fighting the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T09:48:55-07:00","id":1249452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249436#post1249436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh that one!<br /> <br /> Huh, I'd forgotten about that effect. I will point out that it has nothing to do with the lunar bond specifically. I think it's supposed to be allowing you to better relate to the lunar's beastial nature (though this has potentially insulting undertones to it).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, yes! I misremembered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T11:41:09-07:00","id":1249500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249447#post1249447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he means that they can forge new anti-Raksha polities with human armies to fight Raksha, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me, then, do you feel that the current state of affairs in Creation reflects the widespread presence of such polities on the edges of the map? Because I see a Creation where the Fair Folk have made quite the toehold in some locales, treating with merchant-princes from the Guild, preying on humans in the South, finding wary acceptance in Great Forks and Nexus, and occupying the bottom six feet of Halta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-28-2018, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T13:37:25-07:00","id":1249522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249500#post1249500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell me, then, do you feel that the current state of affairs in Creation reflects the widespread presence of such polities on the edges of the map? Because I see a Creation where the Fair Folk have made quite the toehold in some locales, treating with merchant-princes from the Guild, preying on humans in the South, finding wary acceptance in Great Forks and Nexus, and occupying the bottom six feet of Halta.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the writing for Exalted has generally tended to forget that Lunars even exist and then crowbarred them into existing setting elements rather than giving them anything that is principally-<i>theirs</i>, the way that the Blessed Isle is for the DBs or Heaven is for Sidereals or the Underworld for Abyssals. This plus the generally-assumed inevitability of the returned Solars completely overshadowing anything the Lunars have done or ever will do is why I would really like a sourcebook for the Shogunate or the very early Realm, because then there's space for Lunar games to focus on the gruesome, endless war against the Dragon-Blooded and mindfuck intrigues and spy-games with Sidereals without having to give a shit about what the Solars are doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T13:54:32-07:00","id":1249523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249500#post1249500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell me, then, do you feel that the current state of affairs in Creation reflects the widespread presence of such polities on the edges of the map? Because I see a Creation where the Fair Folk have made quite the toehold in some locales, treating with merchant-princes from the Guild, preying on humans in the South, finding wary acceptance in Great Forks and Nexus, and occupying the bottom six feet of Halta.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. But it could.<br /> <br /> I don't think that would be a good thing though.<br /> My point is you <i>could</i> rewrite Lunars as the anti-Raksha splat, you could put in a whole bunch of Lunar-run or Lunar-built societies who defend the world from Raksha, and I don't think it would strain versimillitude. I don't think Lashet is suggesting something utterly impossible, because I don't think that this would give the Lunars an utterly impossible task (as you yourself mentioned, 3rd ed Fae aren't really an infinite horde who could crush humanity if they stopped pissing around, they're essentially refugees who live between Creation and Pure Madness, both of which are somewhat hostile environments for them).<br /> <br /> But my argument to Lashet was that I don't think that would be <i>good</i> for the experience of playing Lunars, because it's too restrictive. None of the Lunar PCs in the games I play regularly fight Raksha (it happened once, at the end of a short-run Lunar game), but some hang out with (and have dated) Raksha.<br /> <br /> Just as I wouldn't want DBs to be the anti-Solar splat (they generally fight everyone who's not a DB... and sometimes DBs), or the Solars to be the anti-Abyssal splat, or the Exigents to be the anti-Ghost splat, or the Liminals to be the anti-Mountain Folk splat, or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T14:28:38-07:00","id":1249532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249406#post1249406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But can they just be Keepers and protectors of Creation from Fair Folks? Lunars always were the less popular splat and the absence of idea seems to be the reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly makes sense for there to be Lunars who, by their inclination, and probably even by some of their powers, relate to the Wyld in a distinct manner.<br /> <br /> The issue I see with it being their whole thing is that dealing with the Fair Folk is something that all of the Exalted can do, and have an interest in doing, and it kind of implies being very far away from the action.<br /> <br /> I find it specious to say that the Solars have no function outside of the War of the Gods. Less specifically than the Sidereals, sure, but between their Castes and the general inspiration of culture heroes, folk heroes and mythic kings, there's a readily grasped useful function to their societies that they can fulfil.<br /> <br /> I don't think that works as well for Lunars, and I think the thing to do is lean into that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T20:42:06-07:00","id":1249603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249522#post1249522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that the writing for Exalted has generally tended to forget that Lunars even exist and then crowbarred them into existing setting elements rather than giving them anything that is principally-<i>theirs</i>, the way that the Blessed Isle is for the DBs or Heaven is for Sidereals or the Underworld for Abyssals. This plus the generally-assumed inevitability of the returned Solars completely overshadowing anything the Lunars have done or ever will do is why I would really like a sourcebook for the Shogunate or the very early Realm, because then there's space for Lunar games to focus on the gruesome, endless war against the Dragon-Blooded and mindfuck intrigues and spy-games with Sidereals without having to give a shit about what the Solars are doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, it didn't ignore them, it assumed that the pre-playable Lunars state of affairs from prior iterations of development was in play, i.e. they were the Fair Folk or in league with them. Reading through the caste books' in-character comments re: Lunars, especially for the earlier ones, is kind of a weird experience along those lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T06:22:08-07:00","id":1249684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249385#post1249385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You speak about methods, not the purpose of Lunars. And they should have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be able to have some fun with the optional Exalt types that will be appearing in Exigents since two of them were envisioned as foils to the Lunar Exalted which will probably be better than pointing the Fair Folk and going &quot;You need us to protect you from them... except that time we failed spectacularly and the Empress saved you, yeah... sorry about that.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T06:35:01-07:00","id":1249688,"title":"","content":"Indeed, important to remember that Lunars weren't thought of as playable until after the setting had been made. So they purposely are glossed over most of early 1e or straight up insane monsters when they appear until their own book. Which...didn't help.<br /> <br /> Ex3 is a redesign to the point where folks should see them as a completely new splat and not think of most holdovers from prior editions. On Discord Minton said quite a few laws and cultural practices in the Realm will be talked about in the Realm and Heirs of the Shogunate because of how bonkers fighting Shapeshifting Demigods can get for over a millenia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T07:31:35-07:00","id":1249697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1249688#post1249688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Discord Minton said quite a few laws and cultural practices in the Realm will be talked about in the Realm and Heirs of the Shogunate because of how bonkers fighting Shapeshifting Demigods can get for over a millenia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good, honestly the biggest problems with Lunars and why they foster the worst tribalism in the community is that it feels like they live in an alternative reality to everyone else.<br /> <br /> If they were handling this like in previous editions Fangs at the Gate would have this embellished account of Dynasts checking under the bed for Lunars and having elabourate checks to see if their household staff had been replaced by a shapeshifter that the material on the Realm wouldn't support at all and once again the Lunars would look like massive bullshitters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T17:46:18-07:00","id":1249847,"title":"","content":"On the subject of what Lunars are for, I was thinking through some of the narrative roles of the mythic trickster, and it brought me back to a key point that might often be forgotten for how fresh it is; that what the Lunars are is explicitly supposed to be something that has changed across the ages.<br /> <br /> I came upon the idea of Lunars doing the trickster thing in terms of challenging and violating taboos as a way of provoking evaluation and criticism of them, as well as providing a vicarious thrill to those that witness and hear of their exploits. It's something that I think could emerge from Lunar actions in the Time of Tumult while not being an essential function of them, but couldn't shake the sense that it would be strongly fitting to them in the Old Realm; as in, I could see that as being the thesis of one of their old Castes.<br /> <br /> I often try to think of some things that give real weight to the idea that their old Castes are gone, and that this means there's something very different between the Lunars that a new Solar might meet and those that they'll see in visions of past lives, and putting Castes in the context of their relationship with the Old Realm and the Solars themselves seems like a good way to do it. Sacred guardian beasts, challenging tricksters, seekers of valuable knowledge and lore through predatory guile ala Anansi, things like that.<br /> <br /> It emphasises that what Lunars are is fluid. They got to be <i>for</i> something in the First Age, because that was a context that afforded that. If one wants to know what they're for in the Age of Sorrows, their Castes are a good place to start, because the thing they have in common are survival and exertion in a world that is hostile to them.<br /> <br /> Why should the Lunars be about protection against and marshalling of the Fair Folk? The world has given them no time or place for that, and so the world doesn't even deserve that effort. The world drove them out into the cold, and so they dropped having elaborate social functions for the sake of thriving out there and coming back with a vengeance.<br /> <br /> I think if the book plays its cards right, it can make that premise into one as compelling as any of the others, while still being highly distinct to these Exalted. I think Second Edition was kind of trying to acknowledge that the station of the Lunars had changed with the Thousand Streams River, but I ultimately view that approach as a half-measure; it all revolved around wanting to make it that Lunars had been this particular thing (Stewards), and despite all that they were put through that they were still trying to be the same thing. I think that could only ever end up lacking credibility because it couldn't escape the sense that trying to be Stewards under the shadow of Realm dominance and the Wyld Hunt only ever meant that they weren't doing very well at it anymore.<br /> <br /> Whereas the First Edition presentation... I'm going to combine things that I know from the books I have with a bit of second-hand hearsay and personal speculation on the Lunar book. Because for all that people rag on their being made playable at just the last minute, I think they also suffer from the fact that the First Edition core's presentation of the Exalted as a whole was still working some of the kinks out, and often portraying a rather simplified model. I'm basing this on the way that the core ascribed Solars and Lunars functions in the First Age based on the literal time of day; that when the sun went down, action and authority went to the Lunars while the Solars would be asleep. It was a very 'fantasy kingdom' take on the First Age, woven into a picture of the general Exalted that was still a bit crude and a little more generic. The gameline got to elaborate on the picture of Solars and First Age later on, making them more well-rounded and sophisticated, but I'd say that the focus on what the Lunars were in the Time of Tumult left little importance for thinking much on what they used to be.<br /> <br /> So you got something like &quot;the Lunars were kind of sort of seconds-in-command to the Solars, don't think about it too hard it doesn't matter anymore&quot;, with all significance of that swept away by their transition into barbaric overlords and ideological primitivists. To my eyes, the bones of the idea of Exalted that have been changed drastically by the turn of ages was still there, and I do think it's a very interesting starting point, but the overlaying details remained very broad and arch. Probably not helped by reports of a divided vision between the writing teams.<br /> <br /> So my point is, take the premise in the original version, and polish it up a bit. Give a bit more thought and detail into what they were before the Usurpation, without giving any more detail than necessary. Make the focus of their transition be that the loss of purpose and position is the point, rather than being a motive for tearing down everything else as well. But you still get to keep them wanting to tear <i>something</i> down, just a bit more coherently motivated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T04:25:38-07:00","id":1250429,"title":"","content":"It's pretty much unlikely, but what about 'function' of Lunars as Explorers and Pathfinders. I mean by design they were created as spies, assassins and infiltrators, so their abilities include shape-shifting adaptability and toughness. After Primordial War they could use this abilities to become travelers who discover new places and develop new nations and whole new ecosystems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T05:50:43-07:00","id":1250434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1250429#post1250429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty much unlikely, but what about 'function' of Lunars as Explorers and Pathfinders. I mean by design they were created as spies, assassins and infiltrators, so their abilities include shape-shifting adaptability and toughness. After Primordial War they could use this abilities to become travelers who discover new places and develop new nations and whole new ecosystems.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a lot like them being dedicated opponents of the Fair Folk; it's definitely a thing that Lunars could and would do, as an application of their capabilities and temperament, but making it the definition of what Lunars are would run into issues of being something not very distinct to them and unmoors them a bit from the heart of the setting.<br /> <br /> Still, it also sounds a bit to me like one of the things that one of their First Age Castes might have done. Best with other elements that would distinguish them from the Eclipse Caste; that is to say, the things that the Eclipse Caste has in addition to being travellers and explorers is different from what this Lunar Caste might do.<br /> <br /> I think it's always been the wrong approach to come at Lunars from the perspective of looking for ends that can be given to shapeshifting (often somewhat circuitous ones) and designate that as the Lunar Thing, rather than focusing on the side where being shapeshifters gives them the freedom to pursue lots of different things to be.<br /> <br /> Hmm, that's giving me a notion of how to picture multiple facets to First Age Castes; a balance between a dedicated function to the Realm (even if it's a somewhat iconoclast or outsider one, like the idea of the challenging trickster) against an application of their own yearnings for freedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T07:21:13-07:00","id":1250446,"title":"","content":"The Lunar Exalted seem to have always had the ability to choose their own Castes, even unto the point of destroying their current selection and creating others.<br /> <br /> More than any other Exalted Host, the Lunar Host is the most capable of adapting to the times.<br /> <br /> That's not insignificant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T08:14:32-07:00","id":1250453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1250446#post1250446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunar Exalted seem to have always had the ability to choose their own Castes, even unto the point of destroying their current selection and creating others.<br /> <br /> More than any other Exalted Host, the Lunar Host is the most capable of adapting to the times.<br /> <br /> That's not insignificant.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does tend to be habitually understated, though, especially in prior editions that over-emphasized the Wyld. The only time that GCG thought to underline it and talk about it directly in 1e was in reaction to how Lunars 1e was underwhelming, so it probably would have helped if he had, you know, tried to make sure that the point made it clearly into the book in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T11:27:31-07:00","id":1250492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1250453#post1250453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does tend to be habitually understated, though, especially in prior editions that over-emphasized the Wyld. The only time that GCG thought to underline it and talk about it directly in 1e was in reaction to how Lunars 1e was underwhelming, so it probably would have helped if he had, you know, tried to make sure that the point made it clearly into the book in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than understated, it just wasn\u2019t as dramatic in previous Editions.<br /> <br /> Third Edition is the first one to suggest that Lunars redesigned their Castes at least once before, and that in all cases they did so because they wanted to rather than because anything forced them to do so.<br /> <br /> Previous Editions also made it about recapturing what was lost rather than creating something new, and also highlighted their failure with the Changing Moon Caste substituting for three Castes and still losing an ability to the No Moons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T14:53:36-07:00","id":1250539,"title":"","content":"Thousand Blades Style might make it in as a stretch goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T15:24:40-07:00","id":1250550,"title":"","content":"Presumably, they'll do an equivalent to Heirs of the Shogunate, which... I can't remember what they said about how much Heirs will have in terms of charms. I don't remember MA, spells and evocations being mentioned, I think they said charms.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think that's plausible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T15:52:19-07:00","id":1250556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1250550#post1250550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably, they'll do an equivalent to Heirs of the Shogunate</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know... It seems to me that Charms are the least of what that document will entail, and that it's mostly setting and character information.<br /> <br /> And I think the Dragon Blooded are uniquely suited to such an expansion, because there's <i>so many</i> of them. I think we're primarily getting the thing because there are more Terrestrial Exalted than can fit in one book (especially when it needs all of that magic). As elaborate groups, bigger than the sum of their parts. Things that <i>need</i> that level of detail.<br /> <br /> I don't think the other Exalted necessitate that level of expansion.<br /> <br /> ... Maybe something more like Miracles.<br /> <br /> Is that splitting hairs? It feels like it's splitting hairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T18:16:08-07:00","id":1250585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1250556#post1250556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know... It seems to me that Charms are the least of what that document will entail, and that it's mostly setting and character information.<br /> <br /> And I think the Dragon Blooded are uniquely suited to such an expansion, because there's <i>so many</i> of them. I think we're primarily getting the thing because there are more Terrestrial Exalted than can fit in one book (especially when it needs all of that magic). As elaborate groups, bigger than the sum of their parts. Things that <i>need</i> that level of detail.<br /> <br /> I don't think the other Exalted necessitate that level of expansion.<br /> <br /> ... Maybe something more like Miracles.<br /> <br /> Is that splitting hairs? It feels like it's splitting hairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I agree. <i>Miracles of the Solar Exalted </i>had a chapter about Past Lives, and then launched immediately into More Solar Charms.<br /> <br /> We already know that <i>Heirs of the Shogunate</i> is going to contain much more setting information, because that's what we paid for in the kickstarter. Lookshy, the Forest Witches, that new, younger empire, and possibly the Grass Spiders. Even if the content is mostly mechanical, like the Gunzosha armor and those weird ghosts that Forest Witches can become, it's content that fleshes out details of the setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've also felt a lack of hope that the Lunar Exalted and their dominions would excite as much response from writers and kickstarter-backers.<br /> <br /> But I didn't say so, because I felt that would set the wrong attitude. The Dragon-Blooded are able to have outright weird shit like the Forest Witches, and new and exciting dominions like that younger empire (Prasad?), and in this edition the Lunar Exalted are finally being allowed to dominate and control and built within territories of the Threshold. We're not limited to tired old places like Mahankala, the Nameless Lair, or Sunken Luthe anymore. (Halta and Chiaroscuro never counted.)<br /> <br /> So I want to see what kinds of dominions and novelties the writers can imagine for the Lunar Exalted before I start suggesting that they can't inspire as much content in a supplement as the Dragon-Blooded can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T18:23:35-07:00","id":1250588,"title":"","content":"I have mixed feelings about the premise of Lunar Dominions coming across in a manner that would feel as though they're equivalent to the many different groups of Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> Like, the Terrestrials being so numerous and diverse that you can divide them up in their own book along the same lines that the core divides the different Exalted. I can't quite imagine an equivalent for Lunars.<br /> <br /> But i mean mixed feelings in a genuine way; I can see merits. I want to get my thoughts in order before I go into that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T19:19:27-07:00","id":1250606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1250588#post1250588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have mixed feelings about the premise of Lunar Dominions coming across in a manner that would feel as though they're equivalent to the many different groups of Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> Like, the Terrestrials being so numerous and diverse that you can divide them up in their own book along the same lines that the core divides the different Exalted. I can't quite imagine an equivalent for Lunars.<br /> <br /> But i mean mixed feelings in a genuine way; I can see merits. I want to get my thoughts in order before I go into that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded don't constitute societies all on their own, because even in the Realm there aren't enough of them for that. There's also their mortal family members, and the countless thousands of mortals over whom they rule.<br /> <br /> Even if the only Wanasan that outsiders see are the Exalted ones, those exorcists should be the tip of the family iceberg, with mortals constituting everything below the water's surface.<br /> <br /> Lunar dominions are rather short on Exalted to make their societies magical, but we know there are kingdoms out there without any particular Exalted presence who still have magical prodigies that capture the imagination. That culture of people who have a method for ten men to sire one child, and the place where only sorcerers may rule, for examples.<br /> <br /> It would be much easier for Lunar dominions to have such defining magical novelties because of the manses, artifacts, and workings that Lunars could use to empower their kingdoms and peoples. And of course, there's the Lunar ability to turn people into beastfolk.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in that kingdom of allied snake people and bird people, and they don't even have a Lunar founder or ruler! Imagine if they did!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T01:12:31-07:00","id":1250678,"title":"","content":"One thing I like about Ex3, and this isn't aimed at anyone in particular, is that the Exalted don't have any explicit &quot;purpose&quot; other than being their patron's contribution to the War of the Gods. It isn't hammered home what they were <i>for, </i>like the Incarnae got together and engineered exactly how they'd go together. They were born of their power in a miraculous fashion, not programmed. We even have some Dragon Bloods having to be won over to the side of the other Exalted instead of being portrayed as being some obligatory army. It was also recently spoiled that the Solar/Lunar Bond was born out of a great conflict between the Solars and the Lunars instead of some sort of petty demand by the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> Instead of being some pat little system specified to function just so, we instead have an organic culture that grew out of these people and the power invested in them by their patron's. So you would still see many Sidereal's coming into the Vizier type role, and Dragon Bloods filling out the ranks etc, but it isn't so forced and twee.<br /> <br /> I'm excited to see what all the Chosen of Luna can be, and not worry about them trying to fill some role other than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T01:45:40-07:00","id":1250681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1250606#post1250606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded don't constitute societies all on their own, because even in the Realm there aren't enough of them for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are other things in the post, but... Not enough of them? There are somewhat isolated tribal communities in South America that are smaller than some of the Great Houses are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T07:09:06-07:00","id":1250736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1250681#post1250681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are other things in the post, but...</div> </div> </div> </div>Things you agree with or things you disagree with but didn't feel like countering? I can't tell just from this one line.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not enough of them? There are somewhat isolated tribal communities in South America that are smaller than some of the Great Houses are. </div> </div> </div>Yet such a small tribal community which includes a Lunar Exalt could still be just as worthwhile to write about as the Wanaasan or Grass Spiders or Forest Witches, especially if that Lunar has empowered them with the sorts of manses, artifacts, sorcerous workings, and mutations that a Lunar can provide above and beyond the blessings of a Dragon-Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T08:19:37-07:00","id":1250753,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I missed a word there. It's only some general talking points. I just need to gather my thoughts a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T16:04:37-07:00","id":1250877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1211970#post1211970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think individual Lunars really have the scope of Great Houses to warrant a chapter just to them that isn't the chapter for quick characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, if it was JUST individuals, but we're talking about individuals so influential and powerful that they have followers who work closely with them and support their ideologies.<br /> <br /> So, Sha'a Oka wouldn't be presented just as an individual luminary, but as the head of &quot;the Lunars who are fighting to conquer the Caul&quot;.<br /> <br /> Leviathan might be the leader of the Western Lunars as a whole.<br /> <br /> Rakshi has multiple lieutenants and perhaps even a Circlemate in the First Edition chapter fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T05:09:44-07:00","id":1251025,"title":"","content":"I'm... not really in an effective mindset for responding to a point that I made four months ago.<br /> <br /> \u2026. <br /> <br /> Oh wait... actually, this isn't so hard.<br /> <br /> I think if Lunars were approached in the manner of such divisions, it would warrant a chapter for sure, but I don't think that the Lunars should be approached in the manner. It kind of plays on a thing that people have been complaining about with them for a while; a sense of being too monolithic, too clumped together, despite their numbers and how logically far apart they should be. That and my personal preferences as regards some elders, in which they're rather isolated figures; deeply respected, but often from a safe distance.<br /> <br /> I think Sha'a Oka should be a special case, and one that would be rolled into the book's chapter on the Caul in any case.<br /> <br /> Even if one was to say that such groupings only represent an overall minority of the Silver Pact in total, there would be a problem in the level of emphasis given in an entire chapter to the subject; the level of emphasis can override impressions compared to the substance of the text.<br /> <br /> So, Dragon Blooded. The only Exalted so numerous and diverse that they can form entirely self-contained, and often tight knit communities within their overall numbers. You can conceivably have Great Houses alone that have more Exalted than all non-Terrestrials combined, and they'll actually live close by to one another and have grown up together and have strong interpersonal ties. Many of the Dragon Blooded are unlike the others because being Exalted suffuses the whole of your life; you can be born with the expectation of it, it can shape formative years (especially if you Exalt as an actual child, the norm for even the outcastes and unlikely among other Exalted), and it can inform perspectives on children. There's a cultural idea to that which can form the manner of outcaste groups even when they're not related by blood. The likelihood that they can get together in groups larger than five also creates stronger grounds to form a distinct group identity and culture; I warrant that the Forest Witches are more like a society than basically any Celestial circle.<br /> <br /> Because of how communities intersect, that also means that in places where groups of Dragon Blooded are embedded, they can feel more interwoven with the fabric of a society. The ten thousand Exalted of the Scarlet Dynasty, the five thousand Exalted of the Seventh Legion, the two thousand of the Dragon Clans, these things are not apart from the Realm, Lookshy and Prasad. And there are a lot of touching off points, of numerous individuals and nebulous group identity, that can leave a deeper impact than the domineering and legendary individual.<br /> <br /> And there are so many Dragon Blooded, scattered all over, able to take innumerable forms and those forms often consisting of many individuals.<br /> <br /> So they start off with a strong advantage in being something divided up into groups that are worth elaborating on to the point that a book filled with the whole Charm set doesn't have space for all of them. The Lunars are playing catch up there.<br /> <br /> Now, I do think that it's possible that Lunar Dominions could be elaborate enough to be somewhat equivalent to a bloodline or community of Terrestrial Exalted. That they could be written as so inundated with Lunar magic and a distinct community identity that they're practically characters in their own right, and interesting enough to expand beyond their home book. That is a way to write them.<br /> <br /> But I... don't think that they should be? My reasons for that are twofold.<br /> <br /> One is that I think it gets into the old problem of positing the Lunars as having their own Realms in miniature, and the threat of crowding out the rest of the setting. I feel as though, even by the standards of Third Edition, the idea of many or most Lunars having elaborately magical domains is just something that overwhelms the setting. Particularly when it's phrased in terms of them taking a small tribal community and loading it with manses and Artifacts and blessings... for one thing, there's the question of what the Lunar is motivated by, and for another it seems to grate strongly against the thesis that the Lunar Exalted are lacking in resources and not best suited for playing the infrastructure game, because that's one in which the Dragon Blooded generally have the advantage.<br /> <br /> That blends into my other reason, which is the manner in which the core book presented Dominions as transitory and disposable. How the general model of them is to build them up and unleash them on the Realm, over and over, in order to sap the resources of the enemy. It's a process that I think makes a lot of sense with the premise of the setting, and it's one that I find compelling enough to want to stick around. I find it incompatible with an approach to them that would warrant expansion into a supplement.<br /> <br /> And thinking about the core again, I also find a new objection. I like the descriptions in the core largely being a matter of process and strategy, that the thing which generally defines a Lunar Dominion being the goals and operations in pursuit of them, rather than having a lot of flash. I find it interesting and challenging and quite appropriate to Lunars (especially considering the asymmetrical fighting approach).<br /> <br /> Lunars will have powers to imbue places with challenges that reward successful petitioners with power, sure. I feel as though the advantage to that of many Lunars will typically be setting something that can sustain itself in a suitable spot (one that is or may yet become hostile to the Realm), and then leave, rather than as part of a general network of power that one will probably need to sit on and maintain (even if it lacks upkeep, if it's too dense and accessible, it kind of becomes a target for the Realm). Communities adjacent to something that a Lunar laid down a few centuries ago do seem liable to be shaped by them, but I feel as though that generally shouldn't be much more elaborate than the kind of description that the core book gave to a lot of places, or What Fire Has Wrought gave to a number of less important satrapies. <br /> <br /> Overall, I think that Lunars will not need more than what their book will provide them, and that too much extra would be reaching a bit. Backer rewards of magic and quick characters for sure, but nothing really equivalent to the true meat of Heirs of the Shogunate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T01:35:26-07:00","id":1251310,"title":"","content":"My friend said he thought they'd reconsidered Lunars not being able to get favoured spell costs. I haven't seen anything about that though, anyone know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T02:35:40-07:00","id":1251319,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Vance mentioned it on the discord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T04:17:05-07:00","id":1251334,"title":"","content":"Yeah, not everyone immediately jumps on being a wizard. So having it tied to Intelligence didn't funnel everyone into favoring it like they thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T04:34:23-07:00","id":1251338,"title":"","content":"Ah, that's cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T05:44:07-07:00","id":1251358,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, the Martial Arts a No Moon stole from a Raksha in Fangs At the Gate is Laughing Monster Style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":717,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","user":"Monghani","date":". 09-04-2018, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T06:04:00-07:00","id":1251365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1251358#post1251358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, the Martial Arts a No Moon stole from a Raksha in Fangs At the Gate is Laughing Monster Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh fuck yes, the Shaping Stances were too awesome to be a niche Fair Folk only Martial Art equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T06:11:37-07:00","id":1251367,"title":"","content":"I wholeheartedly agree with you on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T06:25:45-07:00","id":1251371,"title":"","content":"With 400 Demigods reaching levels of power that can shake the heavens I'm pretty sure the Devs can come up with a few dozens societies and cultures members of their group can create or influence. Gone are the days where the setting had no mention of their impact. A supplement discussing more Lunar Dominions is completely possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T06:50:09-07:00","id":1251374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1251371#post1251371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A supplement discussing more Lunar Dominions is completely possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I quite agree. I said as such in close to those exact words.<br /> <br /> My argument is that it should be avoided, not that it isn't possible.<br /> <br /> I find invoking the history of Lunar presence in the setting to be a false equivalence, considering my basis of reasoning such as &quot;Dominions get built up and then rapidly disposed of&quot; (going to be a lot of scars in the setting from that) and the core book's portrayal of that Dominion in the form of three kinds of asymmetric warfare led by a Lunar's daughter.<br /> <br /> I think there's a lot of room for Lunars to do things without contradicting the idea that some of their capabilities would not be the best course in the environment where they'd either end up as large, immobile targets or attractive objects of seizure for their enemies.<br /> <br /> (Kind of wish that we could keep a bit of a line between the speculation thread and the spoiler thread. :s)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T07:17:29-07:00","id":1251380,"title":"","content":"Oh, my bad. Vance and Minton talk about the subject on discord from time to time so it dips out of needing speculation real quick. We'll be getting looks at Lunars with lots of viewpoints on how they operate and what they should do. The stretch goals for each splat are (so far) set to have an Heirs-like book with more content. Don't think there's much of a point to arguing against that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T09:56:41-07:00","id":1251425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1251358#post1251358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, the Martial Arts a No Moon stole from a Raksha in Fangs At the Gate is Laughing Monster Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, is this just a thing a Lunar did in the fluff, or is it the book\u2019s actual fourth printed Style? I thought it was supposed to be an animal Style.<br /> <br /> Ah. I suppose that Laughing Monster might be the teased \u201csort of new\u201d Style, rather than Seven Drunken Gods.<br /> <br /> So, Swaying Grass, Laughing Monster, Centipede, and a mystery animal Style.<br /> <br /> Does Laughing Monster use \u201cthe staff\u201d as a weapon? For the pun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T10:16:06-07:00","id":1251428,"title":"","content":"Falcon Style was the other animal style. That was revealed in the Animal MA thread last month or so.<br /> <br /> So we have Swaying Grass, Centipede, Laughing Monster, and Falcon Styles in Fangs At The Gate.<br /> <br /> The reason it's &quot;sort of new&quot; is because it, and 3 other styles, were Raksha Shaping Styles that were basically MAs for Shaping Combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":717,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","user":"Monghani","date":". 09-04-2018, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T11:17:54-07:00","id":1251440,"title":"","content":"Yes, I\u2019m familiar with the Shaping Stances and Shaping Combat.<br /> <br /> The Falcon \u201creveal\u201d was shady.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T11:31:47-07:00","id":1251445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1251428#post1251428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Falcon Style was the other animal style. That was revealed in the Animal MA thread last month or so.<br /> <br /> So we have Swaying Grass, Centipede, Laughing Monster, and Falcon Styles in Fangs At The Gate.<br /> <br /> The reason it's &quot;sort of new&quot; is because it, and 3 other styles, were Raksha Shaping Styles that were basically MAs for Shaping Combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> NVM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T11:54:31-07:00","id":1251450,"title":"","content":"It was corroborated by Vance that same day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T12:26:04-07:00","id":1251461,"title":"","content":"I hope that Falcon Style allows for unarmed punches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T12:32:55-07:00","id":1251464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1251367#post1251367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wholeheartedly agree with you on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2nd edition I played a Changing Moon with Graces who hunted the Fae on their own terms by turning their own narratives back on them. I appreciated that 3rd edition for the most part wasn't going to be down for charm share and that being &quot;the wyld exalted&quot; wasn't really the Lunar thing. So this is really encouraging if I want to play that character again.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T12:33:46-07:00","id":1251466,"title":"","content":"&quot;It's a high-flying lucha libre style that gets even better if you can grow wings.&quot; Is what was said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T13:42:19-07:00","id":1251482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1251466#post1251466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;It's a high-flying lucha libre style that gets even better if you can grow wings.&amp;quot; Is what was said.</div> </div> </div> </div>But does that include the memetic \u201cFALCONE PAWNCH!\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T18:29:19-07:00","id":1251530,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nKuZFrq60iM\" target=\"_blank\">What I'm envisioning</a> when I hear that description of Falcon Style...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T10:47:04-07:00","id":1251950,"title":"","content":"I think that Beast has a very good take on what I want Lunars to be. I hope there's a good bit of thematic overlap and inspiration. The necessary and unavoidable monster that stands outside ordinary civilization and embodies the alternatives is a powerful theme for me.<br /> <br /> I'm picking up a little bit of a vibe of a pagan viewpoint (northern, rather than Mediterranean) of life being a series of tests and challenges and plateaus. I'm interested to see how that plays out as a contrast to Immaculate orthodoxy and the bureaucratic hierarchy of heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T12:45:46-07:00","id":1251981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1251950#post1251950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I think that Beast has a very good take on what I want Lunars to be.</b> I hope there's a good bit of thematic overlap and inspiration. The necessary and unavoidable monster that stands outside ordinary civilization and embodies the alternatives is a powerful theme for me.<br /> <br /> I'm picking up a little bit of a vibe of a pagan viewpoint (northern, rather than Mediterranean) of life being a series of tests and challenges and plateaus. I'm interested to see how that plays out as a contrast to Immaculate orthodoxy and the bureaucratic hierarchy of heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhhhh... you mean that <i>the elevator pitch </i>for Beast has a good take on what you want Lunars to be, right? Because <i>what we actually got </i>reads, to me, like a tract on how cool it is to be an abusive social predator (contra Vampire: the Requiem, which emphasizes how awful it is to be an abusive social predator).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T03:16:43-07:00","id":1252159,"title":"","content":"After a long break from Exalted, coming back I see we have DBs and are about to get Lunars! Cool. Have to say these Lunar charms are the best Lunar Charms I've ever seen, 3e looks to have broken the curse!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T03:50:36-07:00","id":1252167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1252159#post1252159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">coming back I see we have DBs</div> </div> </div> </div>I could have sworn...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">are about to get Lunars!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're still a ways off yet, so best to keep everything level.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T04:07:53-07:00","id":1252170,"title":"","content":"I've pottered around a bit, but if I knew, I forgot it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> After nearly 18 months of running Exalted, I realised I needed a big break or I'd just hate it. That plus a bunch of shitty real life things meant I was being pretty argumentative and difficult online, so a break was even more in order! But I'm writing a new campaign now and I'll be glad to get more stuff from new books to put in it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T07:50:25-07:00","id":1252213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1251981#post1251981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uhhhh... you mean that <i>the elevator pitch </i>for Beast has a good take on what you want Lunars to be, right? Because <i>what we actually got </i>reads, to me, like a tract on how cool it is to be an abusive social predator (contra Vampire: the Requiem, which emphasizes how awful it is to be an abusive social predator).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't suppose I'm seeing the same things the same way, and that's fine. For what it's worth, I get where you're coming from - Demon persistently rubs me the wrong way, but people seem to dig it. <br /> <br /> It's not an exact parallel, for good or for bad - its two entirely different settings after all.. Anything in any book in either setting is building material for the stories we'd want to create with our friends and players - add some, use some, discard some. <br /> <br /> What I like are things like... emphasis on creating a group, claiming and making use of territory, cooperating with other splats, and forming a mythology equal and opposite (or counter-balancing, perhaps) to more straightforward heroic legends. It's been a while, but I seem to recall a favorable impression of manipulating both the Beast and its environments together as a sort of whole. <br /> <br /> Hope that clarifies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T08:12:32-07:00","id":1252218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1252213#post1252213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't suppose I'm seeing the same things the same way, and that's fine. For what it's worth, I get where you're coming from - Demon persistently rubs me the wrong way, but people seem to dig it.<br /> <br /> It's not an exact parallel, for good or for bad - its two entirely different settings after all.. Anything in any book in either setting is building material for the stories we'd want to create with our friends and players - add some, use some, discard some.<br /> <br /> What I like are things like... emphasis on creating a group, claiming and making use of territory, cooperating with other splats, and forming a mythology equal and opposite (or counter-balancing, perhaps) to more straightforward heroic legends. It's been a while, but I seem to recall a favorable impression of manipulating both the Beast and its environments together as a sort of whole.<br /> <br /> Hope that clarifies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, yeah, that makes more sense. Most of the passages from Beast that stood out to me were...not that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T08:15:31-07:00","id":1252220,"title":"","content":"The thing to do with Beast is to pull an Infernals 2e, ignore the crap and just have fun being a dragon who is also batman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T08:15:38-07:00","id":1252221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1252218#post1252218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, yeah, that makes more sense. Most of the passages from Beast that stood out to me were...not that.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>[Amicable Otherworldly Comparison Clarification Methodology]</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T16:23:22-07:00","id":1252622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1251981#post1251981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(contra Vampire: the Requiem, which emphasizes how awful it is to be an abusive social predator)</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it doesn\u2019t, at least not much. Maybe First Edition did but Second is SO much lighter on the angst than a lot of people seem to think it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T08:16:19-07:00","id":1254216,"title":"","content":"So, I'd like to talk a bit about Ox-Bodies.<br /> <br /> Both the Lunar barbarian in the Core, and Eska, have the following health levels:<br /> \u22120/\u22121x2/\u22122x4/\u22124x7/Incap.<br /> <br /> So that's 2 extra -2 levels, and 6 extra -4s.<br /> <br /> In 2nd ed, one option (the best one) for Lunar Ox-Bodies was 4x-2s. That was probably a bit too good.<br /> <br /> I suspect that (at Stamina 3-4) Lunars therefore get a -2 and 3x -4. <br /> Perhaps at Stamina 5 this becomes 4x -2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T09:08:29-07:00","id":1254232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1254216#post1254216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'd like to talk a bit about Ox-Bodies.<br /> <br /> Both the Lunar barbarian in the Core, and Eska, have the following health levels:<br /> \u22120/\u22121x2/\u22122x4/\u22124x7/Incap.<br /> <br /> So that's 2 extra -2 levels, and 6 extra -4s.<br /> <br /> In 2nd ed, one option (the best one) for Lunar Ox-Bodies was 4x-2s. That was probably a bit too good.<br /> <br /> I suspect that (at Stamina 3-4) Lunars therefore get a -2 and 3x -4.<br /> Perhaps at Stamina 5 this becomes 4x -2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re: Ox-Bodies<br /> <br /> Solars can purchase up to (Resistance) copies of the charm<br /> DB can purchase up to (Resistance) copies as well<br /> Presumably Lunars will be able to purchase (Stamina) copies since their attribute based<br /> <br /> At sta 1-2<br /> Solars get one -1 and one -2<br /> DB get two -2<br /> <br /> At Sta 3-4<br /> solars get one -1 and two -2<br /> DB get one -1 and one -2<br /> <br /> At Sta 5<br /> Solars get One -0, one -1, and one -2<br /> DB get One -1 and two -2<br /> <br /> So you suggest that lunars get:<br /> <br /> Sta 1-2?<br /> Sta 3-4: one -2 and three -4<br /> Sta 5: four -2<br /> <br /> The problem with this idea is that this indicates that lunars are always operating in the -2 or -4 penalty range when they've taken some damage. I strongly suspect that they'll get at least some access to -1 HL bonuses at some point. Your idea for Stamina 5, is objectively significantly worse than the solar version. <br /> <br /> First, I suspect that the Lunar Ox-Body will be based on Resistance in some way. I dunno if they'll go so far as to make resistance be what the HLs are based on, but if they don't include it somewhere, resistance basically becomes a useless ability for lunars. <br /> <br /> Second, the pattern of the other Ox-Bodies so far has been one where each level only upgrades one or two slots per level OR adds an additional slot. Upgrading three slots in one go seems like it would be a big jump.<br /> <br /> My take would be:<br /> Lunars Ox-Body Technique (up to [Stamina] copies)<br /> Resistance 1-2 - one -2, two -4<br /> Resistance 3-4: two -2, two -4<br /> Resistance 5: one -1, two -2, one -4","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T11:44:34-07:00","id":1254273,"title":"","content":"As I said, the example Lunar in Adversaries of the Righteous has two extra -2s, and 6 extra -4s.<br /> So I'm pretty sure she's got 2 ox-bodies each giving -2, -4, -4, -4.<br /> (She has Resistance 3, incidentally.)<br /> <br /> It's a good point about the level of changes though.<br /> So maybe something like:<br /> 1-2: -2, -4, -4<br /> 3-4: -2, -4, -4, -4<br /> 5: -2, -2, -4, -4<br /> <br /> As to Resistance... I can see where you're coming from, but:<br /> Solars are Ability-based. Except actually their excellencies are Attribute+Ability. There's a few Ability charms that give you bonuses based on your Stamina, Perception or Strength (I don't think there's any that give a bonus based on Dex. And I think for a very good reason!).<br /> <br /> Lunars are just Attribute-based. There's no Ability in there. So, sure, they might get a bonus based on Resistance, but I wouldn't be surprised if all Resistance does for Lunars is raise their dice pool on Resistance rolls, just like every other ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-14-2018, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T12:21:59-07:00","id":1254293,"title":"","content":"If Lunar ox-body does flip the stamina/resistance relation, they'll probably get an option for 0 resistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T12:37:00-07:00","id":1254300,"title":"","content":"No, Solars have attribute + ability <i>dice caps </i>but are, themselves ability based. Look to the Dragon Bloods. they're purely ability based and yet they also base things off of attributes in their charms <i>including</i> Ox-Body.<br /> <br /> I feel that Lunars should be no different.<br /> <br /> Edit: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1254293#post1254293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Lunar ox-body does flip the stamina/resistance relation, they'll probably get an option for 0 resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>True! I hadn't considered that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 09-14-2018, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T12:44:24-07:00","id":1254304,"title":"","content":"So maybe something like:<br /> <br /> Resistance 0 - one -2, two -4<br /> Resistance 1-2: two -2, two -4<br /> Resistance 3-4: two -2, three -4<br /> Resistance 5: one -1, two -2, two -4<br /> <br /> I'm gonna be seriously disappointed if lunars get no access to -1 HL even if they get bonkers numbers of -4. That penalty is not a joke in combat. -4 is a brutal disadvantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T13:15:32-07:00","id":1254320,"title":"","content":"That's probably why they have a whole tree dedicated to going berserk. Things become pretty bonkers if that -4 penalty turns into a +4 bonus and you have a fuckton of health levels sitting on it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T13:24:41-07:00","id":1254322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1254320#post1254320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably why they have a whole tree dedicated to going berserk. Things become pretty bonkers if that -4 penalty turns into a +4 bonus and you have a fuckton of health levels sitting on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope this isn't the case, tbh. Making the assumption that all lunars who use something as fundamental as Ox-Body are berserk ragers is not great charm design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T13:38:34-07:00","id":1254324,"title":"","content":"Relentless Lunar Fury is a fundamental archetype for Lunars in combat(not the 2e version, Ex3 reuses the name and it deals with regeneration and raging). Regeneration has explicitly been called out as something Lunars do better than Solars. So you might have to deal with disappointment in some regard.<br /> <br /> Mind you, could be completely wrong. We won't have the manuscript until next year. But from what we've been told so far this is the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T19:43:33-07:00","id":1255150,"title":"","content":"At Robert's urging, I'm trying to watch <i>The Five Venoms</i> on Netflix.<br /> <br /> Apologies, but I'm finding it boring. I don't think it aged well.<br /> <br /> Halfway through and neither the Lizard nor the Scorpion have fought anyone, and the scrappy kid has only intervened in one fight. The one fight that the real martial artists have had so far.<br /> <br /> It was almost like the kid used White Veil Style to tip the scales of the fight in the Toad's favor without anyone seeming to notice he'd rushed right into the middle of the duel. The Toad and Centipede dismissed him just as quickly as the police.<br /> <br /> He uses a staff, and I wonder if he could be interpreted to be using Laughing Monster Style. That was the Staff Grace-based shaping style of the raksha, and its purpose was to turn two other characters against each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T09:21:41-08:00","id":1275098,"title":"","content":"Okay, so based on the recent release, what are we supposing for the first four Chapters?<br /> <br /> Chapter 1: Lunars<br /> Chapter 2: Silver Pact<br /> Chapter 3: Luminaries<br /> Chapter 4: Schools","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T10:19:25-08:00","id":1275111,"title":"","content":"I think schools and famous Lunars will likely be together, as the Shahan-Ya and their school are rather intertwined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T10:28:35-08:00","id":1275113,"title":"","content":"It'll probably have the schools and basic descriptions of the Shahan-Ya running it in the front, and then actual QCs for a few of them at the back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T10:55:13-08:00","id":1275116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1275111#post1275111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think schools and famous Lunars will likely be together, as the Shahan-Ya and their school are rather intertwined.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1275113#post1275113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'll probably have the schools and basic descriptions of the Shahan-Ya running it in the front, and then actual QCs for a few of them at the back.</div> </div> </div> </div>But neither of you offer an alternative for Chapter 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T11:02:02-08:00","id":1275119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1275116#post1275116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But neither of you offer an alternative for Chapter 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Caul? It seemed to be rather important to the Lunars from what we've seen so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T11:02:05-08:00","id":1275120,"title":"","content":"Character creation, probably.<br /> Chapter 5: Traits<br /> Chapter 6: Charms<br /> Chapter 7: Martial Arts, Evocations, Spells<br /> Chapter 8: Animals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T11:20:05-08:00","id":1275124,"title":"","content":"Current table of contents, subject to changes during development:<br /> <br /> Chapter 1: The Lunar Exalted<br /> Chapter 2: The Silver Pact<br /> Chapter 3: Lunar Dominions<br /> Chapter 4: Character Creation<br /> Chapter 5: Traits<br /> Chapter 6: Charms<br /> Chapter 7: Martial Arts and Sorcery<br /> Chapter 8: Artifacts of Luna's Chosen<br /> Chapter 9: Heroes and Monsters<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T11:42:40-08:00","id":1275131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1275124#post1275124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Current table of contents, subject to changes during development:<br /> <br /> Chapter 1: The Lunar Exalted<br /> Chapter 2: The Silver Pact<br /> Chapter 3: Lunar Dominions<br /> Chapter 4: Character Creation<br /> Chapter 5: Traits<br /> Chapter 6: Charms<br /> Chapter 7: Martial Arts and Sorcery<br /> Chapter 8: Artifacts of Luna's Chosen<br /> Chapter 9: Heroes and Monsters</div> </div> </div> </div>One fewer chapters than Dragon-Blooded; I suppose because there was no reason to divide Chapter 2 or Chapter 3 in the way that What Fire Has Wrought needed to divide its pre-CC chapters.<br /> <br /> Makes sense. Especially since the Lunar Exalted already buck numerical conventions to do whatever fits them best, vis a visa having 3 castes instead of 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T12:19:51-08:00","id":1275138,"title":"","content":"Not to mention they have to have a bigger chapter 9 than others due to not only including notable Lunar NPCs, but Animals to shapeshift into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T13:32:17-08:00","id":1275153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1275138#post1275138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention they have to have a bigger chapter 9 than others due to not only including notable Lunar NPCs, but Animals to shapeshift into.</div> </div> </div> </div>And folks.. <i><b>Folks</b></i>... Imagine the addon book (a la Heirs and Miracles) and what we'll be able to <i>add</i> to it. All the animals, monsters, kaiju, charms, martial arts, Caul details, etc. THAT's where the money is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T13:40:12-08:00","id":1275156,"title":"","content":"As a general rule, chapter divisions are done to serve the needs of the book, rather than to conform to a pattern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T15:46:13-08:00","id":1275188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">kaiju</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I wonder if including kaiju in the book, or associated supplements, might be a bit of a wrong tack considering that Lunars can't acquire their Heart's Blood.<br /> <br /> Like, Lunars can turn gigantic, and maybe a bit weird, through their own powers, but it's been made fairly clear at this point that they only shapeshift into people and animals, and the largest thing that probably counts as a natural animal is still likely to be different in form and function than what most people would regard as kaiju.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T19:01:55-08:00","id":1275219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1275188#post1275188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if including kaiju in the book, or associated supplements, might be a bit of a wrong tack considering that Lunars can't acquire their Heart's Blood.<br /> <br /> Like, Lunars can turn gigantic, and maybe a bit weird, through their own powers, but it's been made fairly clear at this point that they only shapeshift into people and animals, and the largest thing that probably counts as a natural animal is still likely to be different in form and function than what most people would regard as kaiju.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR][/LEFT]</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with you, but I could see it going either way. I mean the chapter has &quot;Monsters&quot; in the title, so it must include something more than just bears and dogs and giraffes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T21:47:18-08:00","id":1275235,"title":"","content":"Thunder Lizards, Whales, and Giant Squid are acceptable forms of daikaiju in a 3rd Edition Lunars book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T23:27:55-08:00","id":1275242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211683-speculating-on-the-content-of-lunars-fangs-at-the-gate?p=1275219#post1275219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon